var scenariolist = [
["Tutorial Scenarios"],
["tutorial.xml", "Tutorial — Khalkhin Gol", "Tutorial — Khalkhin Gol<br>3 July 1939<br><br>Japanese forces have crossed the Khalkhin Gol and occupied positions around the Bain-Tsagan heights.<br><br><b>What you will learn</b><br>For the first three turns the game fights the battle for you and shows one mechanic at a time:<br>• objectives<br>• unit information<br>• transport<br>• reconnaissance<br>• artillery preparation<br>• support fire<br>• reinforcement<br>• resupply<br>• OverRun<br>At the start of turn 4, full command of the Soviet-Mongolian detachment passes to you.<br><br><b>Your task</b><br>• Capture the Khaylastyn Crossing.<br>• Capture the Hamar-Daba Command Post.<br>• Optional: take the Bain-Tsagan Observation Point.", [{"id": 1, "country": 5}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19, "support": [23]}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["Red Army Campaign (1936-1945)"],
["bn9s00.xml", "Battle of Sesena", "BATTLE OF SESENA - 29 OCT 1936<br><br>South of Madrid, Spain<br><br>Comrade, here is your order - Move west with your armored forces and occupy the towns of Esquivias and Illescas! Support this move with your air force. Your infantry occupied Sesena and defend the town against enemy attacks. Good luck!<br><br>ORDERS<br>After 8 turns control 3/2/1 VH for a BV/V/TV.", [{"id": 1, "country": 28}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19, "support": [26]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn9s01.xml", "Battle of Lake Khasan", "BATTLE OF LAKE KHASAN - 2 AUG 1938<br><br>Lake Khasan, Far East of Soviet Union<br><br>The sneaky Japanese attacked and beaten our border troops on the Bezymyannaya and Zaozyornaya hills. Attack the Japanese with superior power and recapture the territories we deserve!<br><br>ORDERS<br>After 9 turns control 7/6/5 VH for a BV/V/TV.<br><br>CORE (recommended)<br>2x Tank (+1)<br>2x Infantry (+2)<br>1x Reconnaissance<br>1x Artillery (+1)", [{"id": 1, "country": 5}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn9s02.xml", "Khalkhin Gol", "KHALKHIN GOL - 3 JUL 1939<br><br>Khalkhin Gol River, Mongolian People's Republic<br><br>The Japanese crossed the Khalkhin Gol river in the north, occupied the Baintsagan hills and tried to surround our troops with a two-pronged assault. Carry out a vigorous counterattack, thwart the enemy intentions and occupy the Japanese positions west and east of the river!<br><br>ORDERS<br>Capture all VH!<br><br>CORE (recommended)<br>2x Tank<br>3x Infantry (+1)<br>1x Reconnaissance<br>1x Artillery<br>1x Fighter Aircraft (+1)", [{"id": 1, "country": 5}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19, "support": [23]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn9s03.xml", "Battle of Grodno", "BATTLE OF GRODNO - 20 SEP 1939<br><br>Southeast of Grodno, East Poland<br><br>Move your units across the city of Grodno to the Lithuanian border. Occupy the city and vicinity and break any resistance!<br><br>ORDERS<br>a. Capture all VH!<br>b. Prevent that more than 2 enemy ground units cross the Polish-Lithuanian border (Exit Points).<br><br>CORE (recommended)<br>2x Tank<br>4x Infantry (+1)<br>2x Reconnaissance (+1)<br>2x Artillery (+1)<br>1x Fighter Aircraft<br>1x Tactical Bomber (+1)", [{"id": 1, "country": 20, "support": [60]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn9s04.xml", "Raate Road", "RAATE ROAD - 2 JAN 1940<br><br>Raate-Suomussalmi Road, Eastern Finland<br><br>Our comrades from the 163rd division in Suomussalmi are cut off and need help. Break through the enemy encirclement and restore the supply route!<br><br>ORDERS<br>a. Reach the Exit Point (Road to Suomussalmi) with at least 5 of your ground units.<br>b. Prevent that the enemy destroy more than 4 of your units.<br><br>NOTES<br>a. The Finns will try to surprise you. Be aware!<br>b. Attention - winter conditions! If possible, equip your troops with tracked movement. Check if you can switch between wheeled and tracked movement for free.<br><br>CORE (recommended)<br>2x Tank<br>4x Infantry<br>2x Reconnaissance<br>2x Artillery<br>2x Fighter Aircraft (+1)<br>1x Tactical Bomber", [{"id": 1, "country": 38}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn9s05.xml", "Vyborg Bay", "VYBORG BAY - 5 MAR 1940<br><br>Karelian Isthmus, Finland<br><br>The Finns asked for a ceasefire because their front is collapsing. But before peace comes, we have to capture the west bank of Vyborg Bay and the city itself! <br><br>ORDERS<br>After 10 turns control 10/8/6 VH for a BV/V/TV.<br><br>CORE (recommended)<br>2x Tank<br>4x Infantry<br>1x Anti-Tank (+1)<br>2x Reconnaissance<br>3x Artillery (+1)<br>2x Fighter Aircraft<br>1x Tactical Bomber", [{"id": 1, "country": 38}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn9s06.xml", "Battle of Bialystok-Minsk", "BATTLE OF BIALYSTOK-MINSK - 27 JUN 1941<br><br>West of Minsk, Belarus<br><br>The treacherous Germans have launched a general attack on our homeland. The western front has collapsed and most of our troops are threatened to be encircled west of Minsk. Escape before the pocket closes! Make your way through the mess to the east!<br><br>ORDERS<br>Reach the Exit Points in time with at least 10 of your ground units before the enemy capture all VH!<br><br>NOTES<br>a. You can't deploy your air force.<br>b. All friendly auxiliary troops are controlled by the AI - you only command your core units.<br>c. Save your core units! Reach the Exit Points as soon as possible - don't get into a fight you can't win. There should also be useful attachments to make your units faster!<br>d. Attention - summer conditions! Don't forget to switch back to wheeled movement.<br><br>CORE (recommended)<br>2x Tank<br>4x Infantry<br>1x Anti-Tank<br>2x Reconnaissance<br>3x Artillery<br>2x Fighter Aircraft<br>1x Tactical Bomber", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}, {"id": 2, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn9s07.xml", "Yelnya Offensive", "YELNYA OFFENSIVE - 2 SEP 1941<br><br>Yelnya, Southeast of Smolensk<br><br>You'll lead the attack against the semi-circular Yelnya salient which the Germans had extended 50 kilometres south-east of Smolensk, forming a staging area for an offensive towards Vyazma and eventually Moscow. Eliminate the threat and win the much-needed victory for us, Comrade!<br><br>ORDERS<br>a. Capture all VH!<br>b. Prevent that more than 9 enemy ground units reach the Exit Points.<br><br>CORE (recommended)<br>3x Tank (+1)<br>4x Infantry<br>1x Anti-Tank<br>2x Reconnaissance<br>1x Flak (+1)<br>3x Artillery<br>2x Fighter Aircraft<br>2x Tactical Bomber (+1)", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn9s08.xml", "Battle of Moscow", "BATTLE OF MOSCOW - 9 DEC 1941<br><br>Dmitrow, North of Moscow<br><br>The German offensives against our capital were halted and our strategic counter-offensive started. Your goal is to cross the Moscow-Leningrad railway line and to liberate the city of Klin.<br><br>ORDERS<br>Capture all VH!<br><br>NOTES<br>Attention - winter conditions! If possible, equip your troops with tracked movement. Check if you can switch between wheeled and tracked movement for free.<br><br>CORE (recommended)<br>3x Tank<br>4x Infantry<br>1x Anti-Tank<br>2x Reconnaissance<br>1x Flak<br>4x Artillery (+1)<br>2x Fighter Aircraft<br>2x Tactical Bomber", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn9s09.xml", "Second Battle of Kharkov", "SECOND BATTLE OF KHARKOV - 12 MAY 1942<br><br>Volchansk, Northeast of Kharkov<br><br>We'll start an offensive to liberate Kharkov. With a dual pincer movement from the Volchansk and Barvenkovo salients, we'll surround and free the city. The main attack takes place in the south, your job is to lead the northern attack.<br><br>ORDERS<br>Kill 64 enemy units and prevent that the enemy destroy more than 15 of your units.<br><br>NOTES<br>Attention summer conditions! Don't forget to switch back to wheeled movement, if wanted.<br><br>CORE (recommended) <br>4x Tank (+1)<br>5x Infantry (+1)<br>2x Anti-Tank (+1)<br>2x Reconnaissance<br>1x Flak<br>4x Artillery<br>2x Fighter Aircraft<br>2x Tactical Bomber", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [4, 37, 359]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn9s10.xml", "Battle of Voronezh", "BATTLE OF VORONEZH - 28 JUN 1942<br><br>Volovo, Northwest of Voronezh<br><br>The Germans launch an offensive towards Voronezh. Strong forces are trying to break through our defensive positions. Delay the advance of the fascists until we bring up reserves to defense the city!<br><br>ORDERS<br>After 10 turns control 8/7/5 VH for a BV/V/TV.<br><br>CORE (recommended)<br>4x Tank<br>5x Infantry<br>2x Anti-Tank<br>2x Reconnaissance<br>2x Flak (+1)<br>4x Artillery<br>3x Fighter Aircraft (+1)<br>2x Tactical Bomber", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [4, 41]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn9s11.xml", "Tatsinskaya Raid", "TATSINSKAYA RAID - 22 DEC 1942<br><br>Bol'shinka, 200km west of Stalingrad<br><br>You'll lead a raid deep into the German rear - the target is the enemy airfield at Tatsinskaya, the primary operating base for the German airlift efforts to Stalingrad. Inflict significant losses on enemy Air Force by destroying as many planes as possible and force the Germans to divert forces attempting to relieve their forces encircled in Stalingrad!<br><br>ORDERS<br>Reach the Exit Point with at least 8 of your ground units.<br><br>NOTES<br>a. You don't have to control all VH! You just have to ensure that you keep at least one VH occupied so that the enemy can't win.<br>b. Attention - winter conditions! If possible, equip your troops with tracked movement. Check if you can switch between wheeled and tracked movement for free.<br><br>CORE (recommended)<br>4x Tank<br>5x Infantry<br>2x Anti-Tank<br>3x Reconnaissance (+1)<br>2x Flak<br>4x Artillery<br>3x Fighter Aircraft<br>2x Tactical Bomber", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn9s12.xml", "Third Battle of Kharkov", "THIRD BATTLE OF KHARKOV - 7 MAR 1943<br><br>South of Kharkov, Ukraine<br><br>We expect a German attack on Kharkov again. Stop the attack and inflict maximum losses on the enemy!<br><br>ORDERS<br>After 10 turns control 6/4/3 VH for a BV/V/TV.<br><br>CORE (recommended)<br>4x Tank<br>5x Infantry<br>2x Anti-Tank<br>3x Reconnaissance<br>2x Flak<br>4x Artillery<br>3x Fighter Aircraft<br>3x Tactical Bomber (+1)", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn9s13.xml", "Battle of Kursk", "BATTLE OF KURSK - 11 JUL 1943<br><br>South of Kursk, Russia<br><br>Despite our prepared defensive positions the Germans continue their advance on Kursk. You will counterattack at Prokhorovka and throw back the Germans before they break through the last lines of defense towards Kursk.<br><br>ORDERS<br>Capture all VH!<br><br>NOTES<br>Attention summer conditions! Don't forget to switch back to wheeled movement, if wanted.<br><br>CORE (recommended)<br>4x Tank<br>5x Infantry<br>3x Anti-Tank (+1)<br>3x Reconnaissance<br>2x Flak<br>4x Artillery<br>4x Fighter Aircraft (+1)<br>4x Tactical Bomber (+1)", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn9s14.xml", "Zhitomir-Berdichev Offensive", "ZHITOMIR-BERDICHEV OFFENSIVE - 27 DEC 1943<br><br>East of Zhitomir, Ukraine<br><br>You task is to defeat the opposing German 4th Panzer Army of Army Group South and the liberation of the Zhytomyr Oblast region, including the cities of Zhitomir and Berdichev.<br><br>ORDERS<br>Capture all VH!<br><br>NOTES<br>Attention - winter conditions! If possible, equip your troops with tracked movement. Check if you can switch between wheeled and tracked movement for free.<br><br>CORE (recommended - Core build phase completed)<br>5x Tank (+1)<br>6x Infantry (+1)<br>3x Anti-Tank<br>3x Reconnaissance<br>2x Flak<br>5x Artillery (+1)<br>4x Fighter Aircraft <br>4x Tactical Bomber", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [17, 359]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19, "support": [47]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn9s15.xml", "Crimean Offensive", "CRIMEAN OFFENSIVE - 7 MAY 1944<br><br>East of Sevastopol, Crimea peninsula<br><br>You're honored to liberate our beloved Sevastopol. The Germans and Romanians have already started evacuation by sea. Don't let a single man escape across the sea!<br><br>ORDERS<br>a. Capture all VH!<br>b. Prevent that more than 4 enemy ground (naval) units reach the Exit Points.<br><br>NOTES<br>Attention summer conditions! Don't forget to switch back to wheeled movement, if wanted.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [4, 13]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn9s16.xml", "Jassy-Kishinev Offensive", "JASSY-KISHINEV OFFENSIVE - 20 AUG 1944<br><br>North of Jassy, Eastern Romania<br><br>In our major offensive on Romania you and your troops will be deployed on the right wing of the attack front. The goal is to encircle and destroy the enemy's 6th Army.<br><br>ORDERS<br>Capture all VH!", [{"id": 1, "country": 13, "support": [7]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn9s17.xml", "Belgrade Offensive", "BELGRADE OFFENSIVE - 12 OCT 1944<br><br>West of Belgrade, Serbia<br><br>The time has come to liberate the Serbian capital from the fascist bondage! With the support of the  Yugoslav Partisans and the Bulgarian Army, it should not be difficult to drive out the Germans and their collaborators.<br><br>ORDERS<br>Capture all VH!", [{"id": 1, "country": 67, "support": [7, 361]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}, {"id": 2, "country": 43}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn9s18.xml", "Lake Balaton Counterattack", "LAKE BALATON COUNTERATTACK - 16 MAR 1945<br><br>East of Lake Balaton, Hungary<br><br>The German offensive flagged - the enemy isn't be able to break through to the Danube. Time for us to attack. Advance to Lake Balaton and crush the enemy formations!<br><br>ORDERS<br>Capture all VH!<br><br>NOTES<br>Attention - winter conditions! If possible, equip your troops with tracked movement. Check if you can switch between wheeled and tracked movement for free.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [4, 359]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn9s19.xml", "Road to Vienna", "ROAD TO VIENNA - 3 APR 1945<br><br>East of Vienna, Austria<br><br>The Germans are on the run - withdrawing towards Vienna. Chase the enemy and destroy as many units as possible so that the enemy cannot establish an effective line of defense in front of Vienna!<br><br>ORDERS<br>a. Capture all VH!<br>b. Prevent that more than 44 enemy ground units reach the Exit Points.<br><br>NOTES<br>Attention summer conditions! Don't forget to switch back to wheeled movement, if wanted.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [4]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn9s20.xml", "Manchurian Offensive", "MANCHURIAN OFFENSIVE - 9 AUG 1945<br><br>Khabarovsk, Far Eastern Russia<br><br>At the Tehran and Yalta Conference, the Soviet Union has promised to enter the Pacific Theater within three months after the end of the war in Europe. So we are going to smash the Japanese puppet state of Manchukuo with a powerful operation. Your task is to overcome the border rivers near Khabarovsk and quickly advance westward into the interior!<br><br>ORDERS<br>Capture all VH!", [{"id": 1, "country": 5, "support": [24]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["Stay Alive - Red Partisans (1941-1945)"],
["bn5s01.xml", "RP Guerrilla Hunter", "Guerrilla hunter — 2 July 1941<br><br>HQ 8th NKVD Rifle Brigade, Estonia<br>CO General Kuznetsov<br><br>German troops are at the Estonian border, and armed Forest Brother groups are active behind our lines. Reports warn of an attempt to free prisoners held in our district, with the ERNA commando supporting the operation.<br><br>Protect the prison and find the armed groups before they can combine against it. The brigade is needed at the front; we cannot leave its rear open while the German advance approaches.", [{"id": 1, "country": 58}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn5s02.xml", "RP German Blitz", "Blitz — 10 July 1941<br><br>HQ 8th NKVD Rifle Brigade, Estonia<br>CO General Kuznetsov<br><br>The Germans are approaching Dorpat, but a train carrying important war supplies still has to pass through the town. If the defence gives way now, the train will be caught on the line.<br><br>Protect it and hold the town's approaches. <br><br>Local militia can reinforce the blocking positions while the brigade covers the railway. Keep the route open for the train even if the outer line must fall back.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [58]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn5s09.xml", "RP Sink the Tirpitz", "Sink the Tirpitz — 5 October 1941 (fictional mission)<br><br>Comrade, Tirpitz is anchored off the Estonian coast under harbour and air protection. We have no surface force here that can challenge her, and the Germans believe the anchorage is secure.<br><br>Three naval commando detachments have been assigned to you. Find a route into the anchorage and sink the battleship while the partisans delay the German troops ashore. Their command of the sea will count for little if our men can reach the ship.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [58]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19, "support": [361]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn5s03.xml", "RP Hit & Run", "Hit and run — 28 April 1942<br><br>HQ Soviet Partisans, Lithuania<br>CO General Karotamm<br><br>The Germans have left a supply depot in Lithuania lightly guarded. They do not expect a large partisan force here, but nearby troops can respond once the alarm is raised.<br><br>Strike the depot, then bring the raiding detachments out through the withdrawal point. Surprise gives us a little time to do the damage; do not spend that time defending the ruins against the relief force.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [60]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn5s08.xml", "RP Revenge", "Revenge — 8 October 1942<br><br>HQ Soviet Partisans<br>Latvia<br>CO General Karotamm<br><br>An SS anti-partisan formation has moved into our Latvian district to rest and refit. Its detachments have brought terror to the occupied villages. For once, they are within reach before they are ready for another operation.<br><br>Find and destroy the three designated enemy formations. Close the approaches while the assault groups attack, so they cannot slip away and return to the villages after we withdraw.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [59, 361]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn5s06.xml", "RP Gypsy Baron", "Operation Gypsy Baron — 15 June 1943<br><br>HQ Soviet Partisans, Belarus<br>CO General Karotamm<br><br>Our attacks on the railways have disrupted supplies for the German offensive around Kursk. The occupation command is now sending troops to drive the partisans out of the district and reopen the lines.<br><br>Hold the positions covering our bases and keep the railway unusable. Make the enemy fight for the routes his supply columns need, without allowing his clearing parties to surround the detachments.", [{"id": 1, "country": 359, "support": [7, 59]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn5s04.xml", "RP Rescue Mission", "Rescue mission — 12 September 1943 (fictional mission)<br><br>An aircraft carrying an American politician to Moscow has come down in occupied Estonia. A British submarine is waiting offshore, but the passenger must reach the rendezvous island before the Germans find him.<br><br>Distract their forces in the south while the rescue group moves north towards Kuressaare. Take its port or airfield, secure transport and bring the passenger to the island. Keep him out of the fighting; the purpose of this raid is to get him home.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [58]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19, "support": [9, 22, 361]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn5s07.xml", "RP Kill Bruno", "Kill Bruno — 28 January 1944<br><br>The Germans have brought a railway gun into our area. Luftwaffe aircraft cover it from two nearby fields, making a direct attack dangerous. A Smersh team is coming to help remove that protection.<br><br>Seize and disable the eastern airfield while the team attacks the western one, then destroy the gun. Block the railway and hold the surrounding positions against the response. Check that every landing strip has been put out of use before committing the main assault.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn5s05.xml", "RP Narva", "Narva — 24 July 1944<br><br>HQ 2nd Shock Army<br>CO General Fedyuninsky<br><br>The Second Shock Army is preparing to break the German defence at Narva. Beyond the town, the Tannenberg Line and the coastal bases offer the enemy another position from which to block our advance.<br><br>Take Narva, force a passage through the line and occupy the ports, airfields and towns beyond it. Keep the following formations moving through the breach before the defenders can withdraw into a new continuous front.<br><br>Original Title & Design: Retreat to the Tannenberg Line by Stephen deJong", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [17, 35, 40]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn5s10.xml", "RP August Storm", "August Storm — 12 August 1945<br><br>HQ Transbaikal Front, Manchuria<br>CO General Malinovsky<br><br>The advance through Manchuria is making progress, but the Japanese positions around Solon still bar the route ahead. Their defences must be broken before the following formations can pass through this sector.<br><br>Take Solon and the positions supporting it. Keep the roads open behind the leading troops so the Transbaikal Front can carry the offensive deeper into Manchuria.", [{"id": 1, "country": 5, "support": [24]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["Yugoslav Front (1941-1945)"],
["bn8s00.xml", "Uprising in Serbia", "Uprising in Serbia — 25 August 1941<br><br>Comrade, the uprising is spreading through western Serbia, but our detachments still lack rifles. Around Bela Crkva, the gendarmerie holds the village arms depots. Krupanj is beyond them, and we cannot attack its garrison with empty hands.<br><br>Take the depots, gather the volunteers and lead the advance on Krupanj. Each village freed gives the rising somewhere to recruit and organise. We must build a force that can hold this country when the occupation troops return.", [{"id": 1, "country": 67, "support": [7]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43, "support": [66]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s01.xml", "Battle of Sabac", "Battle of Sabac — 18 September 1941<br><br>The liberated territory around Uzice gives the uprising a base. To extend it towards the Sava, we must take Sabac, where a strong German garrison still holds the town and its approaches. The Chetniks have agreed to join the attack, though cooperation between our commands remains uncertain.<br><br>Bring the detachments against Sabac and secure the approaches once the garrison is driven out. German relief troops can come down the roads from the north. We need a town we can defend, with the surrounding positions in our hands.", [{"id": 1, "country": 67, "support": [7]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43, "support": [66]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s02.xml", "Betrayal", "Betrayal — 1 November 1941<br><br>The agreement with the Chetniks is breaking down. Reports from east of Uzice warn that their forces are preparing to attack our headquarters. With German troops still pressing the liberated territory, a battle between the resistance movements could leave both exposed.<br><br>March to Uzice and relieve the threatened positions. Protect the headquarters and restore contact between our detachments before the attackers can divide them. The command staffs must survive: without them, the defence of the whole district will come apart.", [{"id": 1, "country": 66}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn8s03.xml", "Retreat to Montenegro", "Retreat to Montenegro — 2 December 1941<br><br>Uzice has been abandoned. German columns and their local allies are driving through western Serbia, and the remaining detachments must get south before the roads are closed. Our next refuge lies in Italian-occupied Montenegro, across the Lim.<br><br>Open the crossing and lead the withdrawal through Dobrakovo. Keep a rearguard facing the pursuit while the scattered detachments join the column. Leave the old positions behind; the movement needs the people who can fight again.", [{"id": 1, "country": 67, "support": [7, 12]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s04.xml", "Rail Raid", "Rail raid — 8 February 1942<br><br>German armoured trains are moving along the railway from Mostar towards Sarajevo. These trains carry guns and men wherever the occupation forces need them; on an intact line they can escape an attack as quickly as they arrive.<br><br>Cut the track ahead of and behind the trains, then bring the detachments against their armed sections. Seal the route out before the crews can force a passage. The raid must leave the trains disabled, not merely delayed until our men withdraw into the hills.", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [7]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s05.xml", "Operation Trio", "Operation Trio — 10 May 1942<br><br>The enemy offensive has reached the liberated territory around Foca. German, Italian and Croatian forces are closing on the district, and the First Proletarian Brigade cannot remain here. Its headquarters must get out with the withdrawing troops.<br><br>Cover the brigade's route to the exits and keep the staff moving behind a fighting rearguard. More detachments are approaching; bring them into the withdrawal as they arrive. Do not let a fight for an abandoned position cut the headquarters off from the column.", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [12, 66]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s06.xml", "Counterattack on Kljuc", "Counterattack at Kljuc — 7 October 1942<br><br>The enemy has taken Kljuc and driven our detachments back along the upper Sana. German and Croatian troops have gained ground, but our brigades are gathering for a counterattack before the new garrisons can settle in.<br><br>Retake Kljuc and the surrounding positions. Send a force across the withdrawal routes while the main attack presses into the town. If the garrison gets away with its weapons, we shall have to fight it again at the next junction.", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [7, 66]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s07.xml", "Case White", "The Neretva crossing — 28 February 1943<br><br>The enemy is pressing us against the Neretva. German forces follow from the west, while Chetnik positions guard the far bank. The hospital columns and headquarters are on the road with us; they cannot outrun the pursuit or find another crossing on their own.<br><br>Force a passage, secure the far bank and bring the hospital and command columns through towards Montenegro. Keep the bridge approaches covered until the last slow-moving group is clear. We will not abandon the wounded to save time.", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [7, 12, 66]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s08.xml", "Case Black", "Breakout on the Sutjeska — 4 June 1943<br><br>Another ring has closed around the main Partisan force. Axis troops hold the approaches out of the mountains, and the way into eastern Bosnia runs across the Sutjeska. Food is short, the columns are crowded, and every day gives the enemy more time to tighten the cordon.<br><br>Find a crossing, break the line beyond it and lead the detachments out. Keep the passage open for the troops behind the assault group. A few men reaching safety will mean little if the main body is left inside the ring.", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [7, 8, 12]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s09.xml", "Operation Istria", "Operation Istria — 25 September 1943<br><br>Italy's capitulation has opened garrisons and arsenals across the coast. New Partisan detachments have formed around captured weapons, but German troops have reached the principal ports before them. The inexperienced local forces need help if they are to keep the territory they have gained.<br><br>Advance towards the coastal towns and relieve the detachments surrounding them. Captured Italian vehicles and guns can strengthen your columns. Take the ports and hold the approaches: the Germans are gathering armour for a counterstroke.", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [7]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43, "support": [62]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s10.xml", "Banja Luka Strike", "Banja Luka strike — 18 December 1943<br><br>German pressure in eastern Bosnia is drawing heavily on our forces. A strike at Banja Luka will threaten an important enemy base and oblige the occupation command to look west. Croatian troops hold much of the town's defence, with German armoured trains able to move along the railway.<br><br>Bring the corps into Banja Luka and seize the airfield and approaches. Surprise gives us a chance to break into the position before the garrison is reinforced. Keep the railway under watch as the attack enters the town.", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [7]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s11.xml", "Knight's Move", "Knight's Move — 25 May 1944<br><br>German airborne troops are descending on Drvar. Their target is Tito's headquarters and the Allied military missions, while ground columns converge on the town to complete the raid. The attack is already under way.<br><br>Protect the command posts and bring the surrounding Partisan formations into the battle. Hold the approaches against the relief columns while the troops in Drvar contain the paratroopers. Above all, keep the headquarters personnel alive and out of enemy hands; the resistance must still have a command when this attack is over.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [41]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43, "support": [9, 19, 22]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s12.xml", "Operation Ratweek", "Operation Ratweek — 3 September 1944<br><br>The roads and railways through Yugoslavia carry the occupation army's supplies and offer its troops a route north. Our offensive against those communications is now being coordinated with Allied aircraft. Around Zagreb, the remaining enemy airfields threaten the bombers assigned to strike the factories and trains.<br><br>Raid the airfields and make them unusable before the bombing force arrives. The bombers must destroy the designated targets and return safely; keeping enemy fighters on the ground is your part of that task. British equipment and a fighter squadron are now available to support the corps in the open country.", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [7, 361]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43, "support": [9]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s13.xml", "Belgrade Offensive", "Belgrade offensive — 12 October 1944<br><br>The Red Army is approaching Belgrade, and our own formations are converging on the capital. German troops need the city's roads and crossings to move forces through the Balkans; they will fight to keep that passage open.<br><br>Advance into Belgrade alongside the Soviet columns and take the city sectors and river approaches. Our fighter-bomber squadron can support the ground attack. Keep contact with the neighbouring forces as the fighting enters the streets, so the garrison cannot slip between them or isolate a leading detachment.", [{"id": 1, "country": 67, "support": [7, 361]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43, "support": [19]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s14.xml", "Knin", "Knin — 26 November 1944<br><br>The German garrison at Knin holds a junction on the withdrawal routes out of Dalmatia. Its positions cover the approaches to the town and the road north towards Padene. Leaving it intact would give the retreating enemy both a refuge and a shield.<br><br>Break into Knin and take the surrounding junctions. Press the southern defences while working towards the road behind the garrison. The enemy must lose the route as well as the town.", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [7, 66]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s15.xml", "Liberation of Mostar", "Liberation of Mostar — 6 February 1945<br><br>The Germans are withdrawing inland, but Mostar still protects the approaches to the route through Sarajevo and the Bosna valley. Their columns are moving before we can close the roads.<br><br>Advance on Mostar, send one group towards Visoko and another along the coast towards Dubrovnik. Cut across the withdrawal rather than following it from town to town. British naval forces will support operations against the island bases, and Soviet equipment is available to strengthen the corps for the pursuit.", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [7, 34, 66]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43, "support": [22]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s16.xml", "Battle of Sarajevo", "Battle of Sarajevo — 1 April 1945<br><br>German and Croatian forces are holding Sarajevo while their columns withdraw to the north. The roads through Podlugovi offer them a way out, and our surrounding formations need your motorised troops to close that gap.<br><br>Drive behind the defenders, cut the road at Podlugovi and join the attack on Sarajevo. Hold the exits against a concentrated breakout. Taking the city after the garrison has escaped would leave the next line just as heavily defended.", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [7, 34, 67]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s17.xml", "Advance on Trieste", "Advance on Trieste — 14 April 1945<br><br>Our advance has reached the routes towards Rijeka and Trieste. German forces still hold the coastal towns and mountain approaches, while Allied armies are coming through Italy from the west.<br><br>Lead the corps up the coast, clear the positions barring the road and take Trieste. Establish contact with the approaching Allies. The remaining garrisons must not be allowed to divide our columns between the mountain passes and the sea.", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [7, 34, 359]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43, "support": [6, 22]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s18.xml", "Battle of Poljana", "Battle of Poljana — 14 May 1945<br><br>The war in Europe has ended, but armed German and collaborationist columns are still moving west through Slovenia. They intend to cross into British-held Austria and are demanding passage through our positions near Poljana.<br><br>Block the roads to the border and hold the surrounding junctions. Accept surrender from troops who lay down their arms; stop those who try to force a passage. Keep the line closed while the approaching columns are disarmed.", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [4, 7, 34]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43, "support": [22, 361]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["Red Destiny (1946-1954)"],
["rd01.xml", "RD Bialystok Insurrection", "Bia\u0142ystok<br><br>21 March 1946<br><br>Comrade General, you know how this war began. Two weeks ago, while their newspapers were still talking about peace, the British and their partners struck our forces in Germany without warning. Their plan has a name - their own staff called it Unthinkable - and in its first line are German divisions they kept under arms after the surrender and have now given back their guns.<br><br>The front in Germany has held and is already pushing them back. But the enemy prepared a second blow behind it. Armed bands of the old Home Army, supplied by air from the West, have come out of the forests around Bia\u0142ystok and driven our garrison out of the town and the roads around it. Every train to the front passes through here.<br><br>Take the area back quickly. Paratroopers will land to help you. The insurgent units are your target; the townspeople are not, and I want them to see the difference.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["rd02.xml", "RD Road To Berlin", "The Road to Berlin<br><br>16 February 1947<br><br>Comrade General, the enemy's offensive is spent. Last spring they reached the Oder; this winter they are falling back, and the Stavka has ordered the counteroffensive that will take Berlin back from them. They seized the city in the first days of the war and have ringed it with defences since.<br><br>The approach through the Seelow Heights is held only by their lighter units. That is your chance. Break through, drive to the eastern edge of Berlin, and give your army its first taste of deep mobile operations.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 86}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["rd03.xml", "RD Siege Of Berlin", "The Siege of Berlin<br><br>28 March 1947<br><br>Comrade General, Berlin is in front of you, and you have been chosen to lead the assault.<br><br>The German divisions of the coalition are well dug in, and a British corps has been sent into the city to stiffen them. Our 5th Division will attack alongside you. Take Berlin, and the coalition loses the one prize it gained in this war.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 86, "support": [22]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd04a.xml", "RD Border Clash At Ulan-Ude", "Border Clash at Ulan-Ude<br><br>19 November 1947<br><br>Comrade General, you are needed in the East. Chiang Kai-shek has joined the war on the side of the coalition, and his armies have crossed our border and pushed deep into the Buryat Republic. They are now outside Ulan-Ude.<br><br>Throw them back across the frontier and retake every town they hold.<br><br>Do not underestimate them. They are weakened by twenty years of war at home, but they carry the same American equipment as the armies in Europe, and they may counterattack.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 15}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["rd05a.xml", "RD Liberation In Almaty", "The Liberation of Alma-Ata<br><br>7 May 1948<br><br>The fighting on the Kazakh front has gone on for five months. Last week the Chinese Nationalists took Alma-Ata from our garrison.<br><br>Your corps is north of the city. Liberate it and drive the enemy out of the area, and the faster you do it, the better.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 15}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["rd04b.xml", "RD Beachhead At Taranto", "Beachhead at Taranto<br><br>4 August 1947<br><br>Comrade General, the coalition is using the ports of southern Italy as its base on our southern flank: its bombers fly from there, and its convoys unload there. The Italian government allowed it. The landing will be at Taranto.<br><br>Your forces will land against strong British resistance. Their ships are the greatest danger to the invasion fleet, so a flotilla of our submarines has been placed under your command to deal with them.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd05b.xml", "RD Advance On Salerno", "Advance on Salerno<br><br>25 April 1948<br><br>The fighting in Italy goes on, but the Italian government is close to leaving the war. It has no wish to see its country become a battlefield for the British.<br><br>End it. Destroy the last large British, French and German force in southern Italy, at Salerno. More of our submarines are on their way in case their surface ships return.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [6, 86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd04c.xml", "RD Evacuation In Thermopylae", "Thermopylae<br><br>13 October 1947<br><br>Comrade General, you are going to Greece. In the spring a British expeditionary corps, Greek royalist troops and a Turkish corps moved north against Bulgaria. They have been stopped, and now they are falling back on Thermopylae to hold the pass while their ships take them off.<br><br>They think they can do here what the Spartans once did against the Persians. Destroy them and take the pass. Watch the coast: our intelligence expects their navy to shell the coast road.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [11, 39, 86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd05c.xml", "RD Landing At Maleme", "Landing at Maleme<br><br>30 January 1948<br><br>Comrade General, Crete is the last coalition stronghold in the Aegean. From its airfields their bombers reach our shipping all the way to the Dardanelles. Your forces will land near Maleme; paratroopers have already come down west of your landing zone.<br><br>The Royal Navy has a strong squadron here. Our submarines have been placed under your command to deal with it.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [6, 86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd06.xml", "RD Drive on Antwerp", "Drive on Antwerp<br><br>7 September 1948<br><br>Comrade General, our offensive has reached the Low Countries. Holland fell quickly, but the enemy has built strong defences around Antwerp: it is the port through which Britain supplies its armies on the continent.<br><br>Your veteran army has been given the task of taking it. Take the city and its port, and the coalition's supply line across the sea is cut.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [6, 86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd07.xml", "RD Frostbite in the Ardennes", "Frostbite in the Ardennes<br><br>11 February 1949<br><br>The enemy has laid a trap in the Ardennes, and our troops are stuck in the forest. The general who led them in did not bring them out.<br><br>Your task is to do what he could not: break out of the forest into the open country of France, and drive the enemy back with everything you have.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 6, "support": [22, 86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd08.xml", "RD Push To Dunkirk", "Push to Dunkirk<br><br>7 June 1949<br><br>The coalition armies in France are finished, and they know it. What is left of the French army, with British and German units, is trying to get away by sea at Dunkirk.<br><br>Do not let them. Every division that escapes will be waiting for us across the Channel. Complete the operation as fast as you can.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 6, "support": [22, 86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd09a.xml", "RD Storming Dover '51", "Storming Dover<br><br>13 December 1951<br><br>Comrade General, the time has come. Two years have passed since the coalition's armies fled the continent, and in all that time London has refused every offer of peace. The war that Britain started will end in Britain.<br><br>Your army has been chosen to land on the English coast and take the beaches at Dover. The British outnumber us almost two to one, but most of their troops are new recruits; the French and German units with them are more experienced but far fewer.<br><br>Our submarines will deal with the British ships in the area. Task Force Bear is landing west of you to take one of the coastal airfields.<br><br>A veteran British force is said to be on its way to the coast. Secure Dover before it arrives.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [33, 86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd10a.xml", "RD The Sack Of London '52", "London<br><br>12 March 1952<br><br>Comrade General, this is the last battle. London is in front of you.<br><br>It will not be easy. The coalition has pulled what is left of its armies into the city, and our intelligence reports veteran German and French units among the British defenders.<br><br>Take London, and the war the coalition began in 1946 is over.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [33, 86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd09b.xml", "RD Passage To Madrid", "Passage to Madrid<br><br>14 February 1950<br><br>Comrade General, France is clear of the coalition. But the French armies of the south escaped over the Pyrenees, and Franco has taken them in: Spain has joined the war against us.<br><br>You have been chosen to lead the attack on Madrid. This road is the fastest way to the capital, and intelligence expects heavy resistance and attacks from several directions along it. End Franco's war.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [33, 86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd10b.xml", "RD Fortress at Gibraltar", "Fortress Gibraltar<br><br>25 October 1950<br><br>At Gibraltar the coalition is making its last stand on the continent. Drive them out.<br><br>They have sent their best troops to hold the fortress and are deeply dug in, and the Royal Navy patrols the strait. We have intercepted a radio message: they may try to bring reinforcements across from North Africa.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [33, 86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd11.xml", "RD Kharkov Rebellion", "The Kharkov Rising<br><br>28 June 1951<br><br>Comrade General, I have grave news. For three years Western intelligence has been dropping weapons, money and instructors to the nationalist bands in the Ukraine. Now they have made their move: armed formations, joined by deserters, have seized the country around Kharkov.<br><br>Defeat them. They are far less experienced than your men, but they have the same weapons as you, stolen from our depots, so be prepared for anything. The people of Kharkov are not the enemy; the armed formations are.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 64}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["rd12.xml", "RD Storming Dover '53", "Storming Dover<br><br>13 December 1953<br><br>Comrade General, the time has come. More than three years have passed since the coalition's armies fled the continent, and in all that time London has refused every offer of peace. The war that Britain started will end in Britain.<br><br>Your army has been chosen to land on the English coast and take the beaches at Dover. The British outnumber us almost two to one, but most of their troops are new recruits; the French and German units with them are more experienced but far fewer.<br><br>Our submarines will deal with the British ships in the area. Task Force Bear is landing west of you to take one of the coastal airfields.<br><br>A veteran British force is said to be on its way to the coast. Secure Dover before it arrives.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [33, 86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd13.xml", "RD The Sack Of London '54", "London<br><br>12 March 1954<br><br>Comrade General, this is the last battle. London is in front of you.<br><br>It will not be easy. The coalition has pulled what is left of its armies into the city, and our intelligence reports veteran German and French units among the British defenders.<br><br>Take London, and the war the coalition began in 1946 is over.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [33, 86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["North Korea (1950-1953)"],
["ncampseo.xml", "Seoul", "SEOUL (25 June 1950)<br><br>Comrade General, the order to cross the 38th Parallel has been given. Soviet-supplied tanks and artillery will support the advance, and most South Korean formations are close to the frontier.<br><br>Your direction is Seoul. Break the border positions and take the capital before the defenders can draw back into a connected line. Our equipment gives us an advantage, but replacement tanks and guns are scarce. Bring them through the first battle ready for the march beyond it.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 18}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["ncamposa.xml", "Suwon", "SUWON (30 June 1950)<br><br>Seoul is behind us, but South Korean troops have gathered on the southern bank of the Han and destroyed the bridges. The river gives them time to recover while we look for a passage.<br><br>Cross the Han and advance on Suwon. The United Nations has called for our withdrawal, and American intervention may follow. Open the roads south before outside forces can strengthen the defence.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 18, "support": [3, 9]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["ncamptae.xml", "Taejon", "TAEJON (16 July 1950)<br><br>American troops have entered the fighting. We met them at Osan, and reconnaissance now reports a larger force on the approaches to Taejon. Aircraft are attacking our columns and ports behind the front.<br><br>Take Taejon. Our Third Division will engage the Kum River positions from the front while your force turns their flank. Cut the roads behind the defenders before they can withdraw towards Pusan.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["ncamppu1.xml", "Pusan Perimeter 1", "PUSAN PERIMETER 1 (5 August 1950)<br><br>The enemy is holding the south-eastern corner of Korea around Pusan. Its port is receiving troops and equipment, while our own divisions have marched and fought for more than a month.<br><br>Break the perimeter before those reinforcements can restore the enemy's strength. You have command of the forces assigned to the offensive. Keep pressure across the front so the defenders cannot move every reserve against the first breach.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [18]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["ncamppu2.xml", "Pusan Perimeter 2", "Pusan perimeter: the second attack — 30 August 1950<br><br>The United Nations and South Korean armies still hold the Pusan perimeter. Every week the port brings them more men and equipment. Replacements and tanks have reached us too, but the divisions are tired and we cannot count on another long pause.<br><br>Break the positions towards Taegu, Pohang-dong and the Naktong approaches. Take the hills and junctions around Yongsan and Masan, keeping the bases behind our attack secure. The ring must be opened before the enemy can take the initiative.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [18, 22]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["ncampwon.xml", "Wonsan", "WONSAN (10 October 1950)<br><br>The retreat has carried our scattered formations back across the 38th Parallel. South Korean troops are closing on Wonsan, and many of our men are still on the roads behind the front.<br><br>Hold the port and keep the northern route open towards Hungnam. A newly formed marine regiment and the guns in the city will support you. Buy time for the withdrawal without allowing the defenders to be cut off inside Wonsan.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 18, "support": [9]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["ncampcho.xml", "Chongju", "CHONGJU (27 October 1950)<br><br>Chinese forces are entering the war, and our battered formations are reorganising near the Yalu. The advancing United Nations troops still threaten the approaches to the river; they must be held while the counteroffensive takes shape.<br><br>Defend Chongju and its surrounding positions. If the enemy leaves an opening, push him back far enough to give the Chinese columns room to assemble. Keep the route to the Yalu in our hands.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25, "support": [21]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [3, 22]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["ncamphon.xml", "Hongch'on", "HONGCH'ON (26 December 1950)<br><br>The Chinese offensive has driven the enemy south again, but our troops are tiring and the United Nations armies are recovering. Chinese formations cover the western front; our forces are to operate through the central mountains and along the east coast.<br><br>Advance from the Kansong sector between the coast and the Hwach'on Reservoir towards Hongch'on. Find routes through the hills that turn the defended roads. We have too few guns to carry the whole offensive by frontal assault.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [6, 18]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["ncampwdr.xml", "Wonju Deep Raid", "WONJU DEEP RAID (7 January 1951)<br><br>The advance has reached Wonju, a communications centre the enemy is expected to defend strongly. Our V Corps will keep its northern and western approaches under pressure.<br><br>Take your corps south through the hills east of the town and break into the enemy's rear. Open the roads beyond Wonju while the garrison is occupied by V Corps. The opposing armies are gaining strength; the chance to pass around them may not last.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [6, 17, 18]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["ncamphoe.xml", "Hoengsong", "HOENGSONG (11 February 1951)<br><br>Chinese forces have broken into the South Korean positions near Hoengsong. Their attack from the north and west gives our corps an opening on the eastern side of the town.<br><br>Advance from the east and take Hoengsong before the enemy can reinforce it. Link the attacks around the road junctions so the defenders cannot shift troops from one threatened sector to another.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25, "support": [21]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [17, 18]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["ncampmun.xml", "Munsan-ni", "MUNSAN-NI (22 March 1951)<br><br>Most of our forces have withdrawn from the ground between the Han and Imjin, but a Chinese rearguard and several of your units remain south of the crossings. Enemy airborne troops are reported on the roads behind them.<br><br>Open the way through Munsan-ni and bring the remaining formations out towards Kaesong. Cover the withdrawal from both directions: troops advancing from Seoul may reach the rearguard while it is still fighting to clear the road ahead.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25, "support": [19, 21]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [18, 22]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["ncampspr.xml", "Spring Offensive First Phase", "SPRING OFFENSIVE FIRST PHASE (22 April 1951)<br><br>The Chinese command is assembling a new offensive. Its main force will strike through the central sector, two North Korean corps will attack near the east coast, and your corps is assigned the western road towards Seoul.<br><br>Break the positions covering that approach and advance with the neighbouring columns. United Nations artillery and aircraft remain powerful. Keep the movement concealed where the terrain permits until the assault groups are close enough to engage.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25, "support": [21]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [11, 16, 18]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["ncampsp2.xml", "Spring Offensive Second Phase", "Spring offensive: the eastern sector — 17 May 1951<br><br>The first spring attack did not recover Seoul. Our forces and the Chinese have shifted their effort towards the central and eastern mountains, where there are more ways around a defended road.<br><br>Drive south from Chunch'on and Kansong and take Sokcho and the hill positions controlling the approaches. Keep contact with the Chinese formations alongside you. The mountains offer cover from enemy aircraft, but they can also separate an advancing column from its food and ammunition.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25, "support": [21]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [6, 17, 18]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["ncampgue.xml", "Majon-ni", "MAJON-NI (11 November 1950)<br><br>Many troops left behind in the retreat have formed partisan groups. You are being sent to join one near Majon-ni, between Wonsan and Pyongyang. A South Korean battalion is reported cut off nearby, with American troops on their way to relieve it.<br><br>Use the local force to attack the enemy communications and prevent that relief. Your regular formations remain away for refitting and cannot join this operation; you will resume their command afterwards. For now, the men already in this district are the force you have.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [18]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["A Long Journey to Freedom (1848-1865)"],
["aljf_0.xml", "Prologue: Knechtschaft oder Revolution!", "Hecker must get through — 20 April 1848<br><br>Dear Friend, I have only time for a few lines. Hecker is negotiating with General von Gagern, but the federal troops demand an unconditional surrender. We have too few men to hold here if the talks fail.<br><br>Our orders are to bring Hecker safely east and find the supporters waiting along the Rhine and Neckar. We must leave before the troops close around us. The rising will need its people more than it needs this patch of ground.", [{"id": 1, "country": 176}], [{"id": 0, "country": 196}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_1.xml", "Der Heckerzug", "Hecker's uprising — 20 April 1848<br><br>Dear Friend, we are marching for a German republic. Volunteers are gathering in the towns, and the German Democratic Legion is approaching from the south. At last it feels as though our little column belongs to something larger.<br><br>We are to secure the towns around the Neckar and bring the force together for an advance on Freiburg. Enemy troops are approaching from the east, so the roads behind us must stay open. Karlsruhe will have to wait until we have the strength to reach it.<br><br>Hecker's assembly point is at position 29,29; he must join the march there.", [{"id": 1, "country": 176, "support": [175]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 196}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["aljf_2.xml", "The Palataine Uprising", "The Palatinate uprising — 13 June 1849<br><br>Dear Friend, the Palatinate has risen, and we have joined the fight again. Prussia is sending experienced troops against us. Their guns and discipline will be difficult to face in open country, however much courage our volunteers bring.<br><br>We are to take the towns that can support the rising and defend the routes between them. More volunteers may join where we establish control. The hills give us a chance to hold the Prussians while the new men are organised.", [{"id": 1, "country": 157, "support": [176]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 196}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["aljf_3.xml", "The decisive Battle at Wagh\u00e4usel", "Waghausel — 21 June 1849<br><br>Dear Friend, the Prussians have pushed us back across the Rhine. Baden's soldiers have joined the revolution, but enemy forces are closing from several directions and there is little room left behind us.<br><br>We must hold the positions around Waghausel and keep the army together. The new troops give us strength; they also need time to find their places in the line. If we are driven apart here, there may be no army left to defend the republic.", [{"id": 1, "country": 157, "support": [175]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 196, "support": [176]}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["aljf_4.xml", "The St. Luis Arsenal", "The St. Louis Arsenal — 10 May 1861<br><br>Dear Friend, for years our battles seemed far away. We taught, printed newspapers, built clubs and raised families here. Now Missouri is divided, and I am taking up arms again. I did not cross the ocean to see another man's freedom treated as property.<br><br>Our German volunteers need weapons, and the arsenal at St. Louis is the first task. Secure it and reopen the northern supply connections. There can be no proper re-equipment until those stores and roads are in our hands.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_5.xml", "The Boonville Races", "Boonville — 17 June 1861<br><br>Dear Friend, we have drawn modern weapons and are marching west from St. Louis. The Missouri carries men and supplies across the state; while the State Guard holds Boonville, that route remains insecure.<br><br>We are to take the town and clear the positions overlooking the river, with a ship supporting the advance. The opposing troops are still organising. My old sergeant says we should reach them before they have time to become an army.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_6.xml", "Flank them at Wilson's Creek", "Wilson's Creek — 10 August 1861<br><br>Dear Friend, Sigel has proposed a movement we remember from the German fighting: Lyon will engage the enemy in front while our column comes in behind. If the two attacks meet, we may break the force threatening our hold on Missouri.<br><br>We are to turn the enemy's rear and seize the positions along our advance. Hold what we take until the main force reaches us. Losing our last foothold would leave this detached column with nowhere to stand.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_7.xml", "Battle of the Hemp Bales", "The hemp bales at Lexington — 20 September 1861<br><br>Dear Friend, the hospital at Anderson's House is full and the canteens are almost empty. The spring is under fire. Now the State Guard is rolling wet hemp bales towards our works, and our shots do little to stop that moving shelter.<br><br>We are to hold Masonic College, the hospital and the approaches north of Lexington. There may be a chance to recover ground in the town, but first the line must survive the next assault. Every position abandoned brings their rifles closer to the wounded.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_8.xml", "Spearhead at Pea Ridge", "Pea Ridge — March 1862<br><br>Dear Friend, we are carrying the advance into Arkansas. The forces immediately ahead appear weak, but reports say Van Dorn is bringing another army towards them. What looks like a pursuit could become a battle on two fronts.<br><br>Take the positions around Pea Ridge and keep the enemy groups from joining. We need control of these approaches before their combined strength can turn us back towards Missouri.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_9.xml", "Assault at Kernstown", "Kernstown — 23 March 1862<br><br>Dear Friend, our march has brought us into the Shenandoah Valley. Its roads lead towards the Potomac, and Jackson's force can draw troops away from the main Union advance merely by threatening them.<br><br>We are to hold the Kernstown line while a second group takes Glasshouse to the west, then bring both groups against the Confederate positions. Our old flanking manoeuvre will be of little use if one column attacks before the other is ready.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_10.xml", "Retreat at Bull Run", "Retreat at Bull Run — 28 August 1862<br><br>Dear Friend, the enemy has turned our flank. Confederate troops are coming from the south, and the attack has begun before we can finish drawing back. The roads towards Washington must not be left open behind a broken army.<br><br>Our orders are to withdraw into the defensive positions and hold the whole line. Keep the columns moving through one another without losing their organisation. This will be harder than advancing: someone must always remain facing the pursuit.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_11.xml", "Must hold Harper's Ferry", "Harpers Ferry — 15 September 1862<br><br>Dear Friend, Harpers Ferry lies where two rivers meet beneath wooded heights. It is a beautiful place for a town and an alarming place to find oneself surrounded. The railway junction makes it too important to abandon lightly.<br><br>We are to defend the town and, if the opportunity opens, take Maryland Heights and threaten Jackson's headquarters at Keller. My sergeant says he can smell Confederates whichever way the wind blows. Today I believe him.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}, {"id": 2, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_12.xml", "Take Fredericksburg", "Fredericksburg — December 1862 (fictional force composition)<br><br>Dear Friend, the engineers are laying bridges across the Rappahannock. Beyond Fredericksburg the Confederate guns overlook the roads and railway from the heights. We have been ordered across that river and up those slopes.<br><br>The corps has received four regiments of Black infantry. They will share the assault with the men who have followed us since Missouri. We must find a way onto the heights without leaving successive regiments alone under the same batteries. I have rarely disliked the look of an order more.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_13.xml", "Battle of Chancellorsville", "Chancellorsville — 2 May 1863<br><br>Dear Friend, we are waiting in country they call the Wilderness. The woods hide everything beyond the next bend, and our scouts have lost contact with the enemy's main body. A quiet road here tells us very little.<br><br>Headquarters orders us to hold the line. Keep the approaches watched and the neighbouring formations in contact. If the Confederates come through these woods, there may be little warning before they are among the forward posts.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_14.xml", "The Siege of Vicksburg", "Vicksburg — 19 May 1863<br><br>Dear Friend, we are back beside the Mississippi. Vicksburg holds the river from its heights; beyond it, Port Hudson is the other remaining barrier to a Union passage. Opening the river would divide the Confederacy's eastern states from those to the west.<br><br>We are to take Vicksburg and secure the De Soto peninsula, with cavalry operating on the eastern approaches. The USS Moose has been assigned to the corps. Keep her with us: a gunboat that knows this river is worth more than another few rifles ashore.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_15.xml", "Gettysburg", "Gettysburg — 1 July 1863<br><br>Dear Friend, what began as a report of Confederate scouts is becoming a battle. Lee's army is close, and the troops around Gettysburg have only just taken their positions. Our corps was meant for another direction, but there is no question where it is needed now.<br><br>Bring the men up to strengthen the line, especially the Codori Heights. Enemy reinforcements are expected from the west; our own are coming from the east and south. The first task is to hold long enough for those scattered columns to become one army.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_16.xml", "Meeting at Bristoe Station", "Bristoe Station — 14 October 1863<br><br>Dear Friend, we have marched all day towards Manassas Junction, and now the firing ahead is growing. The Confederates have struck II Corps without realising how close our own column is behind it.<br><br>Repel the attack from the north and keep the army moving along the railway towards the withdrawal points. The passage must carry our men and the neighbouring formations, not just the first regiments to reach it. Leave a covering force until the tail of the column is clear.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_17.xml", "Seamonsters at Charleston", "Charleston — February 1864 (fictional assault)<br><br>Dear Friend, after a week aboard ship we finally know our destination: Charleston. Some troops are already ashore in the southern swamps, and our corps is to join them in an attack on the port. Most of the men would welcome any order that brought them onto dry ground.<br><br>The harbour forts cover the landing routes. Use the fleet to keep their guns occupied while the troops establish a foothold and advance on the city. We need Charleston itself; do not let every outlying battery draw the landing force into a separate siege.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_18.xml", "The Cadets in New Market", "New Market — May 1864<br><br>Dear Friend, Sigel is with us again. Over a drink we counted the years since the Rhine, but there was little time for old stories. Breckinridge is gathering troops against our advance through the Shenandoah Valley, including cadets from the Virginia Military Institute.<br><br>Our march is meant to protect the Union railway connections and break the Confederate ones. Clear the positions around New Market and secure the roads beyond them. We are deep in enemy country, with no neighbouring column close enough to rescue an isolated advance.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_19.xml", "Sigel's Last Command", "Harpers Ferry — 4 July 1864<br><br>Dear Friend, Early's approach has brought us back to Maryland Heights. Sigel withdrew the troops north of the Potomac rather than leave them trapped in Harpers Ferry. From here we can see the bridges we have been ordered to recover.<br><br>Retake the town and its crossings. The riverfront is defended; look for a passage that brings the troops onto the approaches instead of straight under the enemy's guns. We need the junction open again, with a force able to hold both banks.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_20.xml", "Our Marines at Mobile Bay", "Mobile Bay — 5 August 1864<br><br>Dear Friend, the voyage from New Orleans has brought us to Mobile Bay. The siege engineers aboard were a good clue: our task is to take the forts guarding the entrance and open the bay to the fleet.<br><br>The ships will bombard the positions before the troops land on the islands. Bring the landing parties ashore while the batteries are occupied. The old Moose is still with us; give her time to reach her place before the faster ships carry the attack ahead.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_21.xml", "The Siege of Petersburg", "Petersburg — 25 October 1864<br><br>Dear Friend, Petersburg's railways feed Richmond, and our army still holds only the eastern approaches. The crater left by the earlier mine is a warning of what another unsupported frontal assault would cost.<br><br>We are to extend the siege west and take the connections supplying the town. Reinforcements are coming from the east, with cavalry approaching from the south-east. Use them to close the routes that keep the Confederate army here; the fall of those junctions would threaten Richmond as well as Petersburg.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_22.xml", "The U.S.C.T. attacks Fort Fisher", "Fort Fisher — 13 January 1865<br><br>Dear Friend, we are off the Cape Fear River. Fort Fisher guards the naval approaches, and our corps is to land north of it while another force works towards the western positions. The fleet will support us, but Confederate vessels are still reported upriver.<br><br>Take the fort and the bases it protects. Bring engineers with the landing troops, and keep the ships to waters they can navigate. More naval support is coming. The Black regiments marching with us know as well as anyone what opening this coast may mean for the people still held in slavery beyond it.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_23.xml", "Close the Trap", "Close the trap — 1 April 1865<br><br>Dear Friend, Sigel has returned to command the cavalry, and new regiments have joined us after Fort Fisher. Around Petersburg the rains have swollen the rivers. The men joke that their next battle will be fought from gunboats, but the Confederate attack on our line has already begun.<br><br>Hold against that assault, then advance on Petersburg and the ground south of the Appomattox. Our cavalry must help close the remaining roads. Lee's army knows what losing them would mean and will fight to keep a way out.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_24.xml", "The Key to Richmond", "The key to Richmond — May 1865 (alternate history)<br><br>Dear Friend, Petersburg has fallen, but the Confederate government and army are still holding Richmond. Some of our men are already celebrating. Those of us studying the James River forts have put the celebration aside.<br><br>Advance north and take Drewry's and Chaffin's Bluff, securing the Richmond and Petersburg Railroad. Captured locomotives and river steamers can carry the heavy equipment, and our marines hold a bridgehead at the western ferry. Open the approaches so the whole corps can come against the capital.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_25.xml", "Final Assault at Richmond", "Final assault on Richmond — June 1865<br><br>Dear Friend, we are outside Richmond. The troops who began with us in Missouri have been joined by men who were enslaved when this war began. I think of the road from Germany whenever I look along their line.<br><br>Our orders are to enter the city and take the remaining Confederate positions. Marines, infantry and cavalry will reinforce the attack; keep the river passages open for them and draw battered regiments out before they are spent. I hope my next letter can tell you we are coming home.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["Hungarian Soviet Republic (1919)"],
["rhu190416.xml", "1919/04/16 Escaping from Zilah (Zalau)", "Escaping from Zilah (Zalau)<br><br>April 16, 1919<br><br>Comrade Commisar, the situation is dangerous. After our new, revolutionary government refused to retreat behind the new demarcation lines, the imperialist hyenas insited their capitalist lapdogs, the Romanian and the so called \"Czechoslovakian\" reactionists. They mobilized their armies and attacked our weak, inexperienced troops. Your job is securing the railway station at NagykÃ¡roly as long as possible to cover our retreat.<br><br>ORDER: Hold at least one VH, keep your MSU alive and move it onto the Escape Hex at NagykÃ¡roly.<br><br>NOTES:<br>- AI moves first.<br>- The longer you hold on, the better result you get.<br>- You have 3 free RTP slots.<br><br>12 Turns<br><br>Scenario designed by Csaba (lvjtn)", [{"id": 0, "country": 187}], [{"id": 1, "country": 13}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["rhu190424.xml", "1919/04/24 Breaking through Nyíregyháza", "Breaking through Nyíregyháza<br><br>April 24, 1919<br><br>Comrade Commisar, our troops weren't able to stop the overwhelmind Romanian attacks. We executed a few ex-KuK officers but it didn't help too much. We should retreat behind the Tisza River. You'd better hurry, two Romanian pincers are closing around Nyíregyháza.<br><br>ORDER: Hold at least one VH, keep your MSU alive and move it onto the Escape Hex at Tokaj.<br><br>NOTE: You have 3 free RTP slots.<br><br>16 Turns<br><br>Scenario designed by Csaba (lvjtn)", [{"id": 0, "country": 187}], [{"id": 1, "country": 13}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["rhu190501.xml", "1919/05/01 Szolnok: Securing The Bridgehead", "Szolnok: Securing The Bridgehead<br><br>May 1, 1919<br><br>Comrade Commisar, the Romanians have reached the Tisza, and a smaller vanguard has crossed the river at Szolnok. The retreat must end here and now, if the main troops of the reactionists can cross the Tisza, our proletarian state will collapse. Your job is to secure the western bank of the river and form a bridgehead on the eastern bank, if possible. But be cautious, more and more Romanian divisions are on their way.<br><br>ORDER: Hold at least 4 VHs and keep your MSU alive.<br><br>NOTES:<br>- You are awarded by an Ammunition Wagon (depot RTP) detachment.<br>- You can purchase two new units.<br>- You have 4 free RTP slots.<br><br>14 Turns<br><br>Scenario designed by Csaba (lvjtn)", [{"id": 0, "country": 187}], [{"id": 1, "country": 13}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["rhu190509.xml", "1919/05/09 Defending Salgótarján", "Defending Salgótarján<br><br>May 9, 1919<br><br>Comrade Commisar, while your troops defended Szolnok, the Czech henchmen of the capitalist warlords took Miskolc, the biggest industrial center in North-East Hungary. Now they are surrounding Salgótarján, the last city with steal factory and strong organized working class outside of Budapest. You should relieve Salgótarján immediately!<br><br>ORDER: Hold at least 2 VHs and keep your MSU alive.<br><br>NOTES:<br>- You can purchase three new units.<br>- You have 4 free RTP slots.<br><br>15 Turns<br><br>Scenario designed by Csaba (lvjtn)", [{"id": 0, "country": 187}], [{"id": 1, "country": 47}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["rhu190523.xml", "1919/05/23 Liberating Miskolc", "Liberating Miskolc<br><br>May 23, 1919<br><br>Comrade Commisar, tens of thousands proletars joined the Hungarian Red Army. These factory workers are eager to fight against the capitalist marauders and their mercenaries. Though our new red soldiers aren't trained well enough to defeat the Romanians, we are ready to push back the Czechs, who are famous for their low commitment to fight. Comrade, let's liberate Miskolc!<br><br>ORDER: Take all VHs and keep your MSU alive.<br><br>NOTES:<br>- You can purchase two new units.<br>- You have 5 free RTP slots.<br><br>20 Turns<br><br>Scenario designed by Csaba (lvjtn)", [{"id": 0, "country": 187}], [{"id": 1, "country": 47}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["rhu190530.xml", "1919/05/30  Liberating Kassa (Koice)", "Liberating Kassa (Koice)<br><br>May 30, 1919<br><br>Comrade Commisar, our offensive is going well, and our soldiers are eager to take a revenge for previous losses, another shiny victory would boost their morale. More importantly, there is a good opportunity to deliver a severe blow\tto the Czech marauders. Comrade, your job is to liberate Kassa with its important steel industry and railways junctions.<br><br>ORDER: Take all VHs and keep your MSU alive.<br><br>NOTES:<br>- You can purchase two new units.<br>- You have 5 free RTP slots.<br><br>18 Turns<br><br>Scenario designed by Csaba (lvjtn)", [{"id": 0, "country": 187}], [{"id": 1, "country": 47}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["rhu190609.xml", "1919/06/09 Bártfa (Bardejov): Reaching The Polish Border", "Bártfa (Bardejov): Reaching The Polish Border<br><br>June 9, 1919<br><br>Comrade Commisar, the Czech capitalists are in disarray, they didn't expect how strong the Red Army of workers and peasants could be when they get a proper training about the dialectical materialism. Now we have a unique chance to cut off the Czech defense lines and separate the Romanian and Czech invaders once and for all. Let the Iron Fist of the factory workers smash these imperialist bandits! Your order is to liberate Bártfa near the Polish border.<br><br>ORDER: Take all VHs and keep your MSU alive.<br><br>NOTES:<br>- You can purchase two new units.<br>- You have 5 free RTP slots.<br><br>20 Turns<br><br>Scenario designed by Csaba (lvjtn)", [{"id": 0, "country": 187}], [{"id": 1, "country": 47}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["rhu190613.xml", "1919/06/13 Defending Érsekújvár (Nové Zámky)", "Defending Érsekújvár (Nové Zámky)<br><br>June 13, 1919<br><br>Ah, dear Comrade Commisar, have you got the dedicated copy of Lenin's The State and Revolution? Comrade Szamuely has just arrived from Moscow with the warmest greetings and this special present for you. Our international revolution is going well, our Slovakian comrades will declare their Soviet Republic within days. Unfortunately these pesky Czech marauders simply can't accept their defeat, and they launched a strong counterattack in the area of Nyitra (Nitra) - Vág (Váh) - Garam (Hron) rivers. Give these imperialist lapdogs a bloody nose again!<br><br>ORDER: Hold at least 3 VHs and keep your MSU alive.<br><br>NOTES:<br>- You can repurchase only the lost units.<br>- Both sides get valuable reinforcements.<br>- You have 5 free RTP slots.<br><br>20 Turns<br><br>Scenario designed by Csaba (lvjtn)", [{"id": 0, "country": 187}], [{"id": 1, "country": 47}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["rhu190719.xml", "1919/07/19 Szolnok-Mezöhegyes Offensive", "Szolnok-Mezöhegyes Offensive<br><br>July 19, 1919<br><br>The imperialists fooled us. They promised the Romanian troops would withdraw behind the demarcation line declared on March 20 in exchange for our withdrawal from the Fölvidék (Upper Hungary). But the enemies of our communist revolution broke their words, and their Romanian mercenaries are still staying behind the Tisza. It's time to teach these truce-breakers a hard lesson and liberate our proletarian sisters and brothers by force! Lead our troops to victory, Comrade Commisar!<br><br>ORDER: Take all VHs and keep your MSU alive.<br><br>NOTES:<br>- You can repurchase only the lost units.<br>- AI gets valuable reinforcements.<br>- You have 6 free RTP slots.<br><br>20 Turns<br><br>Scenario designed by Csaba (lvjtn)", [{"id": 0, "country": 187}], [{"id": 1, "country": 13}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["rhu190724.xml", "1919/07/21 Szolnok: The Collapse", "Szolnok: The Collapse<br><br>July 24, 1919<br><br>Comrade Commisar, the situation is critical. Though we have managed to cross Tisza at three locations, and we have gained a large bridgehead east of Szolnok, our offensive has stalled. Our soldiers are exhausted, we have serious difficulties to resupply them, while more and more fresh Romanian troops are arriving at the battlefields. We suspects some of the former KuK officiers in our rank have betrayed our Soviet Republic and delivered important intels to the imperialists. Comrade, a strong and overwhelming capitalist counterattack is imminent! Save our revolution and do not let them cross the Tisza!<br><br>ORDER: Hold at least three VHs and keep your MSU alive.<br><br>NOTES:<br>- AI moves first.<br>- You can repurchase only the lost units.<br>- AI gets valuable reinforcements.<br>- You have 4 free RTP slots.<br><br>20 Turns<br><br>Scenario designed by Csaba (lvjtn)", [{"id": 0, "country": 187}], [{"id": 1, "country": 13}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["Bolshevik Cavalry (1918-1920)"],
["ccampore.xml", "Voronezh", "VORONEZH (22 OCTOBER 1919)<br><br>Comrade Commander, Denikin's advance has brought the White armies towards Moscow, but their widening front has left a flank exposed at Voronezh. Our Eighth Army is still fighting on the Don, and reinforcements are coming from the north.<br><br>Bring your cavalry corps against Voronezh from the west. Take the crossings and junctions before the White command can reinforce them. A breakthrough here will threaten the side of the army advancing on the capital.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["ccampros.xml", "Rostov", "ROSTOV (6 January 1920)<br><br>The White armies are falling back towards the Don. Rostov controls the roads into the Caucasus, and their retreating formations need its crossings to stay connected.<br><br>Take Rostov before they can organise a defence around the city. Use the cavalry to reach the junctions ahead of the retreat. The following formations need those roads open if the offensive is to continue south.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["ccampvol.xml", "Battle of Volodarka", "BATTLE OF VOLODARKA (29 May 1920)<br><br>Your divisions have reached the Polish front south of Kiev. The enemy's advance has taken the city, but its line through the countryside is stretched between widely separated positions.<br><br>Force a passage near Volodarka and open it for the infantry following your cavalry. The Third Don Cossack Brigade is coming to support the attack. A breach here would threaten the roads behind the Polish troops at Kiev.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["ccampkie.xml", "Kiev Counteroffensive", "KIEV COUNTEROFFENSIVE (9 June 1920)<br><br>Our offensive north and south of Kiev has forced the Polish armies back. The Twelfth Army is approaching from the east; your cavalry is in position to threaten the roads out of the city from the south.<br><br>Take Kiev, establish contact with the Twelfth Army and carry the advance west. Reach the crossings before the retreating troops can destroy them. Without those bridges, the infantry and guns will struggle to follow the cavalry.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20, "support": [64]}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["ccamprov.xml", "Delay at Rovno", "DELAY AT ROVNO (1 July 1920)<br><br>The advance from Kiev has brought us to Rovno. Lwow remains the army's direction, but Polish troops are holding the junctions along the route and fighting to gain time for another line farther west.<br><br>Take Rovno and the communications centres around it. Keep the roads between the divisions open as the advance continues. The horses need food as urgently as the guns need ammunition; a column cut off from its supplies will soon lose its speed.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20, "support": [64]}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["ccampbro.xml", "Battle of Brody", "Brody — 29 July 1920<br><br>The First Cavalry Army has reached Brody on the road towards Lwow. Polish formations have fallen back, but they can still gather against the gaps between our extended divisions.<br><br>Secure Brody and the surrounding junctions. Bring the horse artillery forward as the cavalry clears the approaches. The next advance depends on keeping the divisions connected through this road network.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20, "support": [191]}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["ccampzad.xml", "Battle of Zadworze", "BATTLE OF ZADWORZE (17 August 1920)<br><br>Lwow is close, but cavalry cannot take a defended city without infantry and a reliable supply route. Zadworze's railway junction stands between our leading regiments and the support following them.<br><br>Take the junction and open the line. We do not yet know the strength of the force holding it. Clear the approaches quickly enough for the infantry and guns to come forward before Lwow's defenders can complete their preparations.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["ccamplwo.xml", "Lwow", "LWOW (20 August 1920)<br><br>The city is ahead of us, Comrade. Our formations are closing on Lwow from the north and east, with the Fourteenth Army's infantry following the cavalry.<br><br>Enter the city and take the positions controlling its approaches. Prisoners report that the delay at Zadworze has given the defenders time to prepare. Keep contact with the infantry; the streets will give the enemy chances that the open country did not.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20, "support": [64]}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["ccampkom.xml", "Battle of Komarow", "BATTLE OF KOMAROW (29 August 1920)<br><br>The Polish counteroffensive has broken through between Lwow and Warsaw. Our northern armies are retreating to avoid encirclement, and the cavalry has been ordered away from Lwow to help restore the front.<br><br>Break the line at Komarow and push north towards our retreating armies. The Polish forces have used our change of direction to place troops across the route. Open it before their pressure separates the two halves of the front completely.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["ccampro2.xml", "Retreat from Rovno", "RETREAT FROM ROVNO (18 September 1920)<br><br>The campaign has turned against us. Polish troops hold Rovno and are extending their counteroffensive into the south. Our divisions need time to recover, but they will not get it while the enemy closes around them here.<br><br>Bring the army east through the withdrawal routes. Keep the scattered regiments together and cover the crossings until the guns and supply columns are clear. We can reorganise an army that gets away; we cannot replace one left in a pocket.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["ccampwr1.xml", "Kakhovka", "KAKHOVKA (20 October 1920)<br><br>Wrangel has pushed out of the Crimea while our attention was on Poland. His troops are spread across the country north of Perekop, with the narrow isthmus behind them as their route back to the peninsula.<br><br>Cross the Dnieper near Kakhovka and break into their rear. The cavalry must reach the routes towards Perekop before the White columns do. Cut them off from the fortified entrance to the Crimea.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["ccampwr2.xml", "Perekop", "PEREKOP (28 October 1920)<br><br>Our advance is nearing Perekop. White formations are falling back towards the isthmus, where a narrow front would allow them to hold with far fewer men.<br><br>Press on and force a passage into the Crimea before the retreating troops can settle behind those defences. Other armies are clearing the pockets farther north; their troops will join you as they become available. Until then, the speed of your cavalry is our best chance.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["ccampwr3.xml", "Sevastopol", "Sevastopol — 11 November 1920<br><br>The northern approaches to the Crimea are open, and Wrangel's troops are withdrawing towards the ports. Ships off Sevastopol offer them a way to carry an army away even after the peninsula is lost.<br><br>Advance on the port and clear the positions along the roads into it. The cavalry can reach the approaches quickly, but the rearguards still have guns and machine guns. Take the last base before they can turn the streets into another defensive line.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100, "support": [151]}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["The November Revolution (1918)"],
["n_kiel.xml", "1918 Kieler Matrosenaufstand", "1918 - Sailors revolt<br><br>No one still wants war, but the government does not get it. It sends the German fleet into the final battle against the Royal Navy. Your comrades defend themselves. This means mutiny. The ships turned back. The mutineers, however, were captured ...<br>Your comrades need help. Karl Artelt and Lothar Popp, leader of the revolt and USPD members, stand by your side. Go in and win!! <br><br>Note: The Steinhäuser Patrol is on the way to knock down the revolt ...<br><br>Historical:<br>The fleet had been moved from Kiel to Wilhelmshaven to set from there sail to the last battle. Despite utmost secrecy the plans came through to the crews.<br>Thereupon the sailors on three ships of the Third Naval Battle Squadron refused to weigh anchor for the last naval battle of WW1.<br>Part of the crew of SMS Thüringen and SMS Helgoland, two battle ships of the First Naval Battle Squadron, committed outright mutiny and sabotage. However, when a day later some torpedo boats directed their cannons onto these ships, the mutineers gave up and were led away without any resistance.<br>The fleet again entered Kiel. 47 sailors were arrested and detained at the naval base 'Wilhelm Souchon'.<br>Some 250 sailors met in the evening of 1 November in the Union House in Kiel and prevented the fleet from setting sail again. <br>The Revolution started from here with the sailor Karl Artelt and shipyard worker Lothar Popp (both USPD) as ringleaders.<br>The next day, police closed the Union House. Several thousand sailors and workers moved to the \"Großer Exerzierplatz\" (large drill ground). Under the slogan: \"peace and bread\" they demanded the release of the mutineers.<br>On 4 November the governor of the naval base, Wilhelm Souchon, gave way and let the detained sailors free. However, foreign troops marched on to defeat the movement.<br>These were intercepted by the rebels, captured, or joined the uprising.<br>On the evening of 4 November's Kiel was firmly in the hands of about 40,000 rebellious sailors, soldiers and workers.", [{"id": 1, "country": 117}], [{"id": 0, "country": 188}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["n_willhelmsh.xml", "1918 Willhelmshafen", "1918 Willhelmshafen<br><br>After Kiel, the naval base of Wilhelmshaven is now rebelling. Under the leadership of Bernhard Kuhnt, you are now the one representative for the Council of the 21, whom the revolution now badly needs<br>Conquer the north, Aurich, Emden and especially the reservists garrison Oldenburg!!!<br><br>Historically: <br><br>In Wilhelmshaven-Rüstringen was founded on 6th November 1918, after a mass demonstration of over 20,000 naval and shipyard workers and other civilians a workers and Soldiers Council, with its executive organ, the so-called Council or the 21.<br>To Chairman of the Council was appointed Bernhard Kuhnt. The \"21er\" Council <br>took over the power of the fortified towns,the North Sea Station,the encircling land of Oldenburg in Ostfriesland and all the surrounding islands, without resistance of the military station commands and declared on 10 November 1918 in front of 100,000 enthusiastic demonstrators in Wilhelmshaven,<br>the Socialist Republic of Oldenburg and the deposition of the Grand Duke of Oldenburg.<br>Under the impression of demonstrations and pressure from the large majority of Members of Parliament,Grand Duke Friedrich August of Oldenburg declared his abdication on 11 November 1918.<br>The Free State of Oldenburg was therefore declared in the territory of the Grand Duchy of Oldenburg.<br>As a provisional government was formed a Land-governing-body, to what, among others, the Rüstringer Member of Parliament Paul Hug and Kuhnt belonged.<br>Kuhnt became president of the new Free State of Oldenburg.<br>-------------------------------------<br><br>Autor = Matze (M. Kessler)", [{"id": 1, "country": 117}], [{"id": 0, "country": 188}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["n_frankfurt.xml", "1918 Der Aufstand erfasst Frankfurt am Main", "1918 The revolt comes upon Frankfurt<br><br>7 November<br><br>The revolution is fomented. The coastal towns are in our hands. Now freed Frankfurt on Main and  conquer by this the city of Finance, or can Großherzog Ernst Ludwig of Hessen put down the rebellion?<br><br>Historical:<br>According to the Sailors' revolt in Kiel, the revolution spreads to Frankfurt<br><br>There they formed Workers' and Soldiers' Councils and called for the abdication of Grand Duke Ernst Ludwig of Hesse. But he refuses ...<br><br>Autor = Matze (M. Kessler)", [{"id": 1, "country": 117}], [{"id": 0, "country": 188}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["n_berlin.xml", "1918 Ende der Monarchie", "1918 End of the Monarchy<br><br>When the Emperor heard of the revolts in Kiel, he orderd the 4th Jäger Regiment to Berlin. The city burns. The insurgents have the working-class neighborhoods under control.<br><br>Can Police and Jäger put down the rebellion? Or has the Kaiser to quit and leave Berlin?<br><br>there is little support announced for both sides ..<br><br>Historical :<br>In reality, everything went bloodless. After the revolt in Kiel, Wilhelmshaven and other towns the USPD planned in Berlin mass demonstrations and a general strike for the 9th November 1918 . This was heard by the competing SPD under leadership of its chairman, Friedrich Ebert.<br><br>In order to remain master of the situation, <br><br>To anticipate the USPD, Ebert forced Chancellor Max von Baden to announce the abdication of Wilhelm II. <br>The Kaiser was this time at Spa, where the allied armistice terms had been previously negotiated. He then fled to his Dutch exile where he signed the abdication on 28.11.1919.<br><br>Autor = Matze (M. Kessler)", [{"id": 1, "country": 117}], [{"id": 0, "country": 188}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["The Defeat of Denikin (1918-1920)"],
["volarm_00.xml", "The Ice March", "The Ice March<br><br>February 23rd, 1918<br><br>Rostov is ours. The Volunteer Army left in the dark and has gone off the railway into open steppe, where our armoured trains cannot follow.<br><br>Nobody is chasing it into the snow. Take the Don crossings behind it instead - Rostov, Aksaiskaya, Ol'ginskaya - so that nothing of theirs can turn back on the city. Let four of their formations get clear and the Kuban gets an army.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_01.xml", "Tragedy at Ekaterinodar", "Tragedy at Ekaterinodar<br><br>April 9th, 1918<br><br>Kornilov has six thousand men and no base. There are three times that in Ekaterinodar, and he will attack anyway, because he can attack or starve on the steppe.<br><br>He will not try the front of the city: a crossing is being prepared to the west, at Elizabetinskaya. Hold both faces and take Takhtamukay across the river, where his column forms up.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_02.xml", "Belaya Glina", "Belaya Glina<br><br>June 28th, 1918<br><br>Denikin is back in the Kuban with nine thousand men, German rifles bought through Krasnov, and the whole Don behind him. Torgovaya has gone and the Tsaritsyn railway is cut.<br><br>Nothing is coming from the north: Moscow has the Germans in the Ukraine and the Czechoslovak revolt on the Volga. Hold Belaya Glina, Novopokrovskaya and Peschanokopskoye - while we sit on those junctions this army still has a spine.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_03.xml", "The battle for Ekaterinodar", "The battle for Ekaterinodar<br><br>August 13th, 1918<br><br>Tikhoretskaya has gone and Denikin has brought up everything he has for the capital of the Kuban. Half the stanitsas have gone over to him.<br><br>His recruiting is also his weakness: behind him the land goes back to its 1916 owner, the ataman returns, and the punitive detachment explains it to the village - and those villages recruit for us. Hold Ekaterinodar and the western crossing; clear Plastunovskaya, where his staff sits.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_04.xml", "The Taman Army", "The Taman Army<br><br>August 23rd, 1918<br><br>The Taman group is cut off by two hundred versts of White cavalry, sea on one flank and mountains on the other, with thirty thousand people on the road and a rifle for one in three.<br><br>Kovtyukh has one route - the coast road east through Gelendzhik - and German warships to keep him out of the harbour. The order is four words long: get the columns out. Not the ground, not the guns.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_05.xml", "Stavropol", "Stavropol<br><br>November 10th, 1918<br><br>Denikin has drawn a ring round this army from three sides and is pressing it back on the mountains. Stavropol has changed hands twice, and both times cost whole regiments.<br><br>We are the 11th Army on paper, which has improved nothing, and the typhus takes more of us than the shelling. Hold Stavropol and the villages covering the road out of it. Wrangel is coming from the west, Drozdovsky from the north.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_06.xml", "Grozny", "Grozny<br><br>February 1st, 1919<br><br>The Great War ended in November, the Germans are gone from the Ukraine, and the Entente has begun unloading at Novorossiysk for Denikin: rifles, shells, instructors. Wrangel is at Vladikavkaz.<br><br>The Terek is the last thing we hold south of the Don and it is going a stanitsa at a time. Hold Grozny, Shali and Samashki - behind them there is nothing but the passes.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_07.xml", "The Manych", "The Manych<br><br>May 1st, 1919<br><br>The 10th Army put itself across the Manych in the winter and for a few weeks the southern front looked like splitting in two. Wrangel has brought his Caucasus corps up by rail with British armour.<br><br>This steppe belongs to whoever has the most horses, which is not us, so it comes down to the crossings. Hold Velikoknyazheskaya, Uyutnyy and Ekaterinovka; Torgovaya, taken in the winter and lost again, is worth having back.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_08.xml", "Tsaritsyn", "Tsaritsyn<br><br>June 14th, 1919<br><br>The Cossacks have come at this town three times and gone back three times with nothing, which is why the papers call it the Red Verdun. The workers' regiments, the armoured trains and the gunboats are all still here.<br><br>What is different is Wrangel, the tanks the British landed for him, and our own front north of here coming apart since the Veshenskaya rising. Hold Tsaritsyn, its approaches and the river crossing; clear their heavy batteries off Gorodistsje.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_09.xml", "Oboyan", "Oboyan<br><br>August 12th, 1919<br><br>Denikin's Moscow Directive is three armies on three axes for one capital. May-Mayevsky is coming up the Kharkov railway to deliver the middle of it, and Mamontov's cavalry is already in our rear areas.<br><br>The 13th Army is to hold the Oboyan-Pristen line long enough for the reserves forming at Orel and Tula to be worth something. That is a screen, and everyone has been careful to call it something else. Break their group at Yakovlevo and buy three weeks.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_10.xml", "Peregonovka", "Peregonovka<br><br>September 26th, 1919<br><br>Makhno's people have retreated west across half the Ukraine for a month with Slashchev driving them. This morning the whole Insurgent Army turned round in the dark and went at the pursuit head-on.<br><br>There is a great deal between us politically and there will be a reckoning. Tonight that is not the point: the group at Peregonovka is Denikin's, it sits astride the railway to his rear while his front line reaches for Orel, and it can be destroyed.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_11.xml", "Orel: the avalanche", "Orel: the avalanche<br><br>October 11th, 1919<br><br>Kutepov is coming up the Moscow highway with the Kornilov, Markov, Drozdovsky and Alekseyev regiments - officers with nothing left to go home to, and nobody has stopped them this summer.<br><br>We are not asked to stop them either. Hold Orel, Mtsensk, Kromy and Dmitrovsk long enough for the shock group forming behind Kromy - the Latvian riflemen, the Estonians, Primakov's Chervonny Cossacks - to come into line unspent.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_12.xml", "Orel: the storm", "Orel: the storm<br><br>October 16th, 1919<br><br>Five days ago their newspapers printed the distance from Orel to Moscow. They were right about the distance and wrong about everything else.<br><br>That corps has fought eleven weeks without a reserve on a widening front; Makhno is across its supply line, and its regiments are officers, who cannot be replaced out of villages it has just requisitioned. The shock group goes in at Kromy, where its line of retreat runs. Take Orel back.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_13.xml", "Tula", "Tula (alternate history)<br><br>November 3rd, 1919<br><br>Tula makes the rifles. That sentence is the whole of the situation. Their advanced parties are at Plavsk, thirty versts down the road.<br><br>Against them: the workers' regiments of the arms works, a fortified belt the townspeople dug themselves through October, and six divisions freed from Voronezh and Tsaritsyn - which the enemy made possible by concentrating everything here and leaving his own left flank in the air. Hold the belt.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_14.xml", "Moscow", "Moscow<br><br>December 12th, 1919<br><br>Their cavalry is in the outer suburbs. The Council of Defence has not left, the Kremlin garrison is in the line, and the barricades were thrown up by people carrying their own tools.<br><br>Hold the three southern sectors and Red Square. Volkhonka on the Kaluga road is where their staff and heavy batteries have come up; take it and the attack loses its hinge. There is no line behind this one, which simplifies the orders.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_15.xml", "Petrograd", "Petrograd<br><br>January 26th, 1920<br><br>This sector is detached to the 7th Army, and the opponent is no longer Denikin but Yudenich - the North-Western Army, armed out of Reval, with British tanks and naval guns off Kronstadt.<br><br>Petrograd has been stripped for every other front for two years; what is left is the workers' regiments, the sailors and the courses cadets. Hold the city sectors and the airfield - their road in, and their road out, runs through the Moscow highway junction.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_16.xml", "Kharkov", "Kharkov<br><br>December 4th, 1919<br><br>Since Orel this front has not stopped. Kursk went in November, Budyonny is cutting the Donets railway in three places, and the army that was to be in Moscow by Christmas cannot man its own line.<br><br>It is also finding out what its rear is worth: the districts it requisitioned all summer send it no recruits. Kharkov is the hinge - take the three city sectors and the Donbass position goes with them. Be quick; their rearguard is fighting for days, not ground.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_17.xml", "Novorossiysk", "Novorossiysk<br><br>March 12th, 1920<br><br>The Kuban has gone, Rostov has gone, Ekaterinodar went last week, and everything left of them is trying to get into the last port they hold on this coast.<br><br>In the roadstead are British and French warships and nothing like enough transports; their command has listed who is taken off, and the men who are not have worked that out for themselves. Take the Novorossiysk port, or break up the evacuation columns at the moles.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_18.xml", "Perekop", "Perekop<br><br>November 7th, 1920<br><br>Wrangel has spent a summer turning the isthmus into a fortress - the Turkish Wall, the Yushun positions, eight belts of wire, every gun the French landed. He has said publicly that it cannot be taken.<br><br>So it will not be taken the way he built it to be taken. The front attacks frontally while the Sivash, which this wind makes fordable, is crossed the same night. Take Armyansk and the wall, then Krasnoperekopsk and Zalivnaye behind it.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["Czech Legion - Siberian Anabasis (1917-1920)"],
["acampzbo.xml", "Zborov", "Zborov<br><br>July 2nd, 1917<br><br>Four months ago there was a Tsar. There is now a Provisional Government, a committee in every regiment, and an offensive ordered by a minister who has never commanded anything.<br><br>Half the divisions here have voted not to attack, and the men are not cowards: they have worked out that the government asking for one more push is the same one that will not give them the land. The Czechoslovak brigade is the exception - volunteers who face severe punishment if captured by the empire against which they have taken up arms. Their objective is Pluhiv, behind the Austrian third line.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 143}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["acampkie.xml", "Kiev", "Kiev<br><br>February 28th, 1918<br><br>The old army has not weakened, it has dissolved: there are no armies, there are trains full of men going home. Eleven German divisions are marching into the Ukraine at forty versts a day.<br><br>In Kiev is everything Soviet power in the Ukraine still owns - the arsenal detachments, the Red Guard, the archives, the treasury, and eleven thousand people who will be shot or hanged if they are here when the Germans arrive. Five days: hold the Dnieper bridges until they are out.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 117}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["acampbac.xml", "Bachmach", "Bachmach<br><br>March 13th, 1918<br><br>The treaty signed on the third is the worst peace any Russian government has put its name to - Poland, the Baltic, Finland, the Ukraine, a third of the population. A government with no army cannot bargain.<br><br>The new border is east of here, and through this junction must pass sixty thousand legionnaires and every train of grain that can be got out. The Legion covers the junction, we cover the crossing, by written agreement. Hold Konotop and Bachmach until the echelons are through.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 117}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["acamptsj.xml", "Chelyabinsk", "Chelyabinsk<br><br>May 14th, 1918<br><br>It began with a stove leg thrown from a train. Legionnaires going east, Hungarian and Austrian prisoners going home under the treaty, and four years of a war they were all in on opposite sides between them.<br><br>The Soviet arrested the men who lynched the thrower, which was correct; the Legion took the arsenal and freed them by force, which was not; and Moscow has wired an order to disarm a corps strung out over six thousand versts, which it will refuse. Hold the Chelyabinsk prison and the station.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 144}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["acampsam.xml", "Samara", "Samara — May 1918<br><br>The Legion's conflict with Soviet authority is spreading along the railway. Armed echelons are moving through the towns, and opponents of the Bolsheviks see a chance to organise behind them.<br><br>Hold Samara and the stations covering its bridge. The local Red forces are too few to defend every mile of track. Keep the crossings and the route out open while our scattered detachments withdraw towards the city.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 144}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["acampkaz.xml", "Kazan", "Kazan<br><br>August 7th, 1918<br><br>Six hundred million roubles of Imperial gold are in the vaults under this city, still here because the order to move them came too late. That is why the attack is here and not somewhere sensible.<br><br>Kappel has three thousand men; the Fifth Army is nine days old and is still pulling its scattered formations into a defence. Nobody is promised the gold stays. What can be saved is the army and the crossings - and an army that survives can come back for Kazan.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 144}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["acampoms.xml", "Omsk", "Omsk<br><br>December 22nd, 1918<br><br>On the eighteenth of November the officers arrested the Directory in its beds, and Admiral Kolchak has proclaimed himself Supreme Ruler in Omsk, with British advisers and Japanese money.<br><br>Tonight the city rises: the Kulomzino workshops, the garrison's Second Regiment, the underground, and two hundred prisoners who will be freed or shot depending on the hour. The garrison can turn its strength against the rising at any moment. Hold the workers' quarters long enough for those who can get out to get out.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 144}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["acampsem.xml", "Semenov", "Semenov<br><br>February 10th, 1920<br><br>Kolchak was shot at Irkutsk three days ago by sentence of a revolutionary committee, after the Legion handed him over with the gold for a clear line east.<br><br>What is left is Transbaikalia, which was never really his. Ataman Semenov has held the line from Chita eastward for two years on Japanese money and armoured trains, station by station, with a firing party. The partisans here are the villages themselves and have fought him without us since 1918. Chita is the knot.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 191}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["acampwla.xml", "Vladivostok", "Vladivostok<br><br>March 10th, 1920<br><br>Nine thousand versts of railway from Bachmach, and a city at the end of it that belongs to nobody in particular. In January the partisans and the Zemstvo took Vladivostok without much of a fight.<br><br>What they did not take, and cannot, is the garrison: Japanese divisions in the port and the last of the Legion on the quay. Tokyo has not decided whether to go or to stay. Avoid a battle with the garrison and bring the couriers through to the contact point.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 152}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["acampka2.xml", "Kazan: the Red offensive", "Kazan: the Red offensive<br><br>September 10th, 1918<br><br>One month, and the Fifth Army has been rebuilt from the outside in: commissars, tribunals, a supply service, forty-eight guns, the Volga flotilla brought up from Nizhny.<br><br>Opposite, the People's Army is coming apart - conscripts deserting in companies, the Legion going home after all, and Kappel's three thousand unable to hold a city of two hundred thousand that does not want them. This is the first attack this army has made. Take the Romanov Bridge, Kazan and the eastern railway.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 144}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["acampufa.xml", "Ufa", "Ufa — 9 June 1919<br><br>The advance has reached the Belaya. Chapayev's Twenty-Fifth Division is fighting for Ufa, while Kolchak's retreating troops still need the railway east of the city to get across the Urals.<br><br>Take Alatorka and the Iglino junction, keeping our positions around Ufa secure. Cut the line before the White rearguards can cover the withdrawal. A town taken with the enemy already safely beyond it would leave the next battle to be fought all over again.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 144}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["The Polish-Soviet War: The Red Advance (1919-1920)"],
["polsov_01.xml", "Approach to Wilno", "Approach to Wilno<br><br>April 15th, 1919<br><br>There is no front here - a railway, four towns on it, nobody in between. Every division that could hold this ground is in the Ukraine or on the Don.<br><br>Pilsudski is not trying to break the screen but to get behind it, and Moscow will spend nothing on Wilno: the group is not to be encircled, and the road south stays open until the city Soviet and the rolling stock are out. Hold Olita, Orany and Lida until the order to withdraw.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["polsov_02.xml", "Assault on Wilno", "Assault on Wilno<br><br>April 18th, 1919<br><br>They came in at first light along the railway - an armoured train and a cavalry group that rode through the gap to Lida in the dark and were in the streets before the garrison knew the line was cut.<br><br>The city is going; that was decided at Olita three days ago. What is not decided is the twelve thousand men and four hospital trains north and east of it, and the city Soviet. Hold Malaty, Swieciany and Wilno until they are through.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["polsov_03.xml", "Minsk and the Berezina", "Minsk and the Berezina<br><br>August 4th, 1919<br><br>The Western Front has sixteen thousand bayonets on four hundred versts and orders that begin with the word nevertheless. Everything that can march is committed against Denikin and Kolchak.<br><br>Pilsudski takes Minsk now because Denikin has told Paris that a Polish state is a temporary administrative inconvenience - so Warsaw has a short season in which our defeat is not yet their defeat. The city cannot be held; the Berezina line behind it can. Hold Minsk, Stolpce and the crossings until the 16th Army is on that line.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["polsov_04.xml", "Dyneburg: the Latgale winter", "Dyneburg: the Latgale winter<br><br>January 3rd, 1920<br><br>Minus twenty-five, snow to the waist off the roads, and not a machine on either side that starts without a fire under it. The 15th Army has been in these positions since November.<br><br>The Polish attack, with the Latvian army from the north-west, is political before it is military: put Latgale in Riga's hands and cut the wire between us and Kaunas. The town will be given up if it must be; the corps may not. Hold Dyneburg and the positions covering the crossing while the corps comes through.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["polsov_05.xml", "Zhitomir: the Polish blow", "Zhitomir: the Polish blow<br><br>April 25th, 1920<br><br>Three Polish armies and Petliura's two divisions came through the 12th and 14th this morning on a hundred-verst frontage. The 12th is coming apart into detachments.<br><br>The object is not Kiev but a Ukrainian state under Petliura, bought last week with eastern Galicia and western Volhynia - four million Ukrainians sold to hire an army, and the villages know it. The countryside may turn against them, but our army must survive the attack already under way. Hold the Korosten-Zhitomir-Kazatin triangle.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["polsov_06.xml", "The Dnieper crossings", "The Dnieper crossings<br><br>May 5th, 1920<br><br>The order is to give up Kiev without fighting for it, and it is the right order: the city is a salient with a river at its back and their cavalry already north of it at Chernobyl.<br><br>A garrison left in it would be a garrison lost, and the 12th Army is worth more than the honour of the streets. The rearguard has the demolition parties, the mined roads and the wire, and almost nothing that moves. Hold the Dnieper crossings until the last battery is over.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["polsov_07.xml", "The Red tide", "The Red tide<br><br>June 4th, 1920<br><br>The Konarmia is up: fourteen thousand sabres that walked from the Kuban to the Dnieper in fifty-three days. Tomorrow they go into the seam between the Polish 3rd and 6th Armies at Samhorodok.<br><br>Their whole position rests on a front too long for the men holding it, in a country their own requisition parties have turned against them. Break the crust and there is nothing behind it but staffs and depots. Take Zhitomir, Korosten, Fastov and Kazatin - their army cannot withdraw in order without them.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["polsov_08.xml", "Before Warsaw: the Wkra", "Before Warsaw: the Wkra<br><br>August 13th, 1920<br><br>The 1st Cavalry Army was sent for Lvov and has twice been told to come north without coming, and there is a gap of a hundred and fifty versts between the halves of our own front.<br><br>The Polish workers who were to rise have volunteered by the hundred thousand instead: an army crossing the Vistula looks less like a revolution than like Russia. The task is not the capital but that this army group is not bagged - hold Ciechanow, Pultusk and Nasielsk, and bring the divisional cores out east.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["polsov_09.xml", "Komarow: the Konarmia breaks out", "Komarow: the Konarmia breaks out<br><br>August 31st, 1920<br><br>The Konarmia turned north on the twentieth with Warsaw already lost, and has spent the week riding into a pocket that closed behind it. The Polish 1st Cavalry Division is astride the eastern road at Komarow.<br><br>The cavalry must fight for a road junction because it is the only way out. Twelve regiments against six, in fog, at the sabre - and the arithmetic does not help, because they only have to stand. Break out east past Komarow and keep the army.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["polsov_10.xml", "The Niemen", "The Niemen<br><br>September 20th, 1920<br><br>Six weeks ago this army was at the gates of Warsaw. It is digging on the Niemen now with eight thousand rifles where it had thirty, and the conference at Riga has opened.<br><br>The line where the war stops will be roughly the line the armies stand on, so every verst held into October is a verst at the table - and Warsaw attacks now precisely because the Entente is about to impose an armistice. Hold Grodno, Lida and the Niemen crossings until the order to withdraw.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["polsov_11.xml", "Back to Minsk", "Back to Minsk<br><br>October 9th, 1920<br><br>Peace negotiations at Riga are approaching an agreement, but the guns have not yet stopped. This morning Zeligowski's division mutinied, on orders nobody in Warsaw will put in writing, and took Wilno from the Lithuanians.<br><br>Both commands know that the military position will weigh heavily in the peace negotiations. So the front goes forward once more - not for Minsk, already behind our line, but for Molodeczno, Radoszkowicze and the junctions west of it.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["Ejercito Popular (1936-1939)"],
["gce1.xml", "Batalla por Madrid", "Madrid — 13 November 1936<br><br>Commander, the Army of Africa has reached Madrid's western and southern approaches. The direct road into the capital runs through the Casa de Campo and across the Manzanares. If the attackers establish themselves beyond the river, the defence becomes a fight from building to building.<br><br>Hold the bridges and the university district, and recover Puente de los Franceses. Republican mixed brigades, militia and International Brigade volunteers are sharing the defence. Keep a reserve inside the city to seal any crossing the enemy forces. Madrid must remain the centre of our resistance. No pasaran.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225, "support": [208, 209, 214]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226, "support": [203, 205, 206, 210]}], "eqp-gce"],
["gce2.xml", "Valle del Jarama", "Jarama Valley — 16 February 1937<br><br>The direct assault on Madrid has failed, and the Nationalists are trying to cut the road linking the capital with Valencia. The Jarama valley is now the hinge of that attempt to isolate the city.<br><br>Hold the river positions and Morata de Tajuna, then counterattack towards Perales and Pinto. Cerro de los Angeles must remain secure while the line is restored. Our divisions and International Brigade units have Soviet-supplied armour, but experienced enemy infantry stands between them and the road we need to keep open.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225, "support": [207, 208, 209, 214]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226, "support": [206]}], "eqp-gce"],
["gce3.xml", "Batalla de Guadalajara", "Guadalajara — 8 March 1937<br><br>Italian troops of the Corpo Truppe Volontarie are advancing on the Guadalajara front with Nationalist support. Their purpose is to approach Madrid from the north-east and complete the encirclement that the Jarama offensive failed to achieve.<br><br>Stop the columns on the Brihuega-Torija approaches, hold Guadalajara and counterattack towards Algora. The roads concentrate the Italian advance. Our tanks and aircraft can strike there once the infantry has held the leading formations and drawn them away from their reserves.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225, "support": [214]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226, "support": [206]}], "eqp-gce"],
["gce4.xml", "Ofensiva de Brunete", "Brunete — 6 July 1937<br><br>Commander, the Republic is taking the offensive west of Madrid. A breakthrough here threatens the Nationalist salient near the capital and may force the enemy to divert troops from the hard-pressed northern front.<br><br>V and XVIII Corps will move from the north on Brunete and Villafranca del Castillo, with support from the Madrid direction. Take the towns and the strongpoints through Quijorna and Villaviciosa de Odon. Keep Valdemorillo secure behind the attack; we need the roads open before the enemy's reserves arrive.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225, "support": [207, 208, 209, 214]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226, "support": [206]}], "eqp-gce"],
["gce5.xml", "Ofensiva de Aragon", "Aragon offensive — 24 August 1937<br><br>Brunete did not produce the breakthrough headquarters wanted. The northern front remains under pressure, and a new offensive in Aragon is intended to draw Nationalist reserves away from it.<br><br>Attack through Quinto, Fuentes de Ebro, Mediana and Belchite, with another thrust towards Zuera. Zaragoza is the wider aim, but the fortified towns bar the roads to it. Keep Lecera and Puebla de Hijar secure while the columns break through; a stalled offensive will draw no troops away from the north.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225, "support": [207, 208, 214]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226, "support": [206]}], "eqp-gce"],
["gce6.xml", "Batalla de Teruel", "Teruel — 15 December 1937<br><br>The northern Republican zone has fallen. Headquarters now seeks to regain the initiative by attacking the Nationalist salient at Teruel, forcing the enemy to answer our offensive instead of choosing the next battlefield himself.<br><br>Surround Teruel and take the town from Rey d'Harcourt's garrison. Keep Sarrion and the outer approaches secure against the relief forces. The winter roads make ammunition and food difficult to bring forward; the troops entering the city must not be cut off from their supplies.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225, "support": [207, 208, 209, 214]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226, "support": [206]}], "eqp-gce"],
["gce7.xml", "Ofensiva del Ebro", "Ebro offensive — 25 July 1938<br><br>The Nationalists have reached the Mediterranean and divided Republican territory. The Army of the Ebro is preparing a surprise crossing to recover the initiative and draw pressure away from the remaining Republican fronts.<br><br>Cross the Ebro, widen the bridgeheads and advance on Gandesa. Seize the intervening towns and hill positions while keeping the crossings covered. Surprise will help the first troops across, but the army following them needs bridges that survive the enemy's aircraft and counterattacks.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225, "support": [207, 208, 209, 214]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226}], "eqp-gce"],
["gce8.xml", "Contraofensiva del Ebro", "Ebro counteroffensive — 3 September 1938<br><br>Our advance has been stopped short of Gandesa, and Nationalist counterattacks are wearing down the bridgehead. German and Italian aircraft strike the roads and crossings. Headquarters is ordering a withdrawal before the army is trapped against the river.<br><br>Cover the retreat towards the eastern bank and secure the positions at Vinebre and Masroig. Keep the crossing approaches in our hands while the columns pull back. An early rush to safety would abandon the rearguard and turn an organised withdrawal into a rout.<br><br>Campaign note: finish within the Victory or Tactical Victory deadline to continue to the Segre. A Brilliant Victory ends this branch in defeat.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225, "support": [208, 209, 214]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226}], "eqp-gce"],
["gce9.xml", "Batalla del rio Segre", "Segre River — 6 November 1938<br><br>The Ebro battle has exhausted the army, and Catalonia is increasingly exposed. Headquarters is ordering a local offensive south of Lerida to improve the river line and threaten the enemy's communications.<br><br>Cross the Segre through Seros and Aytona and drive towards the enemy command position at Fraga. Protect Torres de Segre and the crossings behind the attack. The army needs a firmer river line and a threat to the Nationalist communications that will draw pressure away from our own.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225, "support": [208, 209, 214]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226}], "eqp-gce"],
["vgce0.xml", "Batalla del rio Segre", "Segre River — 6 November 1938 (alternate history)<br><br>Our success at the Ebro has kept the offensive alive. The enemy is trying to check the renewed advance along the Segre, south of Lerida.<br><br>Cross the Segre and take Fraga and the junctions beyond it. Keep Torres de Segre and the river approaches secure while the main body follows. The road towards Zaragoza will remain closed until we have broken this position and made the crossings safe for our guns.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225, "support": [208, 209, 214]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226}], "eqp-gce"],
["vgce1.xml", "Ataque a Zaragoza", "Zaragoza — 12 February 1939<br><br>Success at the Ebro and Segre has kept the Republic on the offensive. The French border has reopened and Soviet weapons have reached the army. Zaragoza is again within reach.<br><br>Advance through Osera, Fuentes de Ebro and Mediana and take Zaragoza. Italian CTV formations and troops of the Nationalist Thirteenth Division stand in the way; guerrillas behind their lines will assist the attack. Keep our southern bases secure while the army fights for this communications centre.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225, "support": [207, 208, 209, 214]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226}], "eqp-gce"],
["vgce4.xml", "Ceuta", "Ceuta and Tetuan — 5 August 1939<br><br>The Republic has won on the mainland, but Nationalist forces have withdrawn into the Spanish protectorate in Morocco. Ceuta and Tetuan are the last bases from which they can continue the war.<br><br>Land at Ceuta and take the port, then advance towards Tetuan. The fleet from Cartagena will support the landings, and detachments are already ashore. Legion troops and formations withdrawn from Spain defend the approaches. Open the port quickly so our artillery and reserves can follow the first wave.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225, "support": [208, 214]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226}], "eqp-gce"],
["Zhukov: Red God of War (1939-1945)"],
["ga4_0.xml", "Khalkin Gol", "Khalkhin Gol — 20 August 1939<br><br>Comrade, the border fighting has become a battle between the Soviet-Mongolian grouping and the Japanese Kwantung Army. Both sides have reinforced, and Zhukov is ready to use his armour to turn the Japanese flanks.<br><br>Take Nomonhan, its airfield and the neighbouring strongpoint while keeping our forward bases secure. The Japanese infantry can hold prepared positions even where its tanks are outmatched. Pin those positions while the mobile columns turn the flanks and close around the enemy grouping.", [{"id": 1, "country": 5, "support": [24]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89, "support": [304]}], "eqp-comww2"],
["ga4_1.xml", "Chisinau", "Chisinau — 28 June 1940 (fictional engagement)<br><br>Romania has accepted the Soviet ultimatum to evacuate Bessarabia and northern Bukovina. The withdrawal is under way, but the handover of roads, towns and railway equipment is confused, and armed forces are moving through the same narrow routes.<br><br>Occupy Chisinau and Manoilesti and secure the junctions on their approaches. Romanian columns are still on the roads as our troops move in. Keep your formations together through the handover; a blocked junction or an armed confrontation could bring the whole movement to a halt.", [{"id": 1, "country": 13}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2" ],
["ga4_2.xml", "Yelnya", "Yelnya — 30 August 1941<br><br>The Germans hold a salient around Yelnya, close enough to threaten another advance towards Moscow. Their infantry has dug into the villages and approaches, and the position has survived earlier Soviet attacks.<br><br>Drive the Germans out of Yelnya and the villages supporting the salient. Keep Pozhogino and Kostyuki secure as the attack closes from the flanks. Removing this forward position will shorten our line and deny the enemy a base for another advance towards Moscow.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2" ],
["ga4_3.xml", "Istra", "Istra — 6 December 1941<br><br>Comrade General, the German advance on Moscow has been stopped, but its forward troops still occupy the towns and roads north-west of the capital. The winter counteroffensive begins now, before those positions can be made permanent.<br><br>Clear Istra, Solnechnogorsk and the roads between them while keeping the capital's approaches covered. The German infantry is exhausted but can still defend the villages. Press the retreat before its rearguards have time to turn those villages into another continuous line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [303]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2"],
["ga4_4.xml", "Rzhev", "Rzhev breakout — 29 November 1942<br><br>The attacks of Operation Mars have driven Soviet mobile formations into the German defences around Rzhev, but some of the forward troops are now cut off. The immediate problem is to reopen the connection before the pocket is crushed.<br><br>Break the bottleneck at Bolshoye Kropotovo and hold the shoulders of the passage around Novoselovo and Gorskovo. The cut-off troops need a corridor that stays open after the assault passes through. Keep the roads covered against a German counterattack.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2" ],
["ga4_5.xml", "Operation Iskra", "Operation Iskra — 12 January 1943<br><br>Leningrad remains cut off by land. Between the city and the Volkhov Front lies a narrow German-held strip south of Lake Ladoga, fortified around settlements, woods and industrial sites.<br><br>Take Shlisselburg, Lipka and the workers' settlements between the two advancing fronts, then clear the approaches towards Nazija Airfield. The Eighteenth Army has fortified the narrow strip thoroughly. Open a land corridor into Leningrad and hold it wide enough for supplies to pass.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [303]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2"],
["ga4_6.xml", "Operation Kutuzov", "Operation Kutuzov — 15 July 1943<br><br>The German attack north of Kursk has stalled. Soviet forces have opened their counteroffensive against the Orel salient, and Rokossovsky's Central Front is joining the pressure from the south.<br><br>Advance beyond Ponyri towards Ponyri-Pervyje and Tagino. Break the prepared belt while our neighbouring armies press from the other sides of the salient. Ponyri must remain secure behind us as the guns and supply columns come forward.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2" ],
["ga4_7.xml", "Kamenets-Podolsk", "Kamenets-Podolsk — 21 March 1944<br><br>The First and Second Ukrainian Fronts are pressing into the German position in western Ukraine. Their advances threaten the roads by which the First Panzer Army can withdraw from the Kamenets-Podolsk area.<br><br>Take the towns and crossings through Dunayevtsy, Kamenets-Podolsk, Dracynci and Chernovtsy. Keep the Proskurov and Tsyhany approaches covered while the ring closes. The First Panzer Army still has mobile formations capable of forcing a passage through a thinly held road.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [4, 303]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2"],
["ga4_8.xml", "Bagration (Choice)", "Bagration: choose your front — 22 June 1944<br><br>The offensive against Army Group Centre is about to begin. Headquarters offers two assignments: support the First Belorussian Front on the southern approach, or join the Second Belorussian Front farther north.<br><br>Report to Staging Area 1 to join the First Belorussian Front at Bobruisk, or Staging Area 2 to join the Second Belorussian Front at Mogilev. Your next orders will follow the front you choose.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2" ],
["ga4_9.xml", "Bobruisk", "Bobruisk — 24 June 1944<br><br>The German Ninth Army is defending the southern shoulder of the Belorussian front. Bobruisk has been designated a fortress, and the roads through it offer a route west for troops threatened by our breakthrough.<br><br>Break through the positions around Telusha, Bortniki and Gorodets and take Bobruisk. Keep Mormal Airfield secure behind the attack. The Ninth Army must lose the roads through the fortress before its retreating columns can use them to escape towards Minsk.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2" ],
["ga4_10.xml", "Brest-Litovsk", "Brest-Litovsk — 18 July 1944<br><br>The collapse of the German front in Belorussia has opened the way west. The First Belorussian Front is extending its offensive on the southern flank, beyond the Pripet marshes.<br><br>Drive through Kobryn and Pruzany towards Brest-Litovsk and the western junctions. Secure Dzivin Airfield and keep Bereza covered behind the advance. German rearguards are fighting for the time their main columns need to withdraw; take the crossings before they can delay us there.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89, "support": [20]}], "eqp-comww2"],
["ga4_11.xml", "Praga", "Praga — 10 September 1944<br><br>The Germans still hold Praga on the eastern bank of the Vistula, across the river from Warsaw. Their bridgehead threatens our line and blocks an approach to the capital, where the uprising continues.<br><br>Clear Rembertow, Targowek and the Praga districts, with Goraszka secure behind you. Bring the attack through the built-up ground to the eastern bank of the Vistula. We need these approaches in our hands before the army can look beyond the river.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [303]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89, "support": [20]}], "eqp-comww2"],
["ga4_12.xml", "Mogilev", "Mogilev — 23 June 1944<br><br>Comrade Marshal, the Second Belorussian Front is attacking the German Fourth Army. Mogilev controls roads towards Minsk, and the defenders must be held here while the neighbouring fronts break through farther north and south.<br><br>Take Mogilev and Orsha, then secure the routes through Tolochin and its airfield. Gorki must remain open for the following formations. Seizing these junctions will leave the Fourth Army fewer roads on which to move reserves or withdraw towards Minsk.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2" ],
["ga4_13.xml", "Novogrudok", "Novogrudok — 5 July 1944<br><br>Minsk has fallen, and German formations east of the city are being cut off. The next task is to keep the retreat from settling into another front along the roads towards Grodno and Bialystok.<br><br>Drive through Novogrudok and Lida towards Grodno and Volkovysk. Keep Minsk and Pinsk secure as the pursuit stretches west. The mobile columns can reach the next junction quickly; the rifle formations must come up to hold it before another rearguard closes the road.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [4, 303]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2"],
["ga4_14.xml", "Osowiec", "Osowiec — 6 August 1944<br><br>The pursuit has brought the Second Belorussian Front to the approaches of the Osowiec fortress. Its crossings and nearby settlements stand across the next advance towards Lomza and East Prussia.<br><br>Take the fortress and the nearby positions at Goniadz, Monki, Kulesze and Zucielec, with Suchowola covering the rear. The restricted crossings favour the German defence. Bring up the guns and open the passage the army needs for the road west.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2" ],
["ga4_15.xml", "Stargard", "Stargard — 1 March 1945<br><br>The German counterattack from the Arnswalde sector has been checked, but enemy forces in Pomerania still threaten the northern flank of our advance on Berlin. The initiative must pass back to us.<br><br>Take Stargard and Arnswalde, keeping Neuwedell secure behind the attack. These junctions support the German positions in Pomerania. Clearing them will remove bases for another southward counterstroke and protect the flank of the advance towards the Baltic.", [{"id": 1, "country": 303, "support": [7]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2"],
["ga4_16.xml", "Seelow Heights", "Seelow Heights — 16 April 1945<br><br>The First Belorussian Front is to break through from the Oder and open the road to Berlin. Konev's First Ukrainian Front attacks farther south from the Neisse; Rokossovsky's Second Belorussian Front will cross the Oder later.<br><br>Break the Ninth Army's positions at Seelow and Muncheberg and open the routes towards Ahrensfelde and Spreenhagen. Clear the Frankfurt approaches and keep the Oder staging area secure. The northern flank still needs covering while Rokossovsky prepares his crossing.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [303]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89, "support": [20]}], "eqp-comww2"],
["Spartacus: The Slave Revolt (73-71 BC)"],
["spa0.xml", "AC 073 - Escape from gladiator school", "Escape from Capua — 73 BC<br><br>Spartacus, the school at Capua is behind you, but the roads ahead still belong to Rome. The fugitives have only the weapons they could seize in the escape. If the local guards gather before you reach open country, they can surround the whole band.<br><br>Get your people out towards Vesuvius. Keep them together until the pursuit is shaken off; shelter and new followers can be found once you are clear of the town.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa1.xml", "AC 073 - Liberation of surrounding land", "Gathering the fugitives — 73 BC<br><br>Freedom will not last without food and weapons. The estates around Capua hold both, and other enslaved people are looking for a chance to join you. Local guards still control the roads between them.<br><br>Take the settlements and supply points around the camp. Gather the new arrivals under Spartacus, Crixus and Oenomaus, and leave enough fighters with the supplies to protect them. Rome's response will be stronger than the men you escaped at the school.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa2.xml", "AC 073 - Battle at Vesuvius ", "Vesuvius — 73 BC<br><br>Glaber has blocked the approaches to Vesuvius. He expects hunger to bring you down from the mountain, and the Roman camp below is preparing for a siege.<br><br>Find a way through the cordon and strike the besiegers' positions. The mountain has sheltered the band; now it threatens to become a prison. Break the Roman force before more troops arrive to close the remaining paths.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa3.xml", "AC 073 - Conquest of Nola", "Nola — 73 BC<br><br>The band has grown beyond what its first refuges can feed. Nola offers stores, weapons and the prospect of new followers, but its garrison still holds the gates and approaches.<br><br>Gather the fighters and take the town before the Roman response catches up with you. Keep watch on the roads while the supplies are collected. We cannot afford to be shut inside the very place that is meant to sustain the march.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa4.xml", "AC 073 - Battle of Acerrae", "Acerrae: Furius — 73 BC<br><br>Varinius is bringing another Roman army against us, but his detachments are still separated. Furius has come within reach near Acerrae before the main body can support him.<br><br>Overrun his position while he stands alone. Keep watch on the roads from the Roman army; once their columns join, the chance to defeat them separately will be gone.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa5.xml", "AC 073 - Battle near Salinae Heraclae", "The camp of Cossinius — 73 BC<br><br>Cossinius has brought his detachment ahead of Varinius's main army. His camp near Herculaneum is exposed, and the men who might relieve it are still some distance away.<br><br>Strike the camp and secure its approaches before the Romans can regroup. The weapons and supplies will strengthen our own force, and Varinius will have one fewer column with which to close around us.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa6.xml", "AC 073 - Escape from the camp of slaves", "Escape from Varinius — 73 BC<br><br>Varinius has brought up his main army. Our camp is becoming a trap: each day behind its defences consumes food while the Roman lines grow stronger.<br><br>Open a passage and lead the band out through the cordon. Leave a rearguard between the Roman main body and the withdrawing columns until the slower groups are clear. If the passage cannot be opened at once, hold the camp together while another attempt is prepared.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa7.xml", "AC 073 - Conquest of Nuceria", "Nuceria — 73 BC<br><br>The band has escaped, but Varinius is still following. Nuceria lies ahead, with the stores we need and people who may join the rising.<br><br>Take the town and the positions controlling its approaches. Keep the pursuit away while the columns gather supplies and move through. We need to leave Nuceria stronger than we entered it, before the Romans can pin us against its walls.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa8.xml", "AC 073 - Destruction of Varinius at Picentia", "Picentia: turn on Varinius — 73 BC<br><br>Varinius will give us no peace. Every halt for food or recruits allows his army to close the distance, and the march cannot continue indefinitely with his troops at our backs.<br><br>Turn on the pursuit near Picentia. Seize its positions and break the Roman detachments before they can gather into a single line. Defeating this army would give the rising room to move beyond Campania.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa9.xml", "Spartacus or Krixos", "Spartacus or Crixus — 72 BC<br><br>The camp no longer agrees on where freedom lies. Spartacus's followers look towards a road out of Italy; Crixus's group intends to continue the struggle here. The two columns are preparing to separate.<br><br>Choose which leader to follow and move to his assembly point. Your force will march with that column in the battles ahead.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa10.xml", "AC 072 - Battle of Mons Garganos", "Mons Garganus: Crixus — 72 BC<br><br>Crixus, Rome has sent consular armies against the rising. Arrius's troops are ahead of Gellius's main force near Mount Garganus, and they threaten to pin your column while the rest of the Romans come up.<br><br>Attack their camp and take the surrounding positions before they can close around you. Spartacus is marching with his own followers; leave him with that column and fight this battle with yours.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa11.xml", "AC 072 - Battle against L. Gellius Poplicola", "Gellius: Crixus's continuation (alternate history) — 72 BC<br><br>Crixus, the victory over Arrius has bought time, but Gellius is bringing the main Roman army towards you. His columns threaten the roads through Siponto and Herdonia.<br><br>Take those positions and break the ring before it closes. Keep your own column together; Spartacus must remain with his separate force. The Romans expect the first victory to have left your men scattered over their spoils.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa12.xml", "AC 072 - Battle against Lentullus", "Lentulus blocks the road — 72 BC<br><br>Spartacus, Lentulus stands across the northern road, and another Roman army is approaching from behind. If the consuls unite, they can force you to fight on both fronts.<br><br>Break Lentulus's line at Cliternia and open the road for the main body. Keep a rearguard facing the pursuit until the column is through. Crixus commands a separate force and must not be brought into this march.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa13.xml", "AC 072 - revenge for Krixos", "Turn against Gellius — 72 BC<br><br>Lentulus has been driven back, but Gellius is still following from the south. News of Crixus's defeat has reached the camp. His column cannot come to our aid.<br><br>Turn on the pursuers and take their positions while holding Cliternia. Strike before Gellius can join the troops already beaten on the northern road. The surviving army needs room to continue its march.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa14.xml", "AC 072 - Battle at Gallia Cisalpina", "Cisalpine Gaul — 72 BC<br><br>The Alps are closer, but another Roman force stands across the route. Cassius holds the approaches through Mutina and Regium Lepidum, barring the way out of Cisalpine Gaul.<br><br>Break his line and take the towns and their approaches. Keep the column together until the passage is secure. The prospect of leaving Italy will count for little if the Romans can cut the march in two here.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa15.xml", "AC 072 - Battle at Firmum Picenum", "Firmum Picenum — 72 BC<br><br>The army is marching south again. Roman forces are gathering across the roads of Picenum, and every delay gives them time to bring another column against us.<br><br>Take Firmum Picenum, Ancona and Auximum, and secure the positions linking them. The army needs these roads and stores to sustain its march. Keep the passage open while the main body moves through.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa16.xml", "AC 071 - break the siege", "Break Crassus's cordon — 71 BC<br><br>The pirates have taken their payment without bringing the ships. Sicily is beyond our reach, supplies are running down, and Crassus's fortifications seal the land route out of southern Italy.<br><br>Force a passage through the Roman cordon and bring the army out. Hold the breach while the slower columns pass, then pull the rearguard through. No fleet is coming; we must open our own road north.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa17.xml", "AC 071 - Attack on the camp of the Celts", "Relieve the separated camp — 71 BC<br><br>Castus and Gannicus have separated from the main army. Crassus is moving against their camp, hoping to destroy them before Spartacus can intervene.<br><br>March to their relief and secure the positions around Metapontum, Heraclea and Grumentum. Hold the roads between the two forces so the Romans cannot isolate them again. The separated troops need a way back to the army, not another column trapped beside them.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310, "support": [308]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag"],
["spa18.xml", "AC 071 - Battle of Paestum", "The final battle — 71 BC<br><br>Crassus blocks the road ahead near Paestum. Repeated battles and separations have thinned the army, and Pompey is returning to Italy with another Roman force. The space in which we can march is closing.<br><br>Take Paestum and break the positions around it. Bring the surviving groups into one attack before the Romans can hold us here for the next army to arrive. This is the road we have left.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["Viet Cong (1964-1975)"],
["nvc00.xml", "Raid at Binh Gia", "Binh Gia and the coastal approaches — 28 December 1964<br><br>Fighting around Binh Gia is drawing South Vietnamese troops into the countryside east of Saigon. Before they can concentrate, our coastal detachments have a chance to strike the positions at Long Hai and Vung Tau.<br><br>Take those bases and break the defensive network around them. Local forces know the approach routes, but government reserves can return along the roads behind us. Make the enemy answer our attack without leaving the detachments cut off on the coast.", [{"id": 0, "country": 276}], [{"id": 1, "country": 253}], "eqp-olgcw" ],
["nvc01.xml", "Escape from Vung Tau", "Escape from Vung Tau — 29 December 1964<br><br>The raid on the coast has brought a response. South Vietnamese troops are moving to seal the roads around Vung Tau, and our detachments must reach the jungle routes before the cordon closes.<br><br>Lead the withdrawal through the designated exits, with a rearguard covering the slowest groups. If the roads are blocked, hold the remaining bases together until the pressure eases. Do not let the fighting around the crash site draw the force away from its route out.", [{"id": 0, "country": 276, "support": [246]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 253}], "eqp-olgcw"],
["nvc02.xml", "Attack on the Plei Me Camp", "Plei Me — 19 October 1965<br><br>The camp at Plei Me watches the routes through the Central Highlands. Its locally recruited garrison and American advisers can call on aircraft and relief troops from the Pleiku area.<br><br>Attack the camp while a blocking force secures the northern road. Hold the positions you take against the relief column. The operation will fail if the two attacking groups are separated and the road to the garrison remains open.", [{"id": 0, "country": 276, "support": [246]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 253, "support": [9]}], "eqp-olgcw"],
["nvc03.xml", "Ia Drang", "Ia Drang — 14 November 1965<br><br>American helicopter-borne troops are establishing landing zones near our routes through the Central Highlands. Their aircraft can bring reinforcements beyond a conventional front line, but the men on the ground still need clearings they can hold.<br><br>Drive them from X-Ray, Albany and the surrounding positions. Local detachments will support the attack. Use the jungle to approach the clearings; American artillery and aircraft can strike any assault group left in the open.", [{"id": 0, "country": 276, "support": [246]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [253]}], "eqp-olgcw"],
["nvc04.xml", "Military Region IV Crisis", "Cu Chi: preserve the local force — 4 January 1966<br><br>An enemy clearing operation is closing on Cu Chi. The local detachments know the villages and supply routes on which our work here depends. We need those people alive when the enemy columns have passed.<br><br>Cover their withdrawal towards War Zone C. Send the local groups ahead and use the stronger formations to hold the routes behind them. A defensible base can give us time, but do not let the defence of it trap the force we are trying to save.", [{"id": 0, "country": 276, "support": [246]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [0, 3]}], "eqp-olgcw"],
["nvc05.xml", "Asian Clash", "Tuy Hoa — 18 July 1967<br><br>South Korean troops are preparing to clear our positions around Tuy Hoa. The bases here give our local forces access to the coastal districts; losing them would leave those detachments without a secure route inland.<br><br>Hold the bases and draw exposed troops back into positions they can defend together. PAVN formations are available to strengthen the line. Keep the roads between the defenders open as the enemy advances.", [{"id": 0, "country": 246, "support": [276]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 18, "support": [253]}], "eqp-olgcw"],
["nvc05b.xml", "Strike on Kontum", "Kontum outposts — 3 November 1967<br><br>Government outposts around Dak Pek, Dak Seang, Dak To and Kontum overlook the routes between our border bases and the interior. An enemy offensive is expected, and these camps would give it places to assemble and resupply.<br><br>Take the outposts and hold them. Cover the relief routes while the assault groups close on each camp; otherwise fresh troops can arrive as quickly as we drive the garrison back.", [{"id": 0, "country": 246}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [253]}], "eqp-olgcw"],
["nvc06.xml", "Attack on Khe Sanh", "Khe Sanh — 15 January 1968<br><br>The American base at Khe Sanh watches Route 9 near the Laotian border. Its airstrip and hill positions overlook the approaches to our supply network, and aircraft can sustain the garrison even if the ground routes are cut.<br><br>Take the surrounding hills, Lang Vei and the combat base with its airstrip. Reinforcements are coming to support the attack. Bring the guns into position before exposing the assault troops: the defenders' artillery can still reach well beyond their perimeter.", [{"id": 0, "country": 246}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [253]}], "eqp-olgcw"],
["nvc07.xml", "Tet Offensive", "Tet offensive: Hue and Da Nang — 31 January 1968<br><br>The Tet offensive is bringing the war into the cities. Our attacking groups have a brief chance to disrupt the South Vietnamese command before government and American reserves can respond.<br><br>Strike Hue and the Da Nang area. At Hue, the ARVN First Division headquarters and the American advisory compound are important centres of resistance. The rocket batteries will support the assaults; once inside the cities, hold the captured positions against the counterattack.", [{"id": 0, "country": 246, "support": [276]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [253]}], "eqp-olgcw"],
["nvc08.xml", "Laos Counteroffensive", "Laos counteroffensive — 12 February 1971<br><br>South Vietnamese forces have entered Laos along Route 9 with American air support. Their landing sites and firebases threaten the supply routes that connect our northern bases with the fighting in the south.<br><br>Drive them from the Xe Pon valley and recover Tchepone and Route 9. Take the isolated bases before helicopters can reinforce them or lift the defenders out. Our heavier weapons give the assault groups more support, but aircraft still make the open approaches dangerous.", [{"id": 0, "country": 246}], [{"id": 1, "country": 253, "support": [9]}], "eqp-olgcw"],
["nvc09.xml", "Battle of Kontum", "Kontum — 15 May 1972<br><br>The offensive has returned to the Central Highlands. South Vietnamese forces hold Kontum behind a chain of firebases, with American advisers and aircraft supporting the defence.<br><br>Break the outer positions and take the city. Regional units will join the advance, and our anti-aircraft weapons can cover parts of the approach. The defenders will try to hold the assault groups under air attack before they reach the streets.", [{"id": 0, "country": 246, "support": [276]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 253, "support": [9]}], "eqp-olgcw"],
["nvc10.xml", "Liberation of Saigon", "Saigon — 24 April 1975<br><br>The South Vietnamese armies have lost the northern provinces and the Central Highlands. Surviving formations are falling back towards Saigon, where the government is trying to put together another defence.<br><br>Take Bien Hoa and the capital's command and communications centres, then clear the routes towards the coast. The converging columns must reach the city before the defenders can organise a new line. A slow advance will give them time we cannot afford.<br><br>Campaign note: a Tactical Victory ends the campaign unsuccessfully; meet a higher victory deadline.", [{"id": 0, "country": 246}], [{"id": 1, "country": 253, "support": [9]}], "eqp-olgcw"],
["Soviet Black Sea Fleet (1941-1944)"],
["rcampfa1.xml", "Falciu 1", "Falciu — 22 June 1941<br><br>Germany has attacked along the frontier, and Romania has joined the war. Here in Bessarabia, the 150th Rifle Division faces the Prut while the Romanian forces prepare their own advance.<br><br>Form your command from the troops available for requisition, cross at Falciu and take the bridge. Establish a bridgehead from which we can meet the expected offensive. Reinforcements will be sent when they can be spared.", [{"id": 1, "country": 13}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp" ],
["rcampfa2.xml", "Falciu 2", "01. FALCIU 2 (7 July 1941)<br><br>The Romanian offensive is gathering across the Prut. Our bridgehead at Falciu threatens its flank, and the enemy is preparing to clear us from the far bank before advancing into Bessarabia.<br><br>Hold the bridgehead and its crossing. Reinforcements will be sent if they can be spared, but the first attacks will fall on the troops already here. Keep the supply passage open while the forward positions absorb the blow.", [{"id": 1, "country": 13}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp" ],
["rcampki1.xml", "Kishenev", "02. KISHENEV (14 July 1941)<br><br>The German breakthrough north of us has made the Prut position untenable. Your troops have held the Romanians, but remaining here would leave the division cut off from the road east.<br><br>Withdraw through Kishenev towards Odessa. Kishenev controls the last road out of Bessarabia still in our hands; secure it before the pursuing columns reach the junction. Keep the division together through the retreat.", [{"id": 1, "country": 13, "support": [7]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampode.xml", "Odessa 1941", "Odessa — 13 August 1941<br><br>Romanian forces have reached Odessa while the German advance has cut our land routes east. The port is still supplied by the Black Sea Fleet, but everything the garrison needs must now come by sea from the Crimea.<br><br>Hold the approaches and keep your formations alive while the fleet sustains the defence. Fall back into stronger positions when necessary, with the guns covering the movement. Headquarters needs time and an army that can be brought out when the order comes.<br><br>Campaign note: survive the full 20 turns. The scripted defeat then continues the campaign; there is no winning grade here.", [{"id": 1, "country": 13, "support": [7]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampper.xml", "Perekop", "04. PEREKOP (25 September 1941)<br><br>Odessa is still holding, but German forces have reached the narrow entrance to the Crimea. Their attack has nearly carried the Perekop isthmus, and reserves can follow through any gap left open there.<br><br>Counterattack and recover the Perekop positions before the enemy can widen the passage. The roads beyond lead into the peninsula and towards Sevastopol. Stop the advance while its strength is still confined to this narrow front.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp" ],
["rcampro1.xml", "Rostov 1941", "05. ROSTOV 1941 (25 November 1941)<br><br>Rostov has fallen to German mobile formations. The city is the gateway to the Caucasus, but the speed of the enemy advance has left a salient projecting into our line. Winter has reached the steppe, and headquarters has ordered a counterattack.<br><br>Retake Rostov and threaten the roads behind its garrison. Force the German armour to defend the city while our neighbouring formations press its flanks. The crossing must be back in our hands before the enemy can use it to carry the offensive south.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [37]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampker.xml", "Kerch", "06. KERCH (26 December 1941)<br><br>Sevastopol is still holding, but the rest of the Crimea is in German and Romanian hands. A landing at the eastern end of the peninsula will threaten the rear of the forces attacking the fortress.<br><br>Bring your troops across from Taman and land around Kerch. Take the town and join the separate landing groups before the coastal defenders can gather for a counterattack. The army needs a foothold large enough to receive the guns and supplies coming behind you.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp" ],
["rcampfeo.xml", "Feodosiya", "07. FEODOSIYA (29 December 1941)<br><br>The landing at Kerch is one part of our attempt to draw pressure away from Sevastopol. Your force will come ashore farther west, at Feodosiya, threatening the connection between the Kerch peninsula and the rest of the Crimea.<br><br>Take Feodosiya and secure the landing approaches. The German coastal troops are spread out, but they can concentrate quickly once our direction is clear. Open the port and bring the landing groups together before that response arrives.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [13]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampcho.xml", "Crimea Choice", "The Crimean landings — 15 December 1941<br><br>Sevastopol is under pressure. Landings in the eastern Crimea will threaten the enemy's rear and draw forces away from the siege. Your command can join the attack at Kerch or the landing farther west at Feodosiya.<br><br>Take the first selection position for Kerch, or the second for Feodosiya. The army's subsequent orders will bring both routes back into the same campaign.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp" ],
["rcampsev.xml", "Sevastopol 1942", "Sevastopol — 6 June 1942<br><br>The next assault on Sevastopol is beginning. Months of bombardment and repeated attacks have worn down the garrison, and supplies are increasingly difficult to bring across the Black Sea. The fleet is carrying your troops in to reinforce the defence.<br><br>Hold for fifteen days while headquarters decides the next step. Keep the approaches covered, shorten exposed parts of the line when necessary and preserve the formations that can still fight. We have few replacements to send into the fortress.<br><br>Campaign note: survive the full 15 turns. The scripted defeat then continues the campaign; there is no winning grade here.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [13]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampno1.xml", "Novorossiysk 1", "10. NOVOROSSIYSK 1 (20 September 1942)<br><br>The German summer offensive has reached the Caucasus. Rostov and the Maikop oilfields are lost, and the enemy has entered Novorossiysk. The coastal road beyond it leads towards the ports still supplying our forces along the Black Sea.<br><br>Stop the southward advance and recover the hill positions covering the road. We cannot yet retake the whole port. Hold the line that prevents the enemy from carrying its success farther down the coast.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [13, 61]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampsuc.xml", "Suchumi", "11. SUCHUMI (28 September 1942)<br><br>The coastal advance has been checked, but German mountain troops are coming through the Caucasus towards Suchumi. They threaten to reach the Black Sea behind the front and cut its only coastal supply road.<br><br>Hold the port and the positions covering the mountain approaches. Keep the coastal road open to the troops near Novorossiysk. The enemy must be stopped as he emerges from the passes, before his columns can spread along the shore.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp" ],
["rcampor1.xml", "Ordzhonikidze 1", "12. ORDZHONIKIDZE 1 (1 November 1942)<br><br>The First Panzer Army is advancing across the Terek towards the routes serving Grozny and Baku. After a heavy bombardment, its troops are closing on Ordzhonikidze, a junction we cannot afford to lose.<br><br>Bring one group into the town from the eastern assembly area while the force to the north strikes the German flank. The garrison must hold while that counterattack develops. Snow complicates supply off the roads; keep the ammunition columns within reach of the guns.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp" ],
["rcampor2.xml", "Ordzhonikidze 2", "13. ORDZHONIKIDZE 2 (8 November 1942)<br><br>Ordzhonikidze has held, and the attack on the German flank has cut the supply route behind their forward troops. Enemy reinforcements are now coming to reopen it, while the trapped formations prepare to break out.<br><br>Keep the two forces apart, defeat the encircled group and carry the advance west. Hold the road junctions against the relief attack. The town will be threatened again if the Germans restore their connection before we clear the pocket.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp" ],
["rcampmai.xml", "Maikop", "14. MAIKOP (10 January 1943)<br><br>The encirclement at Stalingrad has changed the position in the Caucasus. German forces are withdrawing, with roads west towards Novorossiysk and Taman and another route north-west through Rostov.<br><br>Retake Maikop and its oilfields, then advance to the Kuban. Threaten the western roads so the retreating columns must turn towards the forces approaching from the Don. The provisional airstrip can service aircraft already here, but cannot receive newly deployed squadrons.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp" ],
["rcampro2.xml", "Rostov 1943", "15. ROSTOV 1943 (2 February 1943)<br><br>We are back at the approaches to Rostov. German columns are still coming out of the Caucasus, and the Don crossings offer their mobile formations a route into Ukraine.<br><br>Take Rostov before those columns get across. Close the road from the south while the leading troops secure the river approaches. Every day the crossing remains open allows more of the enemy army to escape the trap.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp" ],
["rcampno2.xml", "Novorossiysk 2", "16. NOVOROSSIYSK 2 (18 March 1943)<br><br>The enemy still holds the Kuban bridgehead, with a short passage across the strait to the Crimea. Novorossiysk anchors its southern flank and keeps an important Black Sea port out of our hands.<br><br>Land with the naval infantry south of the city and join the force attacking along the coast. Cruisers and destroyers will support the landing. Unite the two attacks before the defenders can contain the beachhead and turn back to the coastal front.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [13]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampkry.xml", "Krymskaya", "17. KRYMSKAYA (18 April 1943)<br><br>The Kuban defences have resisted a month of attacks. German and Romanian troops still hold Novorossiysk and the approaches to Krymskaya; now they are counterattacking our southern bridgehead.<br><br>Strike at Krymskaya to draw reserves away from that threatened foothold and break the centre of the enemy line. More of our forces are being committed, but the Germans also have reserves close enough to answer a breakthrough. Keep the attack moving beyond the first positions.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [13]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampno3.xml", "Novocross", "18. NOVOROSSIYSK 3 (9 September 1943)<br><br>Preparations for the offensive against the Kuban bridgehead are complete. The troops on the coast and in our foothold south of Novorossiysk will attack together, with naval infantry from the Black Sea Fleet joining the assault.<br><br>Take Novorossiysk and open the roads beyond it. Coordinate the attacks so the garrison cannot turn its whole strength against either one. The months spent holding the southern foothold must now give the army a passage through the enemy's coastal defences.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [13, 61]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcamptam.xml", "Taman", "19. TAMAN (25 September 1943)<br><br>Novorossiysk has fallen, and the retreating enemy is moving towards Taman. Across the strait lies the Crimea, where troops evacuated from this bridgehead can form another defensive line.<br><br>Drive west through the remaining positions and clear the peninsula. Our formations are tired, but the rearguards are fighting to buy passage for the columns behind them. Reach the evacuation approaches before those columns are safely across.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [13]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampod2.xml", "Odessa 1944", "20. ODESSA 1944 (9 April 1944)<br><br>The winter offensive has carried our armies beyond the Dnieper. As another attack approaches the Crimea through Perekop, your force is to move along the coast towards Odessa.<br><br>Take the port and carry the advance west towards the Romanian frontier. It is not yet clear how long the enemy intends to defend the city. Expect experienced rearguards at the crossings and roads his retreat depends on.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [13]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampse2.xml", "Sevastopol 1944", "21. SEVASTOPOL 1944 (7 May 1944)<br><br>The German and Romanian troops driven back through the Crimea have gathered at Sevastopol. The fortress we once defended is now the last major base from which they can hold the peninsula or evacuate it.<br><br>Take the city before the garrison can get away by sea. The march has stretched our supplies, and some of the infantry is still coming forward. Keep the roads clear for those formations while the leading troops force the outer defences.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [13]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampjas.xml", "Jassy", "22. JASSY (15 June 1944)<br><br>Our bridgehead across the Prut near Jassy gives the army a starting point for the next offensive into Romania. German and Romanian forces are gathering to destroy it while its garrison is short of men and supplies.<br><br>Hold the far bank. You may shorten the perimeter where necessary, but keep a connected position and the crossings supplying it. Watch for German armour massing against a narrow part of the line.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [13]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampfa3.xml", "Falciu 3", "23. FALCIU 3 (22 August 1944)<br><br>The offensive has broken through from the Prut bridgeheads. Enemy formations are withdrawing between our advancing groups, and a junction near Falciu could close their route out.<br><br>Drive south along the western bank to meet the forces crossing from the Kishenev direction. Take Falciu and secure the crossings between the two columns. We fought to hold a bridge here in 1941; now the enemy needs it to get away.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [13]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampbuc.xml", "Bucharest", "24. BUCHAREST (30 August 1944)<br><br>Romania has changed sides, and Romanian formations are now fighting the Germans. German troops are withdrawing through the countryside while others try to hold positions around Bucharest. Your force is closest to the capital.<br><br>Enter Bucharest with the Romanian troops supporting you and clear the remaining enemy positions. Watch for German reinforcements arriving by air. Do not cross the Danube into Bulgaria; headquarters has given no authority for an operation there.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [8, 13]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61, "support": [13]}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcamprus.xml", "Ruse", "25. RUSE (8 September 1944)<br><br>War has been declared on Bulgaria, and our force is to cross the Danube. The Bulgarian army has been ordered not to resist, but some troops may not have received those orders and German forces remain in the country.<br><br>Secure the crossings at Ruse and Turlukai and move onto the inland junctions. Establish contact before opening fire where troops offer no resistance. Keep the columns ready to deal with armed opposition without turning every uncertain encounter into a battle.", [{"id": 1, "country": 8}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp" ],
["rcampsof.xml", "Sofia", "26. SOFIA (12 September 1944)<br><br>Our advance has met little resistance, but armed forces loyal to the old government are reported on the approaches to Sofia. Partisan groups in the area can help us reach the capital and secure it.<br><br>Take Sofia and the positions covering its roads. Keep contact with the local forces as the columns advance; the situation is changing quickly, and reports about the strength and intentions of the remaining garrisons are incomplete.", [{"id": 1, "country": 8}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61, "support": [8]}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["Red Star Over China (1927-1949)"],
["mao1.xml", "Nanchang Uprising", "Nanchang uprising — 1 August 1927<br><br>Comrades, our alliance with the Kuomintang has broken. Other units are joining the rising here at Nanchang, but the local government troops still hold the city and surround our positions on the Gan.<br><br>Strike the old city as the supporting columns come in from the other approaches. Take the junctions between our groups before the garrison can defeat them separately. The rising needs control of Nanchang if it is to survive its first day.", [{"id": 1, "country": 15}], [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], "eqp-olgww2" ],
["mao2.xml", "Autumn Harvest Uprising", "Autumn Harvest uprising — 7 September 1927<br><br>Another rising is being organised in Hunan and Jiangxi after the fighting at Nanchang. Changsha is its intended centre, but the groups marching towards it are unevenly trained and armed.<br><br>Join the gathering forces and take the positions covering their approach. Bring the columns together before committing them against the city. The local Kuomintang troops need only catch them separately to stop the rising before it can establish a base.", [{"id": 1, "country": 15}], [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], "eqp-olgww2" ],
["mao3.xml", "Jiangxi Soviet", "The encirclement closes — November 1930<br><br>Kuomintang columns are entering the Communist base areas in Jiangxi. They are stronger along the roads and in the towns, but their forces are still separated by country our detachments know well.<br><br>Hold the bases and break up the columns before they can close a continuous ring. Use the wooded approaches to gather against an exposed group, then move before its neighbours arrive. Both the field force and the villages supporting it must survive the offensive.", [{"id": 1, "country": 15}], [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], "eqp-olgww2" ],
["mao4.xml", "Long March - Luding Bridge", "Luding Bridge — 29 May 1935<br><br>The march has reached the Dadu River. The pursuers are closing from behind, and the army cannot remain crowded against the water while supplies run down.<br><br>Take Luding Bridge and secure the approaches on the far bank. Liu Wenhui's local forces hold the crossing; even a small garrison can delay an army on this narrow route. Keep the passage open for the columns following the assault group.", [{"id": 1, "country": 15}], [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], "eqp-olgww2" ],
["mao5.xml", "Pingxingguan Pass", "Pingxingguan Pass — 25 September 1937<br><br>The Japanese invasion has brought us into an uneasy alliance with the Kuomintang. Our troops are to strike the enemy's rear while other Chinese forces engage the main advance.<br><br>The Japanese Fifth Division is moving towards Pingxingguan Pass. Block its route and attack the columns caught on the road. Use the country around the pass to approach without exposing the detachments early; the enemy's strength is harder to bring to bear on a narrow, obstructed road.", [{"id": 1, "country": 5}], [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], "eqp-olgww2" ],
["mao5_2.xml", "100 Regiments Offensive", "100 Regiments Offensive<br><br>1-11-1940, Shanzi, North-Central China<br><br>Again, the central committee of the ChCP has agreed to launch another guerrilla assault on the Japanese rearguard in co-operation with our Kuomingtan ''allies''.  Comrade Mao dislikes this attack, but China is calling for Chinese action against the invaders, and that's what we are going to carry out.  The main objectives must be the capture of enemy resources present in your area: the coal mines and factories.  Your battle plan includes some cities and don't forget to cut all enemy lines of communication.<br><br>Act as quick as possible, the Japanese are going to use all available means to defeat any try to stop their penetration into China.<br><br>Fu qi!", [{"id": 1, "country": 5}], [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], "eqp-olgww2" ],
["mao6.xml", "Central Plains Breakout", "Central Plains breakout — June 1946<br><br>The negotiations have not settled the conflict with the Kuomintang. Its troops are gathering around our Central Plains positions, and the routes west from the Wuhan area are threatened.<br><br>Bring the force out towards our comrades in central China before the encirclement closes. The new equipment will be of little use if it is left inside a pocket. Keep the slower columns moving under cover of the rearguard.", [{"id": 1, "country": 15}], [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], "eqp-olgww2" ],
["mao7.xml", "Linjiang Campaign", "Linjiang — 8 March 1947<br><br>Manchuria's factories and railways are essential to our army. Our formations have advanced towards Jilin, Changchun and Siping, but Kuomintang troops still threaten the base at Linjiang and the railway supplying it.<br><br>Hold Linjiang and keep the Beijing-Changchun line open while the forward groups press towards Changchun and Jilin. The enemy must not be allowed to cut the supply route behind an otherwise successful advance.", [{"id": 1, "country": 15}], [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], "eqp-olgww2" ],
["mao8.xml", "Summer Offensive 1947", "Summer Offensive 1947<br><br>16-5-47, Jilin Province, NE China.<br><br>Orders from the central ChCP comitte: it's time to capture Changchun, Siping, and Jilin to complete the conquest of Manchuria. The success on this offensive is extremely important, because it would allow us to undertake further penetrations on to Beijing and Nanjing in the next months.<br><br>It won't be easy, the nationalists still have good units with good equipment, but we count on your elite units to deal with the Kuomingtan troops. The planned Summer Offensive must be victorious.", [{"id": 1, "country": 15}], [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], "eqp-olgww2" ],
["mao9.xml", "Winter Offensive 1947", "Winter Offensive<br><br>1-12-1947 Liaoning Province, NE China.<br><br>The KMT troops are badly wounded.  Our victories at Changchun and Siping have decimated their men, commander, and you must put an end to the nationalist resistance in Manchuria.  Your mission is to secure the communications between our base at Siping and our groups in the South, near to Shenyang.  Then you must take Shenyang.  It is the historical Manchurian capital and is both an important industrial and political center.  The capture of Shenyang will open the way to Beijing and Nanjing.<br><br>I don't think the snow and the bad weather conditions of the Manchurian Winter will be a major problem for you.", [{"id": 1, "country": 15}], [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], "eqp-olgww2" ],
["mao11.xml", "Pyongyang Liberation [Korean War]", "Towards Pyongyang — 25 November 1950<br><br>The North Korean army's retreat has brought United Nations forces close to China's frontier. Our troops are now committed to pushing them back, alongside the North Korean formations still in the field.<br><br>Break the opposing positions on the Chongchon and advance towards Pyongyang. Reopening the capital and its communications would give our allies a base from which to rebuild. The enemy has powerful air support; keep the supply columns covered as the front moves south.", [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [18]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 233}], "eqp-olgww2"],
["mao12.xml", "Chosin Reservoir [Korean War]", "Chosin Reservoir [Korean War]<br><br>27-11-1950 Chosin Reservoir, N of North Korea.<br><br>Your quick advance has created a salient in the enemy lines, like the one at the Chosin Reservoir.  This sector is protected by a North American division.  Your task is to make a surprise attack from two different directions and destroy the entire enemy division.  Be careful, our spies report that it's a crack division and they have air support from an improvised airstrip near the reservoir.  Air reinforcements are on the way.", [{"id": 1, "country": 9}], [{"id": 0, "country": 233}], "eqp-olgww2" ],
["mao13.xml", "Hungnam Pocket [Korean War]", "Hungnam Pocket [Korean War]<br><br>11-12-1950, Hungnam, North Korea.<br><br>Again, your smashing attack has left the enemy forces on the ground isolated.  This is the situation at Hungnam.  The UN forces are surrounded from the North and South by us while the North Korean units will attack from the East.  However, the Hungnam port continues to be their main lifeline, supported by their overwhelming naval power.<br><br>Your mission is to reach the port of Hungnam while destroying all enemy forces along your way.  You must stop any UN evacuation as soon as possible.  A successful evacuation will be a victory for them.  The 2nd, 6th and 10th North Korean divisions (the 2nd Korean People's Army) will be under your direct command and the 20th PLA will arrive from the South as reinforcements.", [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [18, 22]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 233, "support": [25]}], "eqp-olgww2"],
["mao13_2.xml", "UN Counterattack [Korean War]", "Seoul: UN Counterattack<br><br>Seoul, beyond the 38th Paralell, near the pre-war dividing line.<br><br>25-1-1951<br><br>The lightning advances of December and early January provide us with the opportunity to easily retake Seoul for the North Koreans.  However, the situation is becoming dangerous.  Our supply lines to China are long and are constantly being bombed and strafed by the UN air force.  Because of this they are preparing a counterattack to again liberate Seoul.  Our Korean spies have told us that a great number of troops are concentrating South of Suwon, including modern tanks and heavy artillery.<br><br>Be careful, our troops are nearly exhausted due to the quick advances in the past months. Your mission is to protect Seoul at all costs and if possible defeat the capitalist advance.", [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [18]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 233, "support": [25]}], "eqp-olgww2"],
["mao14.xml", "Spring Offensive [Korean War]", "Spring Offensive [Korean War]<br><br>22-4-1951 Seoul, near the 38th Paralell.<br><br>It's time to go back to Seoul.  We have deployed a large number of PLA and KPA units Northwards toward Seoul and with your armies nothing will stop us in our drive.  The South Korean capital must be in our hands again.<br><br>The UN forces have massed their units to protect their silly so-called ''No-Named line''.  Anyway, this situation fits perfectly with our People's War doctrine.  Launch your armies and over run the dirty capitalist's invaders on your way to recapture Seoul.", [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [18, 22, 73]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 233, "support": [25]}], "eqp-olgww2"],
["mao14_2.xml", "Pusan Revisited [Korean War]", "Pusan Revisited (alternate history)<br><br>27-6-1951 Pusan, South Korea<br><br>Just like last year, the UN forces are again encircled on the ''Pusan Perimeter''.  Now, with the bulk of the North Korean forces are guarding the rear, we can assault the enemy positions without the fear of an assault on our back like last years landings at Inch'on.<br><br>You have one mission; destroy the remnants of the capitalist forces.  Otherwise, they will receive more reinforcements and support from their stronghold at Pusan.  Quick drive them into the sea and Korea will become the unified Korean People's Republic.", [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [3, 18, 22]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 233, "support": [25]}], "eqp-olgww2"],
["mao15.xml", "Taiwan Strait - Nuclear Crisis", "Taiwan Strait - Nuclear Crisis<br><br>1-9-1953, Sea of China.<br><br>I hope you had enough rest from your participation on the Korean War.  As one of the heroes of the PRC the High Command of the PLA has a new mission for you.  The new North American government has retired the fleet that was guarding the Taiwan Strait.  This is the opportunity we have been waiting for; the assault on the rebel province of Taiwan.  You must end the existence of the KMT and its leader, Chiang-Kai-Shek.<br><br>Embark your units in Tianjing and reach the Taiwanese coast as soon as possible.  Beijing is sure the UN will take part in operations like in Korea, this time supporting the KMT in Taiwan.  Your highest priority is the conquest of Taipei.  With this city we will complete the unification of all the Chinese territories.", [{"id": 1, "country": 15, "support": [9]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 233}], "eqp-olgww2"],
["mao16.xml", "Sino - Soviet Incident", "Sino - Soviet Incident<br><br>1-10-1955, Amur river, Sino-Soviet border, near Khabarovsk, Far Eastern Siberia.<br><br>A chain of unfortunate incidents with the Soviets along the Chinese - Soviet border has opened the way for the outbreak of full scale military operations.  As you know, the relationship with our former Soviet allies has badly deteriorated.  Moscow doesn't like our own interpretation of Marxism and wants to take us back to the ''correct'' communist system.  To punish us, they have launched an invasion across the Amur River, the natural border between the PRC and the USSR.  They have captured a many square kilometers of Chinese territory, including some villages.<br><br>You are the commander of the best units in the whole PLA, and your mission is to counter-strike the Soviet invaders.  If we want to continue with our own interpretation of the Marxism, we must defeat the Soviets.  Also Mao would be most pleased, if your men capture the important city of Khabarovsk.  He says that these territories are historically Chinese and no soviets must remain on Chinese lands! <br><br>Fu qi!", [{"id": 1, "country": 89}], [{"id": 0, "country": 233}], "eqp-olgww2" ],
["mao17.xml", "Great Leap Forward", "Great Leap Forward<br><br>1-12-1955, Beijing.<br><br>Private Tovarich!  Nice to see you again.  It has been a while since our last meeting at Khabarovsk.  It was a shame to lose the battle against you, but now we can re-negotiate the conditions of the peace treaty.  This is Top Secret and I hope you have told no one of our plans.  As our men from the KGB have told you, we are ready to support you, if you finally decide to undertake a coup against Mao Zedong and his reformed communism.  It is literally destroying China.  We need to take China back to the right and true communist way.  We think you and your so-called ''Gang of Four'' are the perfect team to take down the Maoist system and that destructive plan named ''Great Leap Forward''.  That woman of your gang, ''Madame Mao'' can be very useful in the near future, when you will need to destroy the political image of Mao.<br><br>This is the plan we suggest; in the past month the units under your direct management have been deployed on the coast of the Sea of China in preparation for the Coup.   We are ready to support you by sea.  The Chinese navy will remain loyal to Mao, but it is not powerful enough to deal with a minor Soviet submarine unit.  After we secure the entire coast by taking Tanggu, you must launch the counterattack against the government loyalist units which surely will be sent to defeat our plans.  Take the Tanggu airfield as soon as possible as this will allow us to send you reinforcements by air.  Our planes will be painted with the PRC symbols.  You must avoid the Americans as we don't need any problems with them now.  The incident should be only between Chinese forces.<br><br>The last stand will be Beijing, this won't be easy, as you know, the best PLA units are deployed there.  The price maybe high, but it deserves a try.  You can become the new premier of the People's Republic of China!<br><br>Udachi tovarich!", [{"id": 1, "country": 233}], [{"id": 0, "country": 233, "support": [89]}], "eqp-olgww2"],
["The Great Patriotic War USSR Campaign (1942-1945)"],
["ruscam00.xml", "Operation Uranus", "Operation Uranus — 20 November 1942<br><br>Comrade General, the Germans have committed their strength to Stalingrad. Their Romanian allies hold the long flanks, and our counteroffensive is striking those flanks before the enemy can pull his armour out of the city.<br><br>Break through on the Chir approaches and take the positions around Sirki. Their roads and crossings lead into the Axis rear. Bring the mobile formations through the breach before the German command can turn troops away from Stalingrad to close it.", [{'country': 13, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam01.xml", "Operation Saturn", "Operation Little Saturn — 16 December 1942<br><br>The Sixth Army is surrounded at Stalingrad, but the fighting outside the ring is far from over. On the Don, the Italian Eighth Army holds the next section of the Axis front. Breaking it will threaten the roads and airfields on which the German position in the south depends.<br><br>Break the Italian line and seize the junctions behind it. Their infantry has prepared positions, but the distances between them give our armour room once a breach is opened. Carry the attack through before German reserves can form a new front.", [{'country': 12, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam02.xml", "Magyar Massacre", "The Hungarian front on the Don — 13 January 1943<br><br>Comrade General, the winter offensive is widening. The Hungarian Second Army is stretched along the Don, protecting the northern flank of the Axis forces in southern Russia. Its road and rail connections are the next targets.<br><br>Force the crossings and take the positions along the highway. Those roads can carry the enemy's reserves towards the fighting or his retreat towards Kharkov. Get across them while the Hungarian formations are still tied to their river positions.", [{'country': 4, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam03.xml", " During Operation Star", "Towards Izyum — 2 February 1943<br><br>Stalingrad has fallen. Our armies are pressing west, and Operation Star is opening towards Kharkov. Your sector lies around Izyum, where the roads and crossings can carry the advance into the German rear.<br><br>Drive through the Izyum sector and seize the roads beyond it. The Germans have been pushed back, but their mobile reserves are still dangerous. Headquarters needs the crossing kept open behind the advance so the following formations can come through.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam04.xml", "Kursk", "Prokhorovka — 12 July 1943<br><br>Comrade General, the German southern attack on the Kursk salient has reached the Prokhorovka sector. You are fighting with the Fifth Guards Tank Army against SS armoured formations, including Leibstandarte and Das Reich. Their guns can destroy a careless advance long before our tanks reach useful range.<br><br>Hold Prokhorovka and counterattack towards Ivanovski. The Germans must be denied room to extend their breakthrough. Their anti-tank guns cover the approaches; the Fifth Guards Tank Army needs infantry and artillery with it when the attack reaches the villages.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam05.xml", "Orel Counter Offensive", "Orel counteroffensive — 1 August 1943<br><br>The German attack on Kursk has spent its strength. Operation Kutuzov is now pressing into the Orel salient, the enemy's great forward position between our central fronts.<br><br>Break through towards Karachev and seize the junctions around Orel and Bryansk. These roads allow the enemy to move reserves across the salient and pull threatened formations out. Cut them before the withdrawal becomes an orderly one.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam06.xml", "Krivoi Rog", "Krivoi Rog — 17 October 1943<br><br>Comrade General, Konev's forces are attacking out of the Kremenchug bridgehead into the Dnieper bend. The direction is south, towards the iron-producing district around Krivoi Rog and the railways that supply the German position.<br><br>Push south towards Krivoi Rog and seize the positions covering the railways. Keep the Kremenchug crossings secure behind the attack: the First Panzer Army can still strike back at the narrow connection to our bridgehead.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam07.xml", "Crossing Kiev", "Kiev — 3 November 1943<br><br>The bombardment has opened. Our forces are striking from the bridgehead north of Kiev, seeking a way into a city that has endured more than two years of occupation.<br><br>Break the Fourth Panzer Army's line and clear the approaches to Kiev. Keep the crossings behind the assault open for the troops and guns coming into the bridgehead. The first columns must have an army behind them when they reach the city.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam08.xml", "Zhitomir Halt", "Zhitomir — 7 November 1943<br><br>Kiev has been liberated, and headquarters wants the advance carried west before the Germans recover. Zhitomir is a road and rail junction beyond the new bridgehead, valuable both to our pursuit and to any German counterattack.<br><br>Take Korostyshev and Zhitomir, with Brusilov covering the rear. Enemy armour is moving into the sector, including the newly arriving Twenty-Fifth Panzer Division. Hold the captured junctions against its counterstroke so the Kiev bridgehead can continue to expand.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam09.xml", "Iasi Invasion", "Towards Jassy — 13 April 1944<br><br>The winter advance has brought the Red Army into the borderlands of Romania. Ahead are Romanian defenders and German formations trying to rebuild a front around Jassy and the approaches to the Carpathians.<br><br>Advance from Beltsy towards Botosani, Jassy and Piatra Neamt. Seizing those junctions will cut across the enemy's routes of supply and withdrawal. The rivers and hills favour his defence; keep the route back to Beltsy open while the forward columns force their crossings.", [{'country': 13, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam10.xml", "Operation Bagration", "Operation Bagration — 22 June 1944<br><br>Three years after the invasion, our armies are preparing to break Army Group Centre. In this sector the road west runs through the German Ninth Army's positions around Bobruisk.<br><br>Break the line through Parichi and Bobruisk while holding Bortniki behind the attack. The roads through this difficult country are the Ninth Army's way out. Reach them while our neighbouring armies are still holding the Germans to the front.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam11.xml", "Minsk Offensive", "Minsk — 29 June 1944<br><br>The German front in Belorussia is breaking, and retreating formations are falling back towards Minsk. Its roads and railway junctions offer them a way out of the developing encirclement.<br><br>Advance from Borisov and seize Minsk and its airfield. Close the roads through the city before the retreating formations reach them. Keep Borisov secure so fuel and ammunition can follow the mobile columns into the developing encirclement.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam12.xml", "Vilnius Offensive", "Vilnius — 5 July 1944<br><br>Minsk is behind us. Chernyakhovsky's Third Belorussian Front is sending its mobile forces towards Vilnius, the next major road and rail centre on the route west.<br><br>Take Vilnius and Dabrauljany, keeping Malodeczno secure behind the advance. The mobile columns may reach Vilnius before the rifle formations; contain its garrison until enough troops arrive to clear the city and hold the roads against relief attacks.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam13.xml", "The Gates of Warsaw", "The gates of Warsaw — 1 August 1944<br><br>Our advance has reached the approaches to Warsaw, but the spearheads have outrun much of their support. Around Wolomin, German armoured reserves are gathering against the exposed Soviet tank formations.<br><br>Hold Wolomin and take Sulejowek, with Minsk Mazowiecki covering the rear. The German armour threatens to cut off the forward grouping. Secure these eastern approaches before committing the exhausted spearheads any farther towards the Vistula.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam14.xml", "Debrecen", "Debrecen and Nyiregyhaza — 23 October 1944<br><br>Comrade General, Pliyev's cavalry-mechanised group has pushed north, but the Germans are threatening the narrow connection behind it. Nyiregyhaza lies across the withdrawal routes from the east; losing the corridor could leave our own forward troops surrounded.<br><br>Drive through Nagykallo and secure the corridor between Debrecen and Nyiregyhaza. The Sixth Guards Tank Army is fighting alongside the forward group, but the Germans can attack the narrow road between our positions. Keep it open for supplies and for any troops that must fall back.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam15.xml", "Budapest Offensive", "Budapest approaches — 7 November 1944<br><br>Our armies have entered Hungary, and the offensive is moving towards Budapest. German and Hungarian forces are using the towns south-east of the capital to delay the advance and protect the roads into it.<br><br>Break through from Pilis and Dabas towards Ullo, Gyomro and Dunaharszti. Keep Cegled and Kecskemet secure behind the advancing columns. Clearing this belt of towns will give the army roads on which to bring its strength against Budapest.", [{'country': 4, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam16.xml", "East Prussian Offensive", "East Prussia — 13 January 1945<br><br>The offensive into East Prussia has begun. German forces have prepared successive defensive positions behind the frontier, using towns and road junctions to protect the routes towards Konigsberg and the Baltic coast.<br><br>Drive west from Rastenburg towards Allenstein, Heilsberg and Elbing. Take the road junctions behind the German positions and force the defenders to abandon their prepared lines. The winter roads must carry our supplies as well as the leading columns.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam17.xml", "Stargard tank battle", "Stargard — 15 February 1945<br><br>Our advance towards the Oder has left a dangerous enemy concentration in Pomerania. German armour around Stargard and Arnswalde threatens the flank of the forces preparing to move on Berlin.<br><br>Take Stargard and Arnswalde while protecting Brallenthin. German armour can still move between these towns and strike south into the main front's flank. Clear that threat before the armies on the Oder commit themselves towards Berlin.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam18.xml", "Seelow Heights", "Seelow Heights — 16 April 1945<br><br>Berlin lies beyond the heights, but the German Ninth Army still holds the approaches above the Oder plain. Our artillery has opened the operation; now the First Belorussian Front must turn bombardment into a breach.<br><br>Advance from Kustrin, take Seelow and Muncheberg, and clear the southern approaches through Frankfurt. The infantry and engineers must open passages through the prepared positions for the armour. Once the heights are ours, the roads towards Berlin lie ahead.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam19.xml", "The Last Battle: Berlin", "Berlin — 22 April 1945<br><br>Comrade General, the battle has reached Berlin. German soldiers, police and improvised formations are defending streets, bridges and fortified buildings while our armies close around the city.<br><br>Take the city sectors and Potsdam, with the route through Muncheberg kept open behind you. Each captured crossing gives our assault groups a way into the next district. Bring the infantry and engineers through the barricades before exposing the tanks to the guns inside the buildings.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["Soviet Counter-Offensive Campaign (1942-1946)"],
["rcampx01.xml", "Operation Uranus", "Stalingrad counteroffensive — fictional campaign<br><br>The German Sixth Army is committed to Stalingrad, with Romanian armies holding its long flanks. Operation Uranus is to break those flanks and close the roads behind the troops fighting in the city.<br><br>Force the crossings on the Don and Chir and bring the mobile formations into the Axis rear. German armour and aircraft can still strike the advancing columns. Keep the passages open for the troops following us, and close the ring before relief forces can reach Paulus.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx02.xml", "Operation Saturn", "The Stalingrad pocket is sealed, but the wider Axis front on the Don has not yet collapsed. Italian formations, fortified western approaches, and a strongly defended central airfield block the next stage of the counteroffensive. Strike before the enemy can recover from Operation Uranus, destroy the Italian Eighth Army’s cohesion, and open the road toward Millerovo and Rostov. A rapid victory will expand the encirclement and deny Manstein the forces he needs for a relief attempt. Use armour for depth, not merely for the first line, and keep the winter advance moving.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx03.xml", "The Road to Rostov", "The Chir and Don crossings are heavily guarded, and German aircraft are already moving east to reinforce the threatened sector. Your task is to rupture the river line, seize the bridges, and create the deployment space required for the advance on Rostov. The enemy expects the rivers to slow you long enough for reserves to arrive; prove that expectation fatal. Concentrate artillery on a narrow front, force the crossings under cover, and exploit immediately with mobile units before the defensive network can be rebuilt.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx04.xml", "Airstrike Rostov", "Rostov is the gateway to the Caucasus, but the assault cannot begin until several tactical deployment sites are secured around the city. Reconnaissance reports limited defenders and little air cover—an opportunity that will vanish as soon as the enemy understands your intention. Advance with speed, seize the staging areas intact, and protect the corridors through which the main army must follow. The main army needs these assembly areas before it can bring its strength against Rostov.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx05.xml", "Rostov", "Rostov is held by an Axis garrison with heavy armour, anti-tank batteries, cavalry and local air support. The enemy intends to turn the city into a shield for the Caucasus withdrawal and a fortress on the Don. Use reconnaissance to identify the heavy armour, isolate the strongest positions, and attack the city from more than one direction. A frontal rush will burn away your tank strength; combined arms and careful encirclement can instead trap the defenders and open the southern road toward the Crimea.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx06.xml", "Sevastopol", "Sevastopol stands behind coastal guns, prepared urban defences, and incoming airborne reinforcements. Soviet marines, naval forces, aircraft, and paratroopers have already secured footholds around the fortress, but the final assault must be coordinated before Axis help arrives across the Black Sea. Suppress the batteries, protect the landing zones, and break into the city without allowing the defenders to concentrate against a single approach. The capture of Sevastopol will restore a vital base and place the entire Crimean coast within reach.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx07.xml", "Northwest to Odessa", "The road north from Sevastopol appears lightly held, but scattered Axis units and reconnaissance aircraft can still delay the movement toward Odessa. Treat these skirmishes as an operational race: clear the route, preserve fuel and ammunition, and prevent isolated enemy groups from cutting your columns or reporting their strength. Your army must arrive at the next battlefield organised rather than exhausted. A clean pursuit will keep the Black Sea initiative in Soviet hands and ensure that the heavy guns waiting farther west face a concentrated army, not a string of vulnerable detachments.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx08.xml", "Odessa", "Odessa is protected by dense anti-tank positions, heavy artillery, Italian naval elements, and two formidable railway guns. The enemy has prepared the coastal approaches to punish armour and delay any direct assault, but Soviet naval gunfire and bomber support are becoming available. Neutralise the long-range batteries, secure the shoreline, and open safe lanes for infantry and tanks to enter the city. This is a combined-arms siege: victory depends on using sea, air, artillery, and ground forces as a single system rather than feeding units into the fortifications piecemeal.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx09.xml", "German Counterattack Kharkov", "Kursk has been liberated, but German forces are regrouping around Kharkov under experienced commanders and have shot down the aircraft sent to examine their positions. You must advance with incomplete intelligence against a city that has changed hands before and will be defended by armour, artillery, and mobile reserves. Probe carefully, secure the approaches, and avoid exposing your spearheads to a prepared counterstroke. Take Kharkov, break the enemy’s ability to stabilise the front, and clear the way toward the Dnieper operations that will follow.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx10.xml", "To Kiev - But First Kanev", "German and Romanian remnants are holding Kanev to protect the approaches to Kiev and the Dnieper crossings. The visible garrison appears small, but Luftwaffe activity has blinded reconnaissance along the river and hidden whatever reserves wait beyond the city limits. Seize the crossings, eliminate the holdouts, and establish a secure bridgehead before the main battle for Kiev begins. Speed is important, but a careless river assault could leave your formations divided on opposite banks. Take Kanev cleanly and give the armies converging on Kiev a firm southern anchor.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx11.xml", "Kiev", "The battle for Kiev is already under way. Konev, Malinovsky, and Vatutin are attacking from the north and centre while your force approaches from the south through uncertain terrain and hostile air cover. Your role is to reinforce the encirclement, seize the southern crossings, and prevent the garrison from escaping or receiving relief. Kiev is too large for a single thrust: isolate districts, coordinate armour with infantry, and keep supply routes across the river open. Liberate the city without allowing the battle to consume the army needed for the advance beyond Ukraine.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx12.xml", "Belgrade Liberation", "With Kiev secured, Romanian resistance around Belgrade threatens the flank and communications of the wider Soviet advance. Enemy tanks, anti-tank guns, and mixed Axis units defend the approaches, while damaged airfields must be captured before your own aviation can operate effectively. Clear the region, seize the bases, and eliminate the possibility of a counterattack from the south. The roads behind our advance must be secure before the armies move on towards Poland.", [{'country': 13, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx13.xml", "Poland", "The armies driving through Poland are waiting for your formation on the south-eastern sector of the front. Luftwaffe patrols have destroyed reconnaissance aircraft, but airborne reinforcements are prepared to seize advanced positions and accelerate the junction. Break through the remaining German screen, protect the drop zones, and connect your force with the neighbouring Soviet armies before the enemy can defeat either element separately. Success will complete the concentration for the final advance to the Oder; delay will give Berlin precious time to fortify its approaches.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx14.xml", "The Road to Berlin", "The Oder line is the last great operational barrier before Berlin. Enemy troops are scattered around the approaches, city limits are heavily armed, and surprise detachments wait beyond the areas visible to reconnaissance. Secure the crossings, destroy isolated strongpoints, and bring your army into position before the Western Allies can reach the German capital first. The defenders are depleted but still dangerous, especially where anti-tank guns and urban terrain can halt Soviet armour. Open the road to Berlin and preserve enough strength for the battles inside the city.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx15.xml", "The Battle of Berlin", "Berlin is surrounded, but the Luftwaffe and dense anti-aircraft defences have forced Soviet reconnaissance out of the city. The enemy has converted streets, rail yards, government buildings, and hidden arsenals into a layered defensive system whose true strength remains uncertain. Drive into the capital, divide the garrison, and seize the crossings before the defenders can shift reserves between sectors. Expect ambushes, heavy anti-tank fire, and close urban combat. This is not yet the Reichstag assault—it is the battle to make that final objective reachable.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx16.xml", "The Fall of the Reichstag", "The Reichstag has become the last symbol and one of the strongest fortresses in Berlin. Its defenders possess more ammunition, anti-tank weapons, and heavy artillery than intelligence predicted, while barricades and firing positions have appeared overnight. Reduce the surrounding blocks, isolate the building, and bring infantry and engineers forward under concentrated fire support. Do not squander tanks against hidden guns in the streets. Take the Reichstag, raise the red banner over the centre of German power, and end the European war with a victory worthy of the losses that brought you here.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx17.xml", "Berlin Standoff", "Berlin: the alliance breaks — alternate history<br><br>Fighting has broken out across the occupation line. American, British and French troops are attacking the Soviet sector while our engineers are still putting its defences in order. Yesterday's allies now face one another across the streets.<br><br>Hold East Berlin and secure the roads into the sector. Bring the scattered garrisons into a connected defence before the attackers can split them. Headquarters needs the line stabilised while it establishes how far this fighting has spread.", [{'country': 22, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx18.xml", "Conquer Europe?", "Orders from headquarters confirm the new alliance. German and Italian formations will fight beside us against the Western armies now withdrawing towards Dunkirk. Men who were enemies a few weeks ago must use the same roads and answer the same calls for support.<br><br>Move west with the coalition forces and secure the approaches to the evacuation ports. The German formations will cover the northern flank. Reach the coast before the withdrawing armies have time to organise another bridgehead.", [{'country': 22, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx19.xml", "Taking of Dunkirk", "The Western Allies are compressed around Dunkirk, but the port remains their gateway to the English Channel. Soviet, German, and Italian forces must break the siege perimeter, seize an airfield and deployment zone, and prevent another evacuation across the water. Naval and air support are available, yet transport capacity is limited and heavy artillery cannot all be moved forward at once. Secure the coast, destroy the remaining bridgehead, and establish the bases required for an invasion of Britain. Failure here will give the Allies time to rebuild behind the Channel.", [{'country': 22, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx20.xml", "English Channel", "Operation Nexus carries the new coalition across the English Channel. British, American, and French forces contest the crossing while Soviet and allied transports struggle to deliver armour, artillery, and paratroopers to the southern coast. Capture an airfield immediately or enemy aircraft will turn the beaches and sea lanes into a graveyard. Then seize the deployment zone, widen the lodgement, and prevent the defenders from containing the invasion. The operation is a race between reinforcement and destruction: establish a functioning bridgehead before the Channel closes behind you.", [{'country': 22, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx21.xml", "Annexation of South England", "The invasion has gained a foothold in southern England, and allied armies are pushing toward London from the north. Your force must annex the southern approaches, secure roads and airbases, and prepare the advance on Windsor. The countryside may appear open, but British reserves can use towns, rivers, and narrow routes to delay heavier formations. Keep the landing areas supplied, prevent local counterattacks from reaching the coast, and build a continuous front. A swift southern advance will close the first half of the ring around the British capital.", [{'country': 22, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx22.xml", "Windsor 1946", "Windsor is heavily fortified and stands between your southern army and the encirclement of London. German units have reached the north-eastern outskirts while paratroopers and advance detachments hold scattered tactical positions inside the metropolitan area. Exploit identified gaps, secure the airborne landing zones, and break the Windsor defences before British reserves can seal the corridor. The city’s air and ground support remains strong, so every isolated spearhead risks destruction. Take Windsor, connect the encircling forces, and prepare for the final struggle for London.", [{'country': 22, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx23.xml", "London Blitz", "Britain and France have capitulated, and the war crosses the Atlantic. A Soviet-German naval force, supported by submarines, destroyers, aircraft, and landing troops, approaches the Florida coast before American radar detects the deployment. Enemy destroyers and air units guard the objective, but no reinforcements are expected during the opening assault. Win control of the sea, suppress the coastal defence, and seize the first strategic point intact. If the landing fails, the nearest heavy reinforcements will still be on the other side of the Atlantic.", [{'country': 22, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx24.xml", "Onward to the USA", "The first American coastal position lies east of Florida, while other coalition armies strike farther north. Your air support will remain limited until an airbase is captured, leaving ships and landing forces exposed while the first troops are coming ashore. Secure the tactical point, take the airfield, and expand the beachhead before American forces can coordinate a counterattack. Naval gunfire can open the way, but only ground units can hold what has been won. Establish the bridgehead that will carry the war from the Atlantic shore into the American interior.", [{'country': 9, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx25.xml", "Florida Landing", "The Florida landing has succeeded, and the invasion front is moving north. Savannah is strongly fortified, but a captured airbase gives your army access to air and naval support while reinforcements approach from the coast. The city anchors the American southern defence and blocks the route toward Washington. Isolate its fortifications, protect the supply corridor to the beaches, and coordinate bombardment with a deliberate ground assault. Take Savannah before the defenders can turn it into a prolonged siege and allow the northern coalition armies to join the advance inland.", [{'country': 9, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx26.xml", "Red Savannah", "Savannah has fallen and the road toward the American capital is opening. Coalition armies are driving south and west from the Atlantic while your force prepares the next stage of the offensive. American resistance is reorganising around key transport routes, industrial centres, and the approaches to Washington. Keep the columns moving, capture airfields and supply hubs, and prevent the defenders from forming a continuous line. The forces that clear these roads will be needed again at Washington; bring them through in fighting order.", [{'country': 9, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx27.xml", "Washington in Flames", "Washington lies ahead of the converging coalition armies. American regular troops and emergency formations hold the outer defences, with artillery covering the Potomac crossings and the roads into the government district.<br><br>Break the defensive ring, secure the crossings and bring the army into the capital. Keep the supply road open behind the assault; the city's defenders can still strike from districts our leading troops have passed. Headquarters expects the fall of Washington to end organised resistance.", [{'country': 9, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["Standalone Historical Battles"],
["cubali01.xml", "Sierra Maestra 1958", "Oriente Province, spring 1958. Eighteen months after the yacht Granma put 82 men ashore, Fidel Castro's 26th of July Movement holds the high Sierra Maestra and little else. In Havana, Batista is gathering more than ten thousand soldiers, with tanks and aircraft, for the offensive meant to finish the rebels for good: Operation Verano.<br><br>Don't wait for it. Come down from the mountains, overrun the garrisons, seize the sugar mills and cut the roads to Bayamo and Manzanillo. Every town you take is one the army must fight to win back. How far can a guerrilla army reach before the blow lands? Far enough for Santiago de Cuba?<br><br>From The Latin Generals scenario collection. Special thanks to JML and Paqueo for testing.", [{"id": 0, "country": 107}], [{"id": 1, "country": 83}], "eqp-olgcw" ],
["battle_cuito.xml", "Battle of Cuito Cuanavale (1987)", "South-east Angola, December 1987. The FAPLA offensive against UNITA-held Mavinga has ended in disaster. South African guns and armour caught its brigades on the Lomba River, and the survivors have fallen back on Cuito Cuanavale, the town that anchors the whole southern front.<br><br>In Havana, Fidel Castro has decided that Cuito will not fall. Cuban tank crews, gunners and pilots are on their way, and General Arnaldo Ochoa has taken command. Stop the rout, then turn it around and carry the war back to Mavinga. The fighting that follows is often called the largest battle in Africa since the Second World War, and its echoes will reach all the way to Namibian independence.<br><br>From The Latin Generals scenario collection.", [{"id": 0, "country": 245}], [{"id": 1, "country": 48}], "eqp-olgcw" ],
["amilastc_sfb.xml", "Amin's Last Chance (1979)", "Uganda, March 1979. Idi Amin's invasion of Tanzania's Kagera Salient has backfired. President Nyerere has answered with a counter-invasion, and the Tanzanian army and Ugandan exiles are across the border and driving on Kampala.<br><br>Amin's last hope is his friend in Tripoli. Muammar Gaddafi is flying Libyan troops, armour and Katyusha rocket launchers into Entebbe to stop the invaders on the Kampala road. Command the defenders and hold as much ground as you can for as long as you can. Historically, the Libyan counterattack broke at Lukaya, and Kampala fell on 11 April. This is the other side of Victory at Kampala: the same war, seen from inside a collapsing regime.<br><br>From The Latin Generals scenario collection.", [{"id": 1, "country": 297}], [{"id": 0, "country": 296}], "eqp-olgcw" ],
["1954_dienbienphu.xml", "1954 Battle of Dien Bien Phu", "North-west Tonkin, spring 1954. The French built their fortress in a valley near the Laotian border, certain that no Viet Minh army could bring artillery through the jungle mountains around it. General V\u00f5 Nguy\u00ean Gi\u00e1p's soldiers and porters did it anyway. They dragged guns by hand onto the heights and moved supplies on bicycles.<br><br>B\u00e9atrice and Gabrielle fell in the first days of the siege in March, and French aircraft can no longer land. What is left are the Legionnaires and paratroopers in Dominique, Eliane, Claudine, Fran\u00e7oise and the southern outpost of Isabelle, with a handful of tanks. Close the ring and finish it. The garrison surrendered on 7 May 1954. The next day, the Geneva Conference turned to Indochina.", [{"id": 0, "country": 77}], [{"id": 1, "country": 6}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["khalkin1.xml", "Khalkhin Gol 1 - Japanese Attack (1939)", "The Mongolian steppe, early July 1939. After weeks of border clashes near Nomonhan, the Kwantung Army has decided to \"expel the invaders\". On the night of 2\u20133 July, Lieutenant General Komatsubara's infantry crossed the Khalkhin Gol on a single pontoon bridge and took Bain-Tsagan hill on the west bank. At the same time, General Yasuoka's tanks struck the Soviet bridgehead on the east bank.<br><br>If the Japanese hold Bain-Tsagan, every Soviet and Mongolian unit across the river is cut off. Komdiv Georgy Zhukov cannot wait for his infantry. He sends his tank and armoured-car brigades straight off the march against the hill. Drive the Japanese back over the river before they dig in.", [{"id": 1, "country": 5}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2" ],
["khalkin2.xml", "Khalkhin Gol 2 - Zhukov's Strike (1939)", "20 August 1939, 05:45. For six weeks the two armies have faced each other across the Khalkhin Gol. Zhukov, now commanding the new 1st Army Group, has used them to hide a build-up. He sent fake radio traffic about digging in for the winter, played the noise of pile drivers and engines over loudspeakers, and moved tanks only at night. Meanwhile the Japanese plan an offensive of their own for 24 August.<br><br>Strike first. After the artillery and hundreds of aircraft have done their work, pin the 23rd Division in the centre while the tank brigades on both flanks swing around behind it. Close the pincers at Nomonhan before the enemy understands what is happening. The defeat will weigh on Tokyo two years later, when it chooses to strike south rather than at the Soviet Union.", [{"id": 1, "country": 5}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2" ],
["sparta.xml", "Spartacist Uprising - Berlin (1919)", "Berlin, 5 January 1919. Two months after the revolution toppled the Kaiser, Friedrich Ebert's government has sacked Emil Eichhorn, the left-wing police chief. Crowds pour into the streets. Armed workers occupy the newspaper quarter around Kochstra\u00dfe, and Karl Liebknecht and the Revolutionary Stewards form a committee to overthrow the government.<br><br>Ebert has given Gustav Noske the job of restoring order. \"Someone has to be the bloodhound,\" Noske says, and he calls in the Freikorps: the Reinhard brigade from the north, volunteers from Potsdam and the Garde-Kavallerie-Sch\u00fctzen-Division from the south. Take the Reichstag and strike at their bases before they close in. Historically, the rising was crushed within a week. On 15 January, officers of that same Guard Cavalry division murdered Liebknecht and Rosa Luxemburg.<br><br>Historical liberties: the People's Navy Division (Volksmarinedivision), which stayed out of the January fighting, fights here, and the cavalry from F\u00fcrstenwalde and Freienwalde is invented for balance.", [{"id": 0, "country": 188}], [{"id": 1, "country": 161}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["madrid_36.xml", "Defence of Madrid (1936)", "Madrid, November 1936. Franco's Army of Africa has marched up the Tagus valley almost unchecked, and General Varela's columns stand in the Casa de Campo and at the bridges over the Manzanares. The government has left for Valencia. Everyone expects the capital to fall within days. General Mola boasts of a \"fifth column\" already waiting inside the city.<br><br>Madrid decides otherwise. General Miaja's defence junta, the militias, the first Mixed Brigades of the new People's Army and the International Brigades, who marched down the Gran V\u00eda on 8 November, hold the line at the University City and the Puente de los Franceses. \u00a1No pasar\u00e1n! Keep them out of Madrid. Historically, the city held for almost two and a half more years.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226}], "eqp-gce" ],
["mallorca.xml", "Landing on Mallorca (1936)", "Balearic Islands, August 1936. Menorca stayed loyal to the Republic, but Mallorca went over to the rebels in the first days of the war. Captain Alberto Bayo, an air force officer, sets out from Barcelona with Catalan militia and volunteers to win it back. On 16 August his troops come ashore on the east coast around Porto Cristo, supported by warships and seaplanes.<br><br>Secure the east-coast harbours, then drive inland on Manacor, Inca and Palma before the Nationalists recover and Italian aircraft arrive. Historically, the bridgehead stalled and was evacuated in early September. Bayo's story does not end here: twenty years later, in Mexico, he trained the men of Fidel Castro's Granma expedition.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226}], "eqp-gce" ],
["teruel.xml", "Battle of Teruel (1937)", "Aragon, December 1937. Teruel juts into Republican territory like a gun pointed at the Levante coast, and Franco is massing his army for a new offensive against Madrid. The Republic strikes first to stop it. On 15 December the People's Army attacks in a blizzard, in the coldest Spanish winter in decades, with temperatures falling to around \u221220 \u00b0C.<br><br>Encircle the city, beat off the relief columns and take Teruel street by street. Colonel Rey d'Harcourt's garrison held out in the seminary and the Bank of Spain until 8 January. Teruel was the only provincial capital the Republic ever took from the rebels. Then Franco's counteroffensive came, and the battle became one of the bloodiest of the war.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226}], "eqp-gce" ],
["ebro.xml", "Battle of the Ebro (1938)", "Catalonia, 25 July 1938. After the disasters of the winter and spring, the Republic has been cut in two and is widely written off abroad. The rebel advance through the Levante is driving on Valencia. The Republic needs a feat of arms to prove it is still alive.<br><br>Before dawn, Juan Modesto's Army of the Ebro crosses the river in boats and on pontoon bridges between Mequinenza and Amposta and falls on the Nationalist rear. Take Gandesa and the heights around it, then hold what you have taken against crushing rebel superiority in aircraft and artillery. Historically, Gandesa never fell. The battle lasted 115 days, the longest of the war, and was the last fight of the International Brigades.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226}], "eqp-gce" ],
["partisanen.xml", "Yugoslav Partisans - Operation Weiss (1943)", "Dalmatia, February 1943. On the mainland, the Axis has launched Case White, its largest offensive yet against Tito's Partisans. Across the channel from Split, on the island of Bra\u010d, local Partisans have spent months raiding the occupiers and ferrying men and supplies to the coast. Now a regiment of German mountain troops has landed and taken the harbours.<br><br>Come down from the hills, retake Postira, Milna and Mirca, and throw the Gebirgsj\u00e4ger back into the sea. This is a what-if. In 1943 Bra\u010d was under Italian occupation, and German troops came to the island only after Italy's surrender.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 239}], "eqp-pzliga" ],
["aran.xml", "Val d'Aran Invasion (1944)", "The Pyrenees, October 1944. France is almost free, and thousands of Spanish Republicans who fought in the French Resistance believe Franco will be next. The communist-led Spanish National Union sends some four thousand guerrillas over the mountains into the Val d'Aran, a valley on the northern slope that the winter snows cut off from the rest of Spain.<br><br>The plan is to take Vielha, proclaim a provisional Republican government on Spanish soil, spark a popular rising and draw the Allies into finishing Franco off. Take the valley and the roads south before the army's reinforcements arrive. Historically, no rising came. Franco rushed tens of thousands of troops north, and after ten days Santiago Carrillo ordered the retreat. Can you do better?", [{"id": 1, "country": 234}], [{"id": 0, "country": 91}], "eqp-pzliga" ],
["op_hooper.xml", "Operation Hooper - Cuito Cuanavale (1987)", "Cuito Cuanavale, the turn of 1988. The South African Defence Force has chased the beaten FAPLA brigades back to the Cuito River. In Operation Hooper it means to finish them by destroying the forces still east of the river and, if it can, taking the town.<br><br>This time the defenders are not alone. Cuban tanks and artillery have arrived, Cuban MiG-23s contest the sky, and the Tumpo bridgehead has been ringed with minefields and gun lines. Bleed the South African assaults dry, then strike back toward Mavinga. Pretoria's army left Cuito without the town, and within months Cuban columns were advancing on the Namibian border.<br><br>From The Latin Generals scenario collection.", [{"id": 0, "country": 245}], [{"id": 1, "country": 48}], "eqp-olgcw" ],
["vkampala_sfb.xml", "Victory at Kampala (1979)", "Uganda, March 1979. Idi Amin invaded Tanzania's Kagera Salient last autumn. President Julius Nyerere answered in a way nobody expected, with a counter-invasion. The Tanzania People's Defence Force, with Ugandan exiles at its side, has crossed the border and is driving on the capital.<br><br>Amin has called in his ally Muammar Gaddafi, and Libyan troops are landing at Entebbe. Break them at Lukaya, take Entebbe and its airport, and march into Kampala. The capital fell on 11 April 1979, and Amin fled into exile.<br><br>From The Latin Generals scenario collection.", [{"id": 0, "country": 297}], [{"id": 1, "country": 296}], "eqp-olgcw" ],
["1920_perekop.xml", "1920 Siege of Perekop", "Northern Tavria, November 1920. Poland has signed an armistice, and the Red Army can at last turn its full weight on the last White army in European Russia. Baron Wrangel's troops have fallen back into the Crimea behind the Perekop isthmus. They hold the old Turkish Wall, a rampart the height of a three-storey house fronted by a deep ditch, with the Ishun lines behind it.<br><br>Frunze's Southern Front will storm Perekop head-on while other columns wade the freezing shallows of the Sivash to turn the defences. Makhno's Black Army, allied with the Reds against Wrangel, fights under your command. Break through, take Armyansk and Ishun, and open the road into the Crimea. Within days the Crimea was free, and what remained of the last White army had fled abroad by sea.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103, "support": [136]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-atomic"],
["Greece: Resistance and Civil War (1940-1949)"],
["bn4s00.xml", "Battle of Pindus", "BATTLE OF PINDUS - 3 NOV 1940<br><br>Pindus Mountains, Epirus<br><br>In your defense sector an Italian Division tries to advance on the strategic mountain pass at the town of Metsovo and threatens to cut off our supply routes and to separate our troops in Epirus and in Macedonia. Stop the attack and chase away the Italian troops from the Pindus Mountains! Our Cavalry Division will try to surround the enemy on their right flank and encircle the Italians together with your troops.<br><br>GOAL Capture all VH!<br><br>NOTE The unit occupying the town Vovousa, gets the chance of a Leader!", [{"id": 1, "country": 12}], [{"id": 0, "country": 39}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s01.xml", "Battle of Korytsa", "BATTLE OF KORYTSA - 16 NOV 1940<br><br>Morava Mountains, Albania<br><br>The Italian attack could be stopped along the entire front! Now we will take the initiative and launch an offensive on the eastern flank of the front. Target of the attack is traffic point Korytsa in Albania. A victory will strengthen the morale of our troops and our nation in general.<br><br>GOAL Capture all VH!<br><br>NOTE The unit occupying the town Korytsa gets the chance of gain experience!", [{"id": 1, "country": 12}], [{"id": 0, "country": 39}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s02.xml", "Klisura Pass", "KLISURA PASS - 6 JAN 1941<br><br>Trebeshine Heights, Albania<br><br>After your victory at Korytsa we could penetrate deep into Albanian territory. However, we need the strategic important Klisura pass to consolidate our position. You will be the right one for this job. Occupy the Klisura Pass and the surrounding heights of Trebeshine mountain range! <br><br>GOAL Take all Allies VH!<br><br>NOTE The unit occupying the Klisura Pass, gets the chance of a Leader!", [{"id": 1, "country": 12}], [{"id": 0, "country": 39}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s03.xml", "Italian Spring Offensive", "ITALIAN SPRING OFFENSIVE - 9 MAR 1941<br><br>Trebeshine Heights, Albania<br><br>In the last few weeks the Italians reinforced their army in Albania with fresh troops and we await the start of an offensive. Defend with your troops the Trebeshine Heights and if necessary recapture lost ground! <br><br>GOAL Hold after the tenth turn 10 VH, 9 VH or 8 VH for BV, V or TV!<br><br>NOTE In this mission the AI has the first turn!", [{"id": 1, "country": 12}], [{"id": 0, "country": 39}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s04.xml", "Retreat to Thessaloniki", "RETREAT TO THESSALONIKI - 8 APR 1941<br><br>South of Doiran Lake, Central Macedonia<br><br>As expected, the Germans invaded our country in support of their unsuccessful Allies, the Italians. German armored forces, through Yugoslavia bypassing the Metaxas Line, are on their way to Thessaloniki and threaten to encircle our East Macedonia Army. I fear that we are not able to stop the Germans here. Withdraw your troops immediately to Thessaloniki and try to establish a new defense line there. Use for your non-motorized units the railway line Kilkis-Thessaloniki to escape the rapid German forces!<br><br>GOAL Retreat 22 ground units via Exit Points or hold after the eighth turn 4 VH for BV! Hold after the eighth turn 3 VH or 2 VH for V or TV!<br><br>NOTE It is advisable to delay the deployment partly until the second turn, and then to send non-motorized units immediately via train on their journey. In this mission the AI has the first turn!", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 39}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s05.xml", "Thessaloniki - Evacuation", "THESSALONIKI - EVACUATION - 9 APR 1941<br><br>Thessaloniki, Central Macedonia<br><br>Thessaloniki is not to hold - Evacuate your troops to Athens via sea immediately! The remains of the Krussia Detachment and the 19th Motorised Infantry Division try to kept clear your back as long as possible!<br><br>GOAL Retreat 9 ground units (in sea transport) via Exit Points or hold after the seventh turn 4 VH for BV! Hold after the seventh turn 3 VH or 2 VH for V or TV!<br><br>NOTE Due to the short time between the missions at HQ no new units can be recruited!", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 39}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s06.xml", "Lake Kastoria", "LAKE KASTORIA - 15 APR 1941<br><br>Lake Kastoria, West Macedonia<br><br>As expected, the Germans invaded our country in support of their unsuccessful Allies, the Italians. Our East Macedonia Army capitulated already, our forces in Western Macedonia are destroyed and the Germans are close to Kozani. Thus our main forces in Albania threatens to cut off! We have no other choice but to immediate withdrawal from Albania. Advance with your troops immediately to Lake Kastoria and save our line of retreat!<br><br>GOAL Retreat 6 ground units via Exit Point or hold after the ninth turn 4 VH for BV! Hold after the ninth turn 3 VH or 2 VH for V or TV!", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 39}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s07.xml", "Metsovo Pass", "METSOVO PASS - 19 APR 1941<br><br>South of Grevena, West Macedonia<br><br>After your breakthrough at Lake Kastoria we could not hold open the gap for long time and only a few troops could escaped. You have now the Germans before and behind! A German SS unit, passed Lake Kastoria before, is already on their way to Metsovo pass and there is now the opportunity to attack this force from behind! Prevent the blockade of the Metsovo pass and allow further comrades to escape!<br><br>GOAL Capture all VH!<br><br>NOTE Due to the short time between the missions at HQ no new units can be recruited!", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 39}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s08.xml", "Last Stand at Thermopylae", "LAST STAND AT THERMOPYLAE - 24 APR 1941<br><br>Levadia, Central Greece<br><br>The Empire forces have set up a defensive position at Thermopylae to cover the evacuation of their main forces. Hasten to meet them and take over their positions, so that these forces also have a chance to escape across the sea!<br><br>GOAL Hold after the tenth turn 7 VH, 6 VH or 4 VH for BV, V or TV!<br><br>NOTE In this mission the AI has the first turn!", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 39}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s09.xml", "Crete - Invasion", "CRETE - INVASION - 20 MAY 1941<br><br>Chania, Crete<br><br>The crazy Germans actually try to conquer Crete from the air! Thwart this venture and destroy the German airborne troops!<br><br>Hold after the twelfth turn 6 VH, 5 VH or 4 VH for BV, V or TV!<br><br>NOTE In this mission the AI has the first turn! Last chance to buy a tank for the next six scenarios! ;)", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 39}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s10.xml", "Crete - Evacuation", "CRETE - EVACUATION - 28 MAY 1941<br><br>Sphakia, Crete<br><br>The withdrawal from Crete, the evacuation to Egypt was ordered - the island is not to hold! Move to the south coast of the island and board the waiting vessels!<br><br>GOAL Retreat 12 ground units (in sea transport) via Exit Points!<br><br>NOTE Due to the short time between the missions at HQ no new units can be recruited!", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 39}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s11.xml", "El Alamein", "EL ALAMEIN - 23 OCT 1942<br><br>Alam Naghil, south of El Alamein, Egypt<br><br>It is time to expel the Axis from Egypt! The offensive against the German-Italian positions at El Alamein has begun. Your troops have the task to attack the enemy positions east of Ruweisat Ridge and - if possible - to capture. The main attack will take place in the North and - in case of success -  force the entire German-Italian front to retreat!<br><br>GOAL Capture all VH!<br><br>NOTE A fighter squadron, trained and equipped by our British Allies, is subject to your command. Congratulations!", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 39}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s12.xml", "Crushing the Mutiny", "CRUSHING THE MUTINY - 24 APR 1944<br><br>At sea off Alexandria, Egypt<br><br>Bad news from Egypt! A pro-EAM (National Liberation Front of Greece) mutiny inside the Greek Navy and the first Greek Brigade is broke out. Your troops are shipped from Palestine to Alexandria and help to down the revolt!<br><br>GOAL Capture all VH!<br><br>NOTE In this mission the AI has the first turn!", [{"id": 1, "country": 82}], [{"id": 0, "country": 39}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s13.xml", "Foglia River", "FOGLIA RIVER - 2 SEP 1944<br><br>South of Foglia River , Italy<br><br>Welcome in Italy! The attack on the Gothic Line is under way! However, the German resistance is stronger than expected and parts of the British 8th Army must already be taken out of the front due to high losses and exhaustion. Your troops will replace these units. Perform a frontal assault against the German defense at the Foglia River and show our Allies friends to what Greeks are able!<br><br>GOAL Hold after the ninth turn 12 VH, 11 VH or 9 VH for BV, V or TV!<br><br>NOTE The unit occupying the town Morciano Di Romagna gets full replacements!", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 39}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s14.xml", "Battle of Rimini", "BATTLE OF RIMINI - 15 SEP 1944<br><br>South of Conca River, Italy<br><br>The Germans retreated behind the Conca River and established a new defensive line there. Break through that line, advance on Rimini and free the city!<br><br>GOAL Capture all VH!<br><br>NOTE A bomber squadron, trained and equipped by our British Allies, is subject to your command. Congratulations!", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 39}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s15.xml", "Battle of Athens", "BATTLE OF ATHENS - 12 DEC 1944<br><br>Athens, Greece<br><br>In Athens the Communists are gone over to armed struggle! At present, we have insufficient forces stationed in Athens, but the British have pledged to fly in the 4th Indian Division from Italy immediately. Beat back the communists and clear Athens and the surrounding areas from the rebels!<br><br>GOAL Capture all VH!<br><br>NOTE In this mission the AI has the first turn!", [{"id": 1, "country": 82}], [{"id": 0, "country": 39}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s16.xml", "Battle of Konitsa", "BATTLE OF KONITSA - 25 DEC 1947<br><br>South of Konitsa, Epirus<br><br>The communist rebels have attacked the city Konitsa on the Greek-Albanian border! The garrison defended the town stubbornly and until now was able to fend off all attacks. Advance on Konitsa and expel the rebels!<br><br>GOAL Capture all VH!<br><br>NOTE In this mission the AI has the first turn!", [{"id": 1, "country": 82}], [{"id": 0, "country": 39}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s17.xml", "Battle of Vitsi", "BATTLE OF VITSI - 9 SEP 1948<br><br>South of Lake Kastoria, West Macedonia<br><br>Our last operation in the Grammos mountains was a bust! Most rebels escaped in the Vitsi region. Our job is now to prevent a renewed Redoubt in the Vitsi mountains and to destroy the escaped enemy forces. We plan a coordinated attack from the south and east to encircle the rebels. Your troops will lead the attack from the south and clean the area around the Lake Kastoria!<br><br>GOAL Capture all VH!<br><br>NOTE The unit occupying the town Dendrochori gets full replacements!", [{"id": 1, "country": 82}], [{"id": 0, "country": 39}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s18.xml", "Operation Torch", "OPERATION TORCH - 24 AUG 1949<br><br>East of  Mt Grammos, Pindus Mountains<br><br>We are on the verge of winning the war! The defeated rebels have been entrenched in the mountains at the Albania border and the General Staff has ordered a last major operation in order to complete our victory. The Americans have supplied us with modern dive bomber and they should help to destroy the strong fortifications. Chase off the remaining communist troops from their fortifications in the Grammos mountains!<br><br>GOAL Capture all VH!", [{"id": 1, "country": 82}], [{"id": 0, "country": 39}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s19.xml", "Escape from Egypt", "ESCAPE FROM EGYPT - 8 MAY 1943<br><br>Military Prison Al-Qabbari, Alexandria<br><br>The renowned hero now only a public enemy! Jailed in the military prison of Al-Qabbari you are waiting for your trial because of communist propaganda and insubordination against the Middle East High Command and the Greek government in exile. However, your friends managed to organize your escape to Greece and to provide you with a getaway car. At the airport of Alexandria a plane is ready for take off and alternatively a vessel waiting for you located in the port of Al Muaddiyah. Reach one of these points without to be caught at the control points of the Brits! Friends on the Greek freighters SS Dimitrios Inglessis and SS Thrace monitor the airport and the port for you!<br><br>GOAL Retreat your MSU via Exit Point!", [{"id": 1, "country": 22}], [{"id": 0, "country": 82}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s20.xml", "Punish the Traitors!", "PUNISH THE TRAITORS! - 10 OCT 1943<br><br>East of Kalabaka, Thessaly<br><br>Welcome to Greece, Commander! Experienced leaders like you we are needed urgently. The 13th ELAS Division is now under your command and your first task is a punishment operation against the traitorous EDES Bandits be making common cause with the Germans! Currently, the EDES control parts of the road Ioannina-Metsovo-Kalabaka. You will attack the EDES around Kalabaka and bring the area back under our control!<br><br>GOAL Capture all VH!<br><br>NOTE If you do not like the composition of your new Core, you can sell units and acquire new ones with same experience. However,  the increased 35% chance for a leader get lost. New units start with a chance of 10%!<br><br>The unit occupying the town Spathades, gets the chance of a Leader!", [{"id": 1, "country": 39}], [{"id": 0, "country": 82}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s21.xml", "Battle of Agorelitsa", "BATTLE OF AGORELITSA - 17 JUL 1944<br><br>South of Korifasi, Peloponnese<br><br>You will carry out a strike against the German occupation forces on the western Peloponnese. Target of your attack is the 41st Fortress Division and the neutralization of the coastal artillery near Marathopoli. The Germans have some battle-hardened units in this area, so be careful!<br><br>GOAL Capture all VH!<br><br>NOTE The unit occupying the town Agorelitsa, gets the chance of a Leader!", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 82}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s22.xml", "Battle of Athens", "BATTLE OF ATHENS - 12 DEC 1944<br><br>Athens, Greece<br><br>After the withdrawal of the Germans from Greece, the royalists have returned to our country and think they can - with the help of the disgusting Brits - rob the fruits of our liberation struggle! They also not shy away from massacre peaceful protesters to keep themselves in power. Once again it's time to take up arms and to chase these parasites out of our country!<br><br>GOAL Capture all VH!<br><br>NOTE The British will try to fly in reinforcements, so occupy as soon as possible all airfields!", [{"id": 1, "country": 39}], [{"id": 0, "country": 82}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s23.xml", "Battle of Konitsa", "BATTLE OF KONITSA - 25 DEC 1947<br><br>Konitsa, Epirus<br><br>Our struggle for a free Greece is now entering a decisive phase. Our political leadership has decided that we need a major city as capital for our government to gain further international validity for our fight. The choice has fallen on the city Konitsa at the Albanian border and the battle is already under way. But reinforcements are on the way to Konitsa to relieve the garrison. Fend off the attacks of the Athenian mercenary troops and bring the liberation of Konitsa to a successful end!<br><br>GOAL Capture all VH!", [{"id": 1, "country": 39}], [{"id": 0, "country": 82}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s24.xml", "First Battle of Grammos", "FIRST BATTLE OF GRAMMOS - 18 JUL 1948<br><br>Mt Grammos, Pindus Mountains<br><br>The battle for the Grammos mountains raged for nearly a month and the Athenian fascists send more and more mercenary troops into battle. We have no choice, we must abandon the Grammos mountains temporarily and dare the breakout! To achieve this, you will carry out a concentrated attack on the center of the enemy forces! Beat a breach in the enemy's ranks and lead our troops in Northeast direction to the Vitsi mountains!<br><br>GOAL Retreat 9 ground units via Exit Points!", [{"id": 1, "country": 39}], [{"id": 0, "country": 82}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s25.xml", "Battle of Vitsi", "BATTLE OF VITSI - 9 SEP 1948<br><br>Lake Kastoria, West Macedonia<br><br>It has not gone unnoticed that our main forces have retreated into the Vitsi mountains. With a new offensive the enemy wants us to deathblow here. But he underestimated our remaining strength and attack with only weak forces. After we have fool him with our withdraw he is now trapped! Destroy the enemy troops - a victory is urgently needed in order to maintain the morale of our forces!<br><br>GOAL Capture all VH!<br><br>NOTE In this mission the AI has the first turn!", [{"id": 1, "country": 39}], [{"id": 0, "country": 82}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s26.xml", "Aridaea", "ARIDAEA - 14 DEC 1948<br><br>East of Aridaea, West Macedonia<br><br>The liberation of Greek cities is still at the top of our priorities. Your Division will carry out an surprise attack across the Yugoslav border on Aridaea and free the city! If the resistance is broken here, the further advance on Veroea and Edessa is planned. Let's hope that you succeed and meet an unprepared enemy!<br><br>GOAL Capture all VH!", [{"id": 1, "country": 39}], [{"id": 0, "country": 82}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["Forward, Comrade! (1939-1945)"],
["forward0.xml", "Khalkhin Gol", "Khalkhin Gol<br><br>2 July 1939<br><br>Comrade Komkor, the Japanese have crossed the Khalkhin Gol. Tonight a force of the Kwantung Army is getting over the river near Bain-Tsagan, while its tanks press on our bridgehead on the eastern bank. They mean to cut the bridgehead off and take the crossings from behind.<br><br>Throw them back over the river. Three positions on this bank matter, and all three must be ours before the Japanese can dig in on them.<br><br>Your force is small but complete: rifles, the cavalry of our Mongolian comrades, armoured cars, tanks, guns and fighters. Choose carefully what you add to it now. You will be keeping it for a long time.<br><br>Do not underestimate the enemy. His infantry is well trained and does not surrender, and for the moment his pilots have the better of ours. What he lacks is weight: his tanks are light and few. Our own road is longer still - the nearest railhead is at Borzya, six hundred kilometres behind us - so what you have on the field is what you have.", [{"id": 1, "country": 5}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward1.xml", "Suomussalmi", "Suomussalmi<br><br>7 December 1939<br><br>Comrade Komkor, we have been at war with Finland for a week. Your corps is crossing the border in the northern forests with one task: take Suomussalmi and the villages around it, and open the road west to Oulu. If we reach the Gulf of Bothnia, Finland is cut in two at the waist.<br><br>Suomussalmi, Juntusranta and Piispaj\u00e4rvi must all be taken, and the road back to Raate must stay open behind you. It is the only road there is.<br><br>You will have little beyond your own troops. The rest of the army is on the Karelian Isthmus.<br><br>The reports say the Finns have few men here, almost all of them infantry. I believe the numbers. I do not believe it will be easy. The Finns are on skis, they know every trail, and the frost is already down to thirty degrees. Do not let your columns string out along the road.", [{"id": 1, "country": 38}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward2.xml", "The Minsk Pocket", "The Minsk Pocket<br><br>26 June 1941<br><br>Comrade General, four days ago Germany attacked us along the whole frontier, and the Western Front is in a desperate position. Hoth's 3rd Panzer Group has passed Minsk to the north, Guderian's 2nd Panzer Group to the south, and they are reaching for each other behind the city. When they meet, everything west of that line is surrounded.<br><br>Hold Minsk, its airfield and the Berezina crossing at Borisov for as long as you can. If Minsk cannot be held, you have permission to take your troops out of it. Borisov must be held in any case, or nothing will get out at all.<br><br>You will have what the Western Front can give you: rifle divisions and a great deal of artillery, but very few tanks. The mechanized corps burned themselves out in the first three days.<br><br>In front of you is the bulk of Army Group Centre: tanks, motorized infantry, artillery, and bombers that own the sky. Watch for their 88 mm anti-aircraft guns, which they are firing at our tanks over open sights. Their men have two years of war behind them. Ours have four days.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward3.xml", "Defence of Kishinev", "Defence of Kishinev<br><br>2 July 1941<br><br>The Romanians and the German 11th Army have crossed the Prut into Bessarabia. Their objective is Kishinev and the Dniester crossings behind it. Stop them. Hold Kishinev and the two positions that cover it.<br><br>You will fight with your own troops. The Southern Front has nothing to give you: every division it has is already in the line.<br><br>From the north comes the German 11th Army: experienced, well supplied, and the real danger. From the south-west the Romanian 3rd and 4th Armies are attacking. The Romanians are brave enough, but poorly equipped and new to this war. Your greener units will do better against them than against the Germans.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward4.xml", "Battle of Odessa", "Battle of Odessa<br><br>28 August 1941<br><br>Odessa has been under siege for weeks, and in the last few days the Romanian 4th Army has pushed our lines back towards the city. Counterattack and throw them back: retake Razdelnaya, Vigoda and Yasski, and give the port room to breathe.<br><br>Your own troops will carry most of the weight, with what the Separate Coastal Army can spare.<br><br>The Romanian 4th Army is large but inexperienced, with plenty of cavalry and infantry and few tanks. Our intelligence expects German units to arrive within days to stiffen it.", [{"id": 1, "country": 13}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward5.xml", "The Kiev Pocket", "The Kiev Pocket<br><br>12 September 1941<br><br>Comrade General, the situation is very grave. Guderian's panzer group is driving south behind Kiev, and Kleist's is driving north out of the Kremenchug bridgehead. If they meet, the whole South-Western Front will be inside the ring. The Stavka's order is to hold Kiev.<br><br>Hold the city and its approaches for as long as you can. Every day you hold is a day those German divisions are not on their way to Moscow.<br><br>Part of the 37th Army is under your command. The troops are raw and have few tanks, but there is some heavy artillery.<br><br>West of the city the German 6th Army is attacking with infantry and artillery. Expect their motorized spearheads to appear behind you from the north and the east: Panzer IIs and IIIs with lorried infantry, fast and dangerous.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward6.xml", "The Bryansk Pocket", "The Bryansk Pocket<br><br>30 September 1941<br><br>Guderian has struck again. This morning his XXIV Motorized Corps broke through the Bryansk Front south of the city and is driving north-east. Orel is the obvious objective, and after Orel, our rear.<br><br>Give ground slowly and keep your army in one piece, but do not give up Bryansk, Orel, Dmitriev-Lgovsky or the Desna crossings before you must.<br><br>The 50th Army has been placed under you: some fifty units, most of them untried. Used well, they are enough to slow the Germans down.<br><br>The enemy has plenty of tanks, infantry and bombers. Expect heavy blows from the west and the south; his strongest group is in the south-west.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward7.xml", "Counterblow at Tula", "Counterblow at Tula<br><br>18 November 1941<br><br>The German drive on Moscow is faltering in the south. Guderian's 2nd Panzer Army has been beating at Tula for weeks, and it will attack your line south of the city again at any hour. Hold Tula, and as soon as the attack is spent, strike back and take their start line in the south.<br><br>You command the 49th and 50th Armies. The men are still green, but the divisions have just been brought up to strength, and a reconnaissance battalion has joined your command.<br><br>Parts of the 2nd Panzer Army are well below strength, and its first line is short of tanks and anti-tank guns. But Guderian still has panzer divisions in reserve, and he will commit them.<br><br>A great deal rides on this counterblow. If it goes deep, the Front has something far larger ready to follow it. If Tula only holds while the Germans slip past it, Moscow itself will need you.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward8.xml", "Closing the Ring", "Closing the Ring<br><br>17 February 1942<br><br>After Tula, the Kalinin Front broke through north of Moscow as well, and the two blows have met near Smolensk. Army Group Centre is surrounded. So far it has not tried to break out; I believe Hitler has forbidden it.<br><br>One gap is left. Your army will deploy north-east and south-east of the city and take the last two positions the Germans hold in the neck of the pocket. And whatever happens, hold both links to our troops in the east, or the ring will close around you instead.<br><br>We can give you little more than your own troops. Every other army is holding the ring.<br><br>The Germans in the neck of the pocket are weak, but they have mined and wired every approach, and they are not standing still. Divisions have been pulled out of Army Groups North and South to break in from outside, and the troops in the pocket will try to meet them halfway. Be quick.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward9.xml", "Street Fighting in Moscow", "Street Fighting in Moscow<br><br>5 December 1941<br><br>This is the last line. The Germans have reached the western outskirts of Moscow. Hold the city - every district of it - and when their attack is spent, throw them out of the suburbs.<br><br>You have a tank division, the Moscow garrison, and the bunkers and pillboxes built this autumn. We began mining the approaches, but there was no time to finish.<br><br>Expect several panzer and infantry divisions, and heavy attacks from the air. The Luftwaffe will be over the city every day the weather allows.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward10.xml", "The Demyansk Pocket", "The Demyansk Pocket<br><br>20 March 1942<br><br>Comrade General, since the winter offensive we have held the German II Army Corps and part of the X in a pocket around Demyansk. They are being supplied by air, and now a relief group under General von Seydlitz is on its way to break in from the west.<br><br>Stop Seydlitz and keep the pocket shut. Hold the crossings on the Lovat, the Pola and the Rob'ya, and take the crossings on the Polomet' and the Yavon' from the troops inside.<br><br>You will have little besides your own army, and little room to deploy it. The ground around the ring is forest and swamp, and the thaw is coming.<br><br>The divisions in the pocket have been worn down by the winter. Seydlitz's group is about as strong, and much more dangerous; it will reach our western flank in about two days. Do not let it join up with the pocket. Several bomber groups have also been seen over the area.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward11.xml", "Defence of Voronezh", "Defence of Voronezh<br><br>28 June 1942<br><br>The Germans spent the spring gathering their strength, and this morning they struck. Together with the Hungarians they have opened a great offensive, and its first objective is Voronezh. Slow them down so that we have time to prepare new positions behind you. Hold Zemlyansk, Nizhnedevitsk and the crossings on the Voronezh river.<br><br>You command the 40th and 13th Armies. With them are a few of the new self-propelled guns, straight from the factory. They could be useful to you.<br><br>You face the 4th Panzer Army and the 2nd Army, with the Hungarian 2nd Army supporting them in the south. The Hungarians are less experienced than the Germans. The Germans have new long-barrelled assault guns that outrange our tanks; watch out for them. And a report has just come in: more German troops, with good tanks and tank destroyers, are on their way. They will reach the southern part of the battlefield within a few days.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward12.xml", "The Rzhev Meat Grinder", "The Rzhev Meat Grinder<br><br>30 July 1942<br><br>After the winter offensive the Germans still hold the salient at Rzhev, and it still points at Moscow. The Stavka has ordered it destroyed. Your army will attack at Rzhev in the north, at Sychevka in the south and through Zamyatino in the middle, break the line, and destroy or capture as much of the German force as it can.<br><br>You command the 30th Army. The Germans hold the only airfield in the area, but the army's engineers have plenty of experience building airfields in the field.<br><br>You face the German 9th Army, and the troops in the salient are still very strong. Their front is continuous and will be hard to break, but there is little behind it. The whole area is sown with mines and fortifications. Rzhev itself is heavily defended, and you will need long-range artillery to break in. Their reserves are at Sychevka, so expect hard fighting there as well.<br><br>Replacements will reach you every day of the battle. Use them: they cannot be saved for later.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward13.xml", "Operation Uranus", "Operation Uranus<br><br>19 November 1942<br><br>Today Operation Uranus begins: our great offensive to encircle the German 6th Army at Stalingrad. Your troops will strike the Axis lines from the north-west and from the south. Take Logovsky, Verkhne-Tsaritsynsky, Ivanovka and Vasilyevka.<br><br>The 65th Army is under your command. It will attack the Romanian front in the north and support your blow against the Italian and Hungarian troops in the south-east.<br><br>In the south-west, Hoth's 4th Panzer Army is your opponent. In the north the Romanian 3rd Army holds the line, and in the south-east there are Italian and Hungarian units. The Romanians, Italians and Hungarians are numerous but understrength, poorly equipped and short of ammunition. They should not stop you for long.<br><br>The 4th Panzer Army is another matter. It still has panzer divisions, and among them is a company of the new heavy Tiger tanks.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward14.xml", "Battle on the Myshkova", "Battle on the Myshkova<br><br>12 December 1942<br><br>The Germans are trying to break into the Stalingrad pocket from the south-west. Hoth's relief group has reached the Myshkova river, and we have stopped it there. Now go over to the attack: overrun the enemy and drive him back to where he started, while Nizhne-Kumsky and Vasilyevka stay in our hands.<br><br>You will do it with your own tank army.<br><br>Army Group Hoth is on the far side of the Myshkova. We expect more troops to reach it over the next few days, but most of them will be Germany's allies rather than Germans.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward15.xml", "Kharkov: The Backhand Blow", "Kharkov: The Backhand Blow<br><br>15 February 1943<br><br>Comrade General, victory seems to be within reach - or perhaps it only seems so. The Germans are leaving the Kharkov area and falling back to the south-west. Your army is to push into the empty ground behind them and take Lyubotin and the roads beyond it, while Kharkov and Olshany stay firmly in our hands.<br><br>Many of our generals believe the Germans are beaten and the war will soon be over. I am not so sure. Be careful.<br><br>You will do this with your own tank army. Our reconnaissance reports almost no enemy in the area. I would not bet my life on our reconnaissance.<br><br>The Stavka will judge this operation by how many of the five objectives your army holds when it ends: all five for a brilliant victory, four for a victory, three for a tactical victory. Any of these three results carries your army on along the sector you choose; fewer than three is a defeat.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward16.xml", "Prokhorovka", "Prokhorovka<br><br>12 July 1943<br><br>The Germans are attacking our lines at Prokhorovka. Stop every attack, then counterattack towards Belgorod and take it.<br><br>We knew this offensive was coming and had months to prepare for it. Your tank army is not a veteran one, but every unit has been brought up over strength, and the ground in front of your start positions has been mined.<br><br>You face the II SS Panzer Corps. Expect heavy tank attacks, with the Luftwaffe close behind them; you will need strong air defence and fighters. Tigers, the first Panthers and new heavy tank destroyers have all been identified in front of you.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward18.xml", "Leningrad", "Leningrad<br><br>14 January 1944<br><br>For more than two years the Germans have held Leningrad under siege, and the city has starved. It is time to end it. In the south and the centre the Germans are already falling back. Hit their 18th Army hard enough and they will have to go here too.<br><br>You will have your own tank army, with two divisions of bridging engineers attached. The Germans have blown every bridge.<br><br>The 18th Army still has some good units, but the best German divisions are fighting in the south and the centre. Expect few tanks and a great deal of infantry.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward19.xml", "Vyborg", "Vyborg<br><br>10 June 1944<br><br>The Western Allies landed in France four days ago, and the Germans are pulling troops west. Our next blow falls in Karelia. Advance across the Isthmus and take Viipuri - Vyborg, as it will be called again. Terijoki, Rautu, Taipale and Heinjoki lie on the way.<br><br>You will have only your own tank army.<br><br>You face the Finnish army, which will defend every line on the Isthmus, and you should expect the Germans to send it some help. Even so, the enemy should not be able to stop you.", [{"id": 1, "country": 38}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward20.xml", "Riga", "Riga<br><br>14 September 1944<br><br>After Karelia, the Baltic. Your tank army is to attack the Germans at Riga and drive them out of the city.<br><br>You will have only your own tank army.<br><br>The German 16th and 18th Armies are defending. There are strong panzer divisions outside the city, and in Riga itself fanatical infantry, with plenty of artillery behind it.<br><br>After Riga your army goes straight on into Courland, and from there far to the east. There will be no quiet refit between those battles, so do not burn out your units here.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward21.xml", "The Courland Pocket", "The Courland Pocket<br><br>12 February 1945<br><br>We have tried several times to destroy the Germans trapped in Courland, and every attempt has failed. I think your men are the right ones for the job. Attack on the front between Liepaja and Saldus, break through and take Pavilosta on the coast. Liepaja and its airfield, Skrunda and Saldus must fall too.<br><br>You will have only your own tank army.<br><br>You face the 16th and 18th Armies. They are worn down but very experienced, and they still have two strong panzer units. The approaches are blocked with obstacles, bunkers and minefields.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward22.xml", "The Manchurian Operation", "The Manchurian Operation<br><br>9 August 1945<br><br>The war in Europe is over. Now we keep our promise to the Allies and open a second front against Japan. Your army is to break through the Japanese and Manchukuo lines east of Changchun, then take Changchun, Jilin and Siping.<br><br>You will have only your own tank army. We hold no airfield in this area, so bring engineers who can build one.<br><br>You face two Japanese armies and Manchukuo troops. They are poorly equipped, but they have dug themselves into the mountains east of Changchun, and breaking through will take time.", [{"id": 1, "country": 5}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward23.xml", "The Smolensk Offensive", "The Smolensk Offensive<br><br>7 August 1943<br><br>Now our great offensive begins. You will attack Army Group Centre at Yelnya. The Germans have had time to prepare, but I am sure you can break through. Take Yelnya, Glinka and the villages along the German line.<br><br>You will have only your own tank army.<br><br>Army Group Centre is still strong, though short of tanks. Expect heavy long-range artillery fire, and the Luftwaffe has a strong bomber force here. The ground behind the river crossings is well fortified, but once you are through, resistance will be lighter.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward24.xml", "Operation Bagration", "Operation Bagration<br><br>22 June 1944<br><br>The time has come for our greatest offensive. Several fronts are joining the attack in Belorussia. Your task is Vitebsk: take the city and push on to the west, to Gorodok, Polotsk and Lepel.<br><br>You will have only your own tank army.<br><br>Vitebsk is protected by strong fortifications and held by the LIII Army Corps; further south, the VI Army Corps holds the line. The Germans have good tanks and tank destroyers here, among them Tiger IIs and a unit of Ferdinands. It might be wise to put your best troops in the south, break through there, and let the rest close in on Vitebsk.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward25.xml", "Krak\u00f3w", "Krak\u00f3w<br><br>17 January 1945<br><br>Our armies are crossing Poland. Your task is Krak\u00f3w, to the west of you: take the city, its two airfields and the towns around it.<br><br>You will have only your own tank army.<br><br>Krak\u00f3w is held by the German 17th Army, with what is left of the 4th Panzer Army. They are far under strength, but they still have some formidable Panthers and Tiger IIs. The hardest fighting will be in the city itself.<br><br>After Krak\u00f3w you go straight on to the Oder, and then to Berlin, with no time to refit between the battles. Bring your units out of this one in good order.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward26.xml", "Fortress K\u00fcstrin", "Fortress K\u00fcstrin<br><br>26 March 1945<br><br>Your troops have reached the Oder at K\u00fcstrin. Take the fortress and the villages around it, secure the river line, and build a bridgehead on the far bank.<br><br>You will have only your own tank army.<br><br>K\u00fcstrin is held by its garrison, and beyond the Oder strong German forces will try to stop your bridgehead. Taken together, they should not be a problem for your troops.<br><br>Speed matters more than usual here. Our allies in the west are also racing for Berlin, and the agreements about who takes the city are only as strong as our position on the Oder.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward27.xml", "Battle of Berlin", "Battle of Berlin<br><br>16 April 1945<br><br>Comrade General, this is the last battle. Your troops are in position on the Oder, and there is a great deal to do:<br>- cross the Oder at the Seelow Heights and destroy the 9th Army;<br>- take Frankfurt, Cottbus, Schwedt and Oranienburg;<br>- surround what is left of the 9th Army near Halbe, and let none of it break out to the west;<br>- take Berlin and Potsdam;<br>- stop Wenck's 12th Army coming from the Elbe, and take Wittenberg.<br><br>The 2nd Belorussian Front will support you in the north, where it will take Schwedt and deal with the 3rd Panzer Army, and the 1st Ukrainian Front will support you in the south. This is the last battle, so spend everything you have: replacements are waiting for you.<br><br>The 9th Army, the 12th Army and the 4th Panzer Army are veteran but worn out. They still have Tiger IIs and Panthers, and our intelligence even speaks of super-heavy prototypes. Around Berlin you will also meet the Volkssturm and the Hitler Youth. The city itself is defended by the remnants of the 9th Army, police units, the Volkssturm and SS Battle Group Mohnke.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward28.xml", "Breakthrough at Dessau", "Breakthrough at Dessau<br><br>19 May 1945<br><br>After careful planning, the General Staff has decided to strike the Allied lines at Dessau. The Allies have concentrated a great many troops on this sector; if we break through here, they will have to pull back everywhere else. Take Dessau, Halle and Merseburg, and push on to Stassfurt and Quedlinburg.<br><br>Besides your tank army, a second army will support the attack from positions west of yours.<br><br>The enemy has several armoured divisions. German units that went over to the Allies in the spring are fighting in their ranks. Expect strong opposition in the air: the USAAF and the RAF have several air forces around Dessau, and heavy bombers will support their ground troops.", [{"id": 1, "country": 22}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward29.xml", "Battle of East Frisia", "Battle of East Frisia<br><br>23 June 1945<br><br>We have trapped several Allied armies in East Frisia. We know they plan to evacuate them by sea through Emden and Wilhelmshaven. Take both ports before the ships arrive, and destroy as much of the trapped force as you can, so that it never comes back at us.<br><br>Besides your tank army, a smaller army will support you; its troops will be useful for the attack on Emden.<br><br>The trapped enemy still has dangerous armoured divisions and plenty of infantry. German units that went over to the Allies in the spring are fighting in their ranks. Their air force will give you trouble, all the more because you have no airfield at the start and the nearest one is too far away. Make sure you have engineers who can build one.", [{"id": 1, "country": 22}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward30.xml", "Battle of the Ruhr", "Battle of the Ruhr<br><br>26 July 1945<br><br>The factories of the Ruhr are working for the Western Allies now. Take the Ruhr from them and their armies on the continent will be much harder to supply. Take the Ruhr cities and D\u00fcsseldorf, and build a bridgehead over the Rhine.<br><br>Besides your tank army, several divisions will support you. At your request we have given you more anti-aircraft units.<br><br>The enemy is not numerous. East of the Ruhr the Allies have built a line protected by obstacles, minefields and barbed wire; further south the resistance seems lighter.", [{"id": 1, "country": 22}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward31.xml", "The Ardennes", "The Ardennes<br><br>20 August 1945<br><br>Where the Germans failed, we intend to succeed. In the Ardennes the Allies have built their last defensive line. If we break through, the road to Antwerp is open, and the Allies can no longer use its port to bring in reinforcements.<br><br>Another army will support your attack, and a unit of IS heavy tanks has been attached to you.<br><br>The Allies are still numerous. Beware of ambushes in the woods, and remember that the IS tanks carry very little ammunition and are vulnerable in this terrain.", [{"id": 1, "country": 22}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward32.xml", "Assault on Antwerp", "Assault on Antwerp<br><br>10 October 1945<br><br>Victory is close. Your troops are on the approaches to Antwerp. Destroy the last Allied troops and take the port, so that no more Allied reinforcements can land.<br><br>Several ships cover the harbour, so part of our fleet has been placed under your command, and bombers will support you. The Allies hold the only airfield in the area; it would be wise to build one of your own at the start of the battle.<br><br>The Allies have abandoned the ground south of the city and covered it with mines and obstacles. Beyond that line their front is thin. Further back they still have heavy tanks - Shermans of the latest type - and green armoured divisions are unloading in the harbour right now.", [{"id": 1, "country": 22}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward33.xml", "Breakthrough at Dessau", "Breakthrough at Dessau<br><br>19 May 1945<br><br>After careful planning, the General Staff has decided to strike the Allied lines at Dessau. The Allies have concentrated a great many troops on this sector; if we break through here, they will have to pull back everywhere else. Take Dessau, Halle and Merseburg, and push on to Stassfurt and Quedlinburg.<br><br>Besides your tank army, a second army will support the attack from positions west of yours. German units that surrendered to us in the spring are fighting under your command, and more can be called up if you need them.<br><br>The enemy has several armoured divisions. Expect strong opposition in the air: the USAAF and the RAF have several air forces around Dessau, and heavy bombers will support their ground troops.", [{"id": 1, "country": 22}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward34.xml", "Battle of East Frisia", "Battle of East Frisia<br><br>23 June 1945<br><br>We have trapped several Allied armies in East Frisia. We know they plan to evacuate them by sea through Emden and Wilhelmshaven. Take both ports before the ships arrive, and destroy as much of the trapped force as you can, so that it never comes back at us.<br><br>Besides your tank army, a smaller army will support you; its troops will be useful for the attack on Emden. German units that surrendered to us in the spring are fighting under your command, and more can be called up if you need them.<br><br>The trapped enemy still has dangerous armoured divisions and plenty of infantry. Their air force will give you trouble, all the more because you have no airfield at the start and the nearest one is too far away. Make sure you have engineers who can build one.", [{"id": 1, "country": 22}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward35.xml", "Battle of the Ruhr", "Battle of the Ruhr<br><br>26 July 1945<br><br>The factories of the Ruhr are working for the Western Allies now. Take the Ruhr from them and their armies on the continent will be much harder to supply. Take the Ruhr cities and D\u00fcsseldorf, and build a bridgehead over the Rhine.<br><br>Besides your tank army, several divisions will support you. At your request we have given you more anti-aircraft units. German units that surrendered to us in the spring are fighting under your command, and more can be called up if you need them.<br><br>The enemy is not numerous. East of the Ruhr the Allies have built a line protected by obstacles, minefields and barbed wire; further south the resistance seems lighter.", [{"id": 1, "country": 22}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward36.xml", "The Ardennes", "The Ardennes<br><br>20 August 1945<br><br>Where the Germans failed, we intend to succeed. In the Ardennes the Allies have built their last defensive line. If we break through, the road to Antwerp is open, and the Allies can no longer use its port to bring in reinforcements.<br><br>Another army will support your attack, and a unit of IS heavy tanks has been attached to you.<br><br>The Allies are still numerous. Beware of ambushes in the woods, and remember that the IS tanks carry very little ammunition and are vulnerable in this terrain.", [{"id": 1, "country": 22}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward37.xml", "Assault on Antwerp", "Assault on Antwerp<br><br>10 October 1945<br><br>Victory is close. Your troops are on the approaches to Antwerp. Destroy the last Allied troops and take the port, so that no more Allied reinforcements can land.<br><br>Several ships cover the harbour, so part of our fleet has been placed under your command, and bombers will support you. The Allies hold the only airfield in the area; it would be wise to build one of your own at the start of the battle.<br><br>The Allies have abandoned the ground south of the city and covered it with mines and obstacles. Beyond that line their front is thin. Further back they still have heavy tanks - Shermans of the latest type - and green armoured divisions are unloading in the harbour right now.", [{"id": 1, "country": 22}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward38.xml", "The Kuban Bridgehead", "The Kuban Bridgehead<br><br>3 September 1943<br><br>For months the Germans have held their bridgehead on the Black Sea coast. We have pushed them back, but every attempt to destroy them has failed. Now we know they intend to evacuate it before they are cut off, and we will attack before they can get away. Break the line, take Novorossiysk, Krymsk, Anapa and Taman, and destroy the German forces.<br><br>You will have only your own tank army. The Germans hold both airfields in the area, but an engineer unit has been attached to you, and it should be able to build a small airfield within a few days.<br><br>You face the German 17th Army, with Romanian and Slovak troops. The Romanians and Slovaks are weak. The Germans have few tanks and only one fighter group. There may be no great counterattack, but you must be quick.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward39.xml", "Counterattack at Zhitomir", "Counterattack at Zhitomir<br><br>13 November 1943<br><br>I am sorry to cut your rest short. While your troops were refitting, the situation near Zhitomir has turned serious. After we retook Kiev, the Germans counterattacked with several panzer divisions. Hold Zhitomir and Korostyshev, and stop any advance on Kiev.<br><br>Because of the refit, not all of your units could set out together. At first you will have only a few troops near Zhitomir; the rest will come up over the next days. The 94th Rifle Division is defending Zhitomir, and it is under your command.<br><br>The Germans are not numerous, but some of their tanks are formidable, and they are very close to Zhitomir. A sudden blow could be devastating. Be careful.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward40.xml", "The Brody Cauldron", "The Brody Cauldron<br><br>20 July 1944<br><br>With your advance, the ring around the German divisions at Brody is closed. They will try to break out. Stop them from getting across the river to the west, destroy as much of the encircled force as you can, and keep Lutsk in our hands.<br><br>Troops of the 1st Ukrainian Front will support you.<br><br>You face the XIII Army Corps. It is under strength and has only a few serious tanks. With a solid front, the breakout should not be hard to stop.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward41.xml", "Jassy-Kishinev", "Jassy-Kishinev<br><br>20 August 1944<br><br>Romania must be knocked out of the war. Without the Romanian oilfields, the Germans cannot keep up serious resistance for long. Break through the Axis line at Jassy and push on to Piatra Neam\u021b.<br><br>You will have only your own tank army.<br><br>You face Army Group South Ukraine: Army Group W\u00f6hler and Army Group Dumitrescu, each a mixture of German and Romanian armies. The Germans have some heavy tanks and will counterattack hard if your first blow is weak. The Romanians have lost heavily in this war, and their units are well below strength.", [{"id": 1, "country": 13}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward42.xml", "Sz\u00e9kesfeh\u00e9rv\u00e1r", "Sz\u00e9kesfeh\u00e9rv\u00e1r<br><br>16 March 1945<br><br>While the Germans try to break through our lines at Lake Balaton, your task is to break through the German and Hungarian line at Sz\u00e9kesfeh\u00e9rv\u00e1r. Take the city, its airfield and N\u00e1daslad\u00e1ny. With the city in our hands, the road to Vienna is open.<br><br>You will have only your own tank army.<br><br>You face Army Group Balck. Its troops are exhausted, but they still have some strong tanks and fighters.<br><br>After this battle your army goes straight on into Czechoslovakia, and from there far to the east. There will be no quiet refit in between, so bring your units out of this one in good order.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward43.xml", "The Road to Prague", "The Road to Prague<br><br>6 May 1945<br><br>Berlin has fallen. Now we must destroy the German armies still fighting in Czechoslovakia and free Prague. Your road north begins on the Hron: break the German line at Nagysall\u00f3, take L\u00e9va and L\u00f6k, and advance north.<br><br>The 2nd Ukrainian Front will support your attack, and Romanian, Czechoslovak and Polish troops are under your command. There is no airfield in the area, so you will have to build one before your aircraft can fly.<br><br>You face the German 8th Army. It has lost much of its strength, but in the last few days it has received some experimental heavy tanks, straight from the proving grounds. The Germans also have new fighters here, but no airfield nearby, so they can support their troops for only a few days.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["Sim Pobedishi! - The Red East (1918-1920)"],
["simpob_00.xml", "By this sign: the Komuch offensive", "By this sign: the Komuch offensive<br><br>June 8th, 1918<br><br>Samara fell this morning. Czechoslovak battalions took the Volga bridge before the demolition party reached it, and a Committee of Constituent Assembly deputies has declared itself the government of Russia.<br><br>It has a committee and a press; its armed strength comes from the forces holding the railway. And the railway is the front. Hold Simbirsk, Melekess, Stavropol and Syzran, and take Samara back if it can be done.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_01.xml", "The gold in the vaults: Kazan", "The gold in the vaults: Kazan<br><br>August 4th, 1918<br><br>Six hundred million roubles of the Imperial reserve lie in the vaults under this city. That, and not the map, is why Kappel's column is coming here.<br><br>Whoever walks out with them pays for a year of war, so Kazan cannot be traded for space. Kappel has three thousand men and two gunboats; the 5th Army is three days old. Hold the Kremlin, the academy and the river crossings.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_02.xml", "The Committee comes apart: Samara and Syzran", "The Committee comes apart: Samara and Syzran<br><br>September 18th, 1918<br><br>Kazan was retaken on the tenth and Simbirsk on the twelfth. The mobilised peasants will not fight for the Committee, and the Czechoslovaks have decided they are going home.<br><br>Samara and Syzran are the last of it. The Committee's staff and treasury are loading at Krotovka for Ufa, and every column that gets out can be organised against us again. Take both towns and hold Simbirsk behind them.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_03.xml", "Thirty below: the winter blow at Ufa", "Thirty below: the winter blow at Ufa<br><br>January 6th, 1919<br><br>There is a Supreme Ruler now, by his own proclamation: Kolchak took Omsk in November by arresting the Committee's ministers, and the Entente recognised it by going on unloading rifles for him.<br><br>Behind his front the atamans are already hanging people along the railway, and the villages are turning against them. That will not stop the troops already coming west. His first stroke is at Ufa, where the 5th Army holds a hundred and fifty versts with nine thousand men at thirty below. Hold Ufa and the approaches.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_04.xml", "Khanzhin's breakthrough: the spring offensive", "Khanzhin's breakthrough: the spring offensive<br><br>March 1st, 1919<br><br>Khanzhin's Western Army came out of the thaw at the junction of the 5th and 1st Armies with three to one on the axis of attack. Behind it Gaida is driving on Vyatka.<br><br>If Gaida joins hands with the interventionists at Archangel, the northern half of the Republic is cut off from Moscow. Hold Belebei, Tuymazy, Abdulino, Sterlitamak and Meleuz; Ufa behind their front is their railhead.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_05.xml", "The drive for the Volga: the spring offensive", "The drive for the Volga: the spring offensive<br><br>March 14th, 1919<br><br>They have not stopped, and there is nothing behind this sector to stop them with. Khanzhin is driving for the Volga on a front too wide for his own supply.<br><br>He has been told the river must be reached before the Southern Front opens, and an army in that much of a hurry pays for every verst. Hold the line of towns from Belebei to Sterlitamak while the enemy stretches his supply farther from the railway. We need time to gather a force that can answer him.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_06.xml", "The ring at Orenburg", "The ring at Orenburg<br><br>April 17th, 1919<br><br>Dutov's Cossacks have besieged Orenburg on and off for a year. Without it their Host has no capital and no junction.<br><br>We hold it because it is the only rail link to Turkestan - cut it and Central Asia is on its own for the rest of the war. The garrison is the town: railwaymen, the Kirghiz and Tatar detachments, a workers' regiment. There will be no relief; the relieving force has gone to Buzuluk, because Frunze is about to attack. Hold the ring.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_07.xml", "Frunze attacks: Belebei", "Frunze attacks: Belebei<br><br>May 15th, 1919<br><br>Frunze's southern group has broken the Western Army at Buguruslan and Bugulma. The initiative on this front has changed hands for the first time since January.<br><br>Khanzhin is trying to reform on the Belebei position with the old People's Army under a new name. Everything depends on hitting that position before it becomes one: Chapayev's 25th Division goes in first, and must break through before the retreating troops can dig in.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_08.xml", "The tide turns: Chistopol", "The tide turns: Chistopol<br><br>May 26th, 1919<br><br>North of this sector Gaida's Siberian Army is still pushing on Vyatka and has not understood that the army on its left has collapsed.<br><br>Take Bugulma and the Azanakayevo junction now and that whole northern group is fighting with a hole where its flank used to be. Fail, and their reserves come south and it is their offensive again - aimed at the Volga crossings, and fought for in front of Kazan.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_10.xml", "Twice in one year: Kazan", "Twice in one year: Kazan (alternate history)<br><br>June 10th, 1919<br><br>The May attack was held, and the counterstroke has carried them back onto the Volga. Kazan is the front line again.<br><br>The front is being rebuilt around this city while it is held: every division that comes up the line arrives because Kazan was still ours when it started loading. Hold the Kremlin, the academy and the crossings until the reinforcing formations are in place.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_11.xml", "Where it all began: Samara", "Where it all began: Samara<br><br>July 14th, 1919<br><br>A year and a month since the Czechoslovaks took this bridge, and it is being argued over again. Their advance down the Volga has been slowed, not stopped.<br><br>Front headquarters is shuttling staffs between three threatened directions by rail, which is what happens when a front has more axes than reserves. This group will not be reinforced. Hold Samara, Simbirsk and Syzran; Melekess and Krotovka are their staging points.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_12.xml", "Cutting the Republic in two: Vyatka", "Cutting the Republic in two: Vyatka<br><br>October 20th, 1919<br><br>Gaida was dismissed in the summer, but a change of commander has not ended the Siberian Army's northern drive.<br><br>It still wants Vyatka and a junction with the interventionists from Archangel. If they meet, the Republic is cut in half along the Northern Dvina. Hold the Vyatka sectors and Karavayevy; Vakhrushi is their forward railhead.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_13.xml", "The Black Baron: Saratov", "The Black Baron: Saratov<br><br>November 13th, 1919<br><br>Wrangel's Caucasus Army has come up the Volga from Tsaritsyn to shake hands with Kolchak's people.<br><br>A junction of the two White fronts on the middle Volga is the one thing both commands have wanted all year and never arranged, largely because neither will serve under the other. They are not to arrange it here. Hold the Saratov sectors and Atkarsk; Volsk is where the link is being tried.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}, {"id": 2, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_14.xml", "The junction before Moscow: Ryazan", "The junction before Moscow: Ryazan<br><br>December 12th, 1919<br><br>Ryazan is not a front-line town. It is where the roads from the south and the east meet before Moscow, which is why a group made of other people's spare regiments is standing in it in December.<br><br>If this line goes there is one more behind it, and then there is Moscow. Hold Ryazan, Kolomna and Kashira. Their forward group has come up at Venev on the Tula road, and it is worth more to us than to them yet.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_15.xml", "Sixty versts from Moscow: Klin", "Sixty versts from Moscow: Klin<br><br>December 30th, 1919<br><br>Klin is on the Petrograd railway sixty versts from Moscow. There is nothing behind this one.<br><br>Everything the Republic could scrape together in a fortnight is here: the courses cadets, two workers' regiments from the Moscow factories, the internationalist battalion, and regiments retreating since Saratov that are being asked to stop today. Hold Klin and the four villages until the next defensive line can be organised.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_16.xml", "The May counterattack: Zhitomir", "The May counterattack: Zhitomir<br><br>May 19th, 1920<br><br>The Polish armies took Kiev on the seventh. The 12th and 14th Armies were pushed back over the Dnieper and are being put together again behind it.<br><br>Warsaw's object here is a client state under Petliura, bought last month with eastern Galicia and western Volhynia. Attack now: the Western Front opened in Belorussia on the fourteenth, and every Polish division kept here this fortnight is one that does not entrain north. Take Korosten, Zwiahel, Zhitomir and Kazatin; hold Malin and Fastov.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_17.xml", "Across the Belaya: Ufa", "Across the Belaya: Ufa<br><br>May 29th, 1919<br><br>The Western Army is broken, and the town it has supplied itself from all spring is on the far bank of a wide river with one bridge.<br><br>Chapayev's 25th Division crosses on rafts north of the city; the rest of the group goes for the Chishmy junction to cut the line out from under the garrison. There is no reserve for another attempt. Take Ufa before the rearguard has bought enough time for the main body to get away.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_18.xml", "The house on Voznesensky Lane: Ekaterinburg", "The house on Voznesensky Lane: Ekaterinburg<br><br>July 12th, 1919<br><br>The 2nd and 3rd Armies are over the northern Urals. Ekaterinburg is the junction of everything on this front and the last real city before Siberia.<br><br>Their evacuation began before our guns were in range: six columns of staff, treasury and archives on the Tyumen line, and what is in them decides what anyone can prove afterwards about the house on Voznesensky Lane. Take the city and let nothing reach the eastern exit.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_19.xml", "Both shoulders at once: Chelyabinsk", "Both shoulders at once: Chelyabinsk<br><br>July 25th, 1919<br><br>The 5th Army came through the passes into Chelyabinsk yesterday. Keeping it is evidently a different question from taking it.<br><br>Kolchak's staff planned exactly this: let the Reds in, close from Miasskoye and from the north, and destroy an army in a street it thinks it owns. The city rose to help take it - the railway workshops turned out three regiments in a week. Hold the town and its approaches while the neighbouring formations come up.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_20.xml", "They are not finished: the Tobol (I)", "They are not finished: the Tobol (I)<br><br>September 1st, 1919<br><br>Kolchak's armies have been reorganised behind the Tobol. Dieterichs combed out the rear areas, the Siberian Cossacks are mobilised wholesale, and their staff counted correctly: our divisions are at half strength, six hundred versts from railhead.<br><br>The reports that said this enemy was finished were wrong, and this is the bill for them. The blow has fallen on the left, where the Cossack cavalry has open steppe. Hold the line of villages; Petropavlovsk is what all of it is a step towards.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}, {"id": 2, "country": 191}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_22.xml", "An offensive running on nothing: the Tobol (II)", "An offensive running on nothing: the Tobol (II)<br><br>September 25th, 1919<br><br>Their offensive is a month old and running on nothing.<br><br>Every recruit put into the line this month came from a village that is now sending its sons to the partisans instead, and their supply comes down one railway with the Siberian detachments sitting on it. They have gained ground and lost the army that gained it. Hold Kurgan, Chashinskiy, Vargashi and the Tobol crossing.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}, {"id": 2, "country": 191}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_23.xml", "The bridge over the Ob: Novonikolayevsk", "The bridge over the Ob: Novonikolayevsk<br><br>December 7th, 1919<br><br>Omsk fell without a fight three weeks ago. Their government left by train and their army left on foot, and the two have not been in the same place since.<br><br>In front of us is the Great Siberian Ice March: retreating troops, refugees and families, many of them sick with typhus, moving east down one railway in December. Novonikolayevsk is the bridge over the Ob - take it and the column east is cut off from the column west.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_24.xml", "The town took itself: Krasnoyarsk", "The town took itself: Krasnoyarsk<br><br>January 4th, 1920<br><br>Krasnoyarsk has taken itself: the garrison arrested its own commander on the last day of December, and the town is held by a revolutionary committee, the railway workers and Shchetinkin's partisans.<br><br>Our leading divisions are four days behind. Kappel's column is coming down the line - what is left of three armies, on foot, in forty degrees of frost, with nothing to lose. Hold the city and Drokino with what is here. The partisans know this country as we do not; they are allies.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_25.xml", "The last of it: Irkutsk", "The last of it: Irkutsk<br><br>January 27th, 1920<br><br>The Political Centre rose here at the end of December and handed the city, and the Supreme Ruler, to the Revolutionary Committee. Kolchak is in the prison, and so is what is left of the gold.<br><br>Out of the taiga comes what survived the march: Kappel died on the road, and Voitsekhovsky has demanded the city, the prisoner and a contribution. Semyonov is east of the lake, and the Baikal ice is the only way past. Hold Irkutsk and Listvennichnoye.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["Korean War - Battles of 1950-51 (CC76)"],
["w92_kor01.xml", "DEFENSE OF SEOUL", "Good morning commander. I'm going to make a brief introduction of the present situation. The North Korean Peoples Army have crossed the 38th paralel, striking the ROK forces alongside the frontier. So, the situation is hopeless and some people including the president Truman are believing that this is the beginning of the 3rd  World War... The forces of the Republic of Korea with their outdated equipment and few soldiers are not able to stop the Soviet equiped North Korean forces which are now at the gates of the capital of South Korea; Seoul. It's sure that we won't be able to hold Seoul for too long, however we will need some time to make an organised retreat of the ROK forces.<br><br>Your task is; manage the ROK forces to avoid a quick victory of the NKPA forces over Seoul. Fortunately, a US task force will help you from the turn 5. (You will receive enough prestige to build your task force in the 5th turn). <br><br>Good luck commander!", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9}], "eqp-cc76" ],
["w92_kor02.xml", "KUM RIVER LINE", "The withdrawal continues commander, and the situation has not any sight to be changed for now. The North Korean forces have arrived to the North of the important city of Taejon, which is surrounded by the Kum river.<br><br>Your mission this time is again to get enough time to make a good retreat to the South. You should establish a defensive line on the South bank of the Kum river, to gain enough time to save as much units as possible. Taejon must not fall until the established time, otherwise the remain units in other parts will be surrounded and surely defeated.<br><br>Good Luck.<br><br>NOTE: Deployment zone is limited to 8 hexes.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9}], "eqp-cc76" ],
["w92_kor03.xml", "PUSAN PERIMETER", "Please, sit down general... The NKPA forces have conquered the most of the Korean peninsula. Now, the U.N. forces are trying to resist in the Pusan Perimeter. This area is established around the important port of Pusan, the last capital of the Republic of Korea. Pusan must not fall at any costs!, otherwise, the Communists will be victorious and Korea entirely unified under the communist sign of North Korea.<br><br>Your task is to resist the North Korean strike, and then, stage a counterattack to break the enemy lines. Our 8th Army have received some reinforcements like some M26 Pershing tanks and other units which will be a great help to deal with the commies.<br><br>Good luck commander!.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9}], "eqp-cc76" ],
["w92_kor04.xml", "INCH'ON LANDING", "If this operation is not finally sucessful, surely Harry will claim for my head!! hehe. Well, you are the proper commander to land on Inch'on, the traditional port of Seoul. Yes, you are right, the plans are to free Seoul from the North Koreans while they are busy at the Pusan Perimeter. A success in Inch'on, will mean that the NKPA forces will be in a complete disarray.<br><br>Intelligence reports that the enemy forces are consisting of mainly rookie units of two divisions which are currently still in the making.<br><br>Your mission is; land at Inch'on and then drive to Seoul. Liberate the capital from the Communists.<br><br>Good Luck!!!.<br><br>NOTE: Deployment zone is limited to 8 hexes.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9}], "eqp-cc76" ],
["w92_kor05.xml", "ADVANCE TO PYONGYANG", "Good morning, commander. The U.N. forces have completely turned the situation, now we are in front of the North Korean capital. The perimeter of Pyongyang it's defended only by a few enemy divisions, but beware!; the North Koreans still have many U.N. POWs in the nearly areas of Pyongyang, and they can execute them, so a fast action it's mandatory there. <br><br>Take Pyongyang as soon as possible, and free the prisoners taking the North Korean capital city from the commies. Also take care: the North Korean soldiers will act as guerrillas as soon as their units become into disarray.<br><br>Good luck.<br><br>NOTE: Deployment zone is limited to 10 hexes.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9}], "eqp-cc76" ],
["w92_kor06.xml", "BATTLE OF THE CHONGCHON", "Warning!, a huge chinese force have crossed the Yalu river and it's falling over our positions in North Korea. Your troops in the vicitinies of the Chongchon river are in the way of the chinese army and will receive the assault of the main PLA (Peoples Liberation Army) strike, which is probably intended to free Pyongyang. The mountains will be a great help for us, althought the Chinese army is largely bigger than our troops deployed here.<br><br>Good Luck!.<br><br>NOTE: Deployment zone is limited to 18 hexes.", [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9}], "eqp-cc76" ],
["w92_kor07.xml", "CHOSIN RESERVOIR", "Warning!, the Chinese are launching an incoming strike on our forward positons at the  Chosin Reservoir. We should expect again a human wave assault. Althought the enemy it's outnumbering our troops, we think the higher quality of your troops can stop the chinese hordes, under this horrible icy weather...<br><br>Good luck.<br><br>NOTE: Deployment zone is limited to 8 hexes.", [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9}], "eqp-cc76" ],
["w92_kor08.xml", "HUNGNAM EVACUATION", "This is a really bad situation, a good part of our troops are near to be traped in North Korea, and the only choice for an evacuation, it's to reach the port of Hungnam. Your task is to drive your units quickly to the port of Hungnam. Try to stop the chinese forces as much as possible while our units are embarking in the port... other units are retrating in other points of Korea, and a quick retreat will allow the PLA forces to use their troops agaisnt the other places.<br><br>I will ask Harry for nuclear support agaisnt the chineses, while you are doing your job, commander.<br><br>Good luck.<br><br>NOTE: Deployment zone is limited to 14 hexes.", [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9}], "eqp-cc76" ],
["w92_kor09.xml", "OPERATION THUNDERBOLT", "[General Mathew Ridgway speaking]<br><br>Please sit down commander. I'm the new C-I-C of the U.N. forces in Korea. As you know, Seoul it's back on the communist hands. We can't allow a situation such this, so we have planned an operation to liberate Seoul and turn the things into a more favorable scenario for us.<br><br>You should fix the chinese forces at the right or our lines, and make a fast advance to Seoul by the left. Take care, the enemy T-34 are still a menace to our Shermans, althought we have the support of some M26 tanks.<br><br>Your task is clear; liberate Seoul!.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9}], "eqp-cc76" ],
["w92_kor10.xml", "CHINESE SPRING OFFENSIVE", "Warning!, the PLA and the NKPA are launching a full scale operation agaisnt our lines!. Our troops are largely outnumbered by the communists, but we can count on the higher quality of our brave men to save Seoul from the communist menace again.<br><br>You should try to stop the communist onslaught, and then launch a counterattack to restore the lines. Seoul must not fall!!!.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9}], "eqp-cc76" ],
["w92_kor11.xml", "SPRING OFFENSIVE 2ND STAGE", "The communist Spring offensive it's closely to be stopped at the Seoul area. However, the enemy offensive remains powerful Eastwards to Seoul. Take control over the situation and stop the communist assault also here.<br><br>Good luck!.<br><br>NOTE: Deployment zone is limited to 17 hexes.", [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9}], "eqp-cc76" ],
["w92_kor12.xml", "THE FALL OFFENSIVES", "Since the last Spring, the PLA keeps some good forward positions which we are going to clear of communist troops, this is really important because there are near to sign a truce with the enemy, and the peace talks will start soon. It's politicaly important to get as much territories as possible, because the conflict can be renewed in the future. The vicitinies of the Soyang reservoir are garrisoned by an important number of PLA troops. Also the NKPA has some units in the North.<br><br>Your task is to recapture the Soyang reservoir area and clear the coast of enemy elements. The navy is here to help you bombing the coastal positions.<br><br>Good luck, maybe we will be in home at Christmas...<br><br>NOTE: Deployment zone is limited to 17 hexes.", [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9}], "eqp-cc76" ],
]
